oundaries, and clarification questions.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may confuse AI/ML responsibility with embedded-system or telemetry-pipeline ownership.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Case intake, role boundary, stakeholder ownership", "reason_behind_concept": "A clear intake prevents the learner from jumping into analysis, assuming missing context, or taking ownership of software/embedded issues.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use when the case request is incomplete and the learner must clarify what can be checked at L1 versus what must be escalated."}, "student_confusion": "Which parts of the problem am I responsible for as an L1 AI/ML learner?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Case Intake", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer’s request is short and incomplete: “Check if this telemetry sample is usable for anomaly detection.” You have the CSV sample, warning logs, UDP description, and shared-memory field list, but sensor meanings, valid ranges, timestamp rules, and ownership are not fully clear. You must convert this vague request into a clear case intake by recording knowns, unknowns, assumptions, AI/ML boundaries, software/embedded dependencies, and clarification questions before analysis begins."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l1-m2", "title": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "Spreadsheet filter/sort, evidence checklist, basic data scan", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available