nt what can be acted on and what should be handed off."}, "student_confusion": "Should I clean the data, escalate the issue, or mark it as not ready?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Readiness Action", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You must perform a first-level telemetry-readiness action using the evidence already validated. They must count and mark missing values, identify timestamp gaps, list packet jumps, connect warning logs to data trust issues, identify unclear fields, and explain how each issue could affect anomaly detection. The output must be a usable technical handoff, not a generic observation note."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l1-m4", "title": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "tools": {"tools_used": "Risk log, escalation matrix", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m4-empower", "url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod4_01_artifact.pptx", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "M4 Empower: Final Risk and Escalation Note submission: blocker and owner decision", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Risk and Escalation Note: What decision can you defend using evidence: ready, partially ready, blocked, or escalate? Focus on blockers, risk severity, consequences, owners, and escalation criteria.", "follow_up": "Make sure your decision is based on evidence and does not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900},