 meaning, missing value basics, labelled versus unlabelled data"}, "module_no": 2, "description": "Build the L2 Model Evidence Validation Checklist by completing the L2 telemetry baseline workflow task: The learner receives the cleaned telemetry sample with 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, 4 remaining missing sensor_temp values, 3 remaining missing rpm values, and no labelled anomaly column. The learner must decide whether this cleaned sample is fit for beginner-level baseline testing and document what limitations remain before applying any anomaly logic.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may apply anomaly logic before checking remaining missing values, field meaning, label absence, and baseline feature suitability.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Field completeness, missing-data pattern, feature suitability, label availability, baseline model-readiness decision", "reason_behind_concept": "Baseline results are only interpretable when the learner knows what evidence remains incomplete and what the workflow cannot prove.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use before applying threshold or statistical logic to confirm that the cleaned sample is usable only for controlled baseline testing."}, "student_confusion": "How do I know whether a cleaned sample is good enough for beginner baseline testing?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Model Evidence Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You receive the cleaned telemetry sample with 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, 4 remaining missing sensor_temp values, 3 remaining missing rpm values, and no labelled anomaly column. You must decide whether this cleaned sample is fit for beginner-level baseline testing and document what limitations remain before applying any anomaly logic."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m3", "title": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "tools": {"tools_used": "Spreadsheet/notebook, missing-data handling note, baseline method table, suspicious-output review sheet", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: can another engineer reproduce and review the baseline workflow?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note: What workflow decision can you defend: further testing, evidence fixes, escalation, or blocked for model use?", "follow_up": "Decide whether the workflow result supports learning, more testing, evidence fixing, escalation, or blocked model use."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Workflow action kickoff: build a reproducible baseline without overclaiming accuracy", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note: What is the risk of running simple anomaly logic without documenting field choice and missing-data handling?", "follow_up": "Name the risk of running logic without documenting method choice, missing-data handling, or limitation."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: transfer simple anomaly workflow logic to another unlabelled case", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note: How would this workflow logic transfer to another unlabelled anomaly-detection case?", "follow_up": "State how this simple baseline rule could be reviewed before L3 integration-readiness."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide: simple threshold or statistical anomaly logic for baseline review", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note: What concept helps you choose or explain a threshold or statistical baseline without claiming true anomaly labels?", "follow_up": "Explain why your chosen threshold/statistical rule is simple enough for L2 and not a production model."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Select fields, handle missing values, and inspect candidate suspicious rows", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note: What fields, missing-value decisions, simple logic, and suspicious rows can you observe or produce?", "follow_up": "Use selected fields, remaining missing values, and field suitability before choosing a baseline method."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m3-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Workflow note task: document method, output observations, limitations, and handoff", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note: How will you write the workflow note so another engineer can reproduce and challenge your method?", "follow_up": "Include field choice, missing-data handling, baseline method, suspicious output review, and limitation note."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your chosen rule, missing-data handling, and suspicious-output review are documented clearly, but do not ask it to select the final decision for you.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the validated fields from M2 to create a reproducible baseline workflow note that feeds risk review in M4."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m3-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m3-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note", "description": "Can you document a controlled L2 baseline anomaly workflow, including the method used, why it is suitable for L2, how missing values were handled, and why outputs are only suspicious rather than confirmed anomalies?", "instructions": "Complete the workflow artifact by documenting dataset used, field-selection rationale, missing-data handling choice (dropped, marked, excluded from baseline logic, or handled through a simple documented rule), allowed baseline method used (fixed threshold, range check, z-score-style outlier flag, mean/standard-deviation rule, or manually documented suspicious-row rule), suspicious output observations, false-positive review, human-first reasoning, handoff message, and final action decision. Explain why the method is suitable for L2 and why the outputs are suspicious, not confirmed anomalies. Do not use advanced ML models, clustering, neural networks, or production scoring pipelines.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l2-m3", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l2/ART_L2_M3_Baseline_Anomaly_Workflow_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M3_Baseline_Anomaly_Workflow_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m3-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m3-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m3-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m3-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note", "description": "Can you draft a controlled L2 baseline anomaly workflow with a simple method, clear missing-data handling, and non-production limitation language?", "instructions": "Draft the workflow before final submission. Include your field choices, missing-data handling option, simple baseline method idea, suspicious-output review plan, and limitation note. Use AI only as a coach to test whether your reasoning is clear, not to choose the method or final decision for you.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Fixed thresholds, range checks, z-score-style flags, mean-standard-deviation rules, missing-data handling, suspicious-row review", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Mean, standard deviation, threshold, outlier, reproducible notebook or worksheet logic"}, "module_no": 3, "description": "Build the L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note by completing the L2 telemetry baseline workflow task: The learner must prepare a controlled beginner baseline anomaly workflow using selected telemetry fields. They must document field selection, state how remaining missing values are handled (dropped, marked, excluded from baseline logic, or handled through a simple documented rule), choose an allowed simple method such as fixed threshold, range check, z-score-style outlier flag, mean/standard-deviation rule, or manually documented suspicious-row rule, and explain why the choice is suitable for L2 but not a production model. Advanced ML models, unsupervised clustering, neural networks, and production scoring pipelines are not allowed at L2.", "estimatedTime": "3 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may run anomaly logic without documenting missing-data handling, method choice, or why the baseline is not production-ready.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Missing-data handling options, allowed baseline methods, suspicious-output review, reproducibility, L2 limitation language", "reason_behind_concept": "A workflow note must be reproducible and explainable so another engineer can understand what was tested and why the output is only baseline evidence.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use after validation when the learner can safely design a small baseline workflow using only allowed fields and clearly stated assumptions."}, "student_confusion": "Which simple method can I use, and how should I safely handle the remaining missing values?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Baseline Workflow Action", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You must prepare a baseline anomaly workflow using the selected telemetry fields. They must document field selection, handle remaining missing values by stating whether values are dropped, marked, excluded from baseline logic, or handled through a simple documented rule, apply or design an allowed simple baseline method (fixed threshold, range check, z-score-style outlier flag, mean/standard-deviation rule, or manually documented suspicious-row rule), identify suspicious rows, explain why outputs are suspicious and not confirmed anomalies, and prepare a workflow note another engineer can reproduce. They must not use advanced ML models, clustering, neural networks, or production scoring pipelines at L2."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m4", "title": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "tools": {"tools_used": "Risk log, false-positive review table, escalation matrix", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: what must be escalated before further model use?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note: Which risks must be escalated before the workflow can support further model use?", "follow_up": "Decide whether the suspicious output needs more testing, evidence fixing, escalation, or should be blocked from model use."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Risk kickoff: suspicious output is not the same as confirmed anomaly", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note: What could go wrong if suspicious rows are communicated as confirmed anomalies?", "follow_up": "State why a suspicious row should not be treated as a confirmed anomaly."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: transfer risk review to a future real-time inference planning case", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note: How would you transfer this risk classification to future real-time inference planning?", "follow_up": "Name one warning sign you would check before trusting suspicious outputs in another workflow."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Concept guide: risk categories for baseline model limitations and escalation", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note: What concept helps you classify baseline model risks and escalation ownership?", "follow_up": "Explain the difference between a false-positive risk, data gap, workflow limitation, and escalation item."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Identify false-positive risks, label gaps, threshold sensitivity, and integration concerns", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note: Which risks do you see: false positives, label gaps, threshold sensitivity, missing data, or integration mismatch?", "follow_up": "Use suspicious outputs, false-positive causes, label gap, threshold sensitivity, and integration concerns."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m4-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Risk log task: classify observed risks, owners, severity, and next actions", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note: How will you record severity, owner, impact, escalation reason, and recommended next action?", "follow_up": "Write the risk with observed evidence, consequence, severity, owner, escalation reason, and next action."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to help list possible false-positive causes and escalation owners, then make your own evidence-based classification.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses M3 suspicious-output observations to classify risks and prepare closure limitations for M5."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m4-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m4-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you separated suspicious outputs from confirmed anomalies and identified false-positive risks, label gaps, integration concerns, owners, and escalation needs?", "instructions": "Classify model risks using observed evidence, impact on anomaly detection, impact on integration, severity, owner, escalation reason, and recommended next action. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence used, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, reproducibility, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l2-m4", "version": 1, "file_url": "http