model use.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may present suspicious outputs as true anomalies instead of reviewing false-positive causes and escalation ownership.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Suspicious output versus confirmed anomaly, false-positive risk, threshold sensitivity, label gap, escalation ownership", "reason_behind_concept": "Risk review prevents a weak baseline from being treated as a reliable anomaly detector or integrated without confirmation.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use after suspicious outputs appear and the learner must classify risks before communicating baseline usefulness."}, "student_confusion": "How do I decide whether a suspicious flag is a real anomaly, a data issue, or an escalation item?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Model Risk & Escalation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The baseline workflow produces suspicious outputs, but suspicious output does not mean confirmed anomaly. Some flags may be caused by remaining missing values, weak feature meaning, no labelled anomaly data, threshold sensitivity, or mismatch between offline testing and future real-time inference. You must classify false-positive risks, model/workflow limitations, data gaps, and integration concerns, then decide what must be escalated and to whom."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m5", "title": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "tools": {"tools_used": "Closure report template, limitation checklist, senior-review message draft", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: suitable for learning, further testing, evidence fixes, or blocked?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: Can you defend the closure decision: learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, or blocked for model use?", "follow_up": "Make the closure decision clear: learning only, further testing, evidence fixes, escalation, or blocked for model use."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Closure kickoff: communicate baseline usefulness without production-readiness claims", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: What is the workplace risk if the closure report overclaims the baseline workflow result?", "follow_up": "Frame the closure risk as overclaiming baseline results to a senior engineer."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: reuse closure language for another baseline AI/ML review", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: How would you reuse this closure style for another AI/ML baseline review?", "follow_up": "State one communication habit you will reuse when reporting uncertain AI/ML outputs."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m