 assumptions, limitations, and next-step decision.", "module_continuity_link": "Turns M4 risk classification into a senior-review communication and closure decision."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m5-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m5-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Model Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final baseline workflow decision clear, professionally communicated, and supported by evidence, assumptions, limitations, reproducibility notes, and open issues?", "instructions": "Write the closure report showing work completed, evidence used, model quality observation, reproducibility note, assumptions and limitations, open issues, stakeholder message, closure confidence, and closure decision. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence used, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, reproducibility, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l2-m5", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l2/ART_L2_M5_Model_Quality_Closure_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M5_Model_Quality_Closure_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m5-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m5-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m5-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m5-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Model Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final baseline workflow decision clear, professionally communicated, and supported by evidence, assumptions, limitations, reproducibility notes, and open issues?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Model/workflow limitation communication, reproducibility note, closure decision options, stakeholder-ready summary", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Professional technical communication, summary writing, decision language"}, "module_no": 5, "description": "Build the L2 Model Quality and Closure Report by communicating the controlled baseline workflow result with clear limitation language. The learner must state what was tested, which fields were used, how missing values were handled, what suspicious outputs appeared, what assumptions and risks remain, whether outputs are only suspicious and not confirmed anomalies, and whether the workflow supports learning, further testing, evidence fixes, escalation, or is blocked for model use.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may give a vague success message without limitations, reproducibility notes, or a clear readiness decision.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Closure decision, limitation language, reproducibility note, stakeholder communication, next-step readiness", "reason_behind_concept": "Closure communication protects the team from overusing a baseline result and shows exactly what further evidence or testing is needed.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use after risk review when the learner must give a clear and role-safe closure decision to a senior reviewer."}, "student_confusion": "How do I communicate a useful baseline result without making it sound production-ready?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Model Closure Communication", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer asks whether the baseline anomaly workflow can support next-step planning. You must communicate what was tested, which fields were used, what suspicious outputs appeared, how missing values were handled, what assumptions were made, what risks remain, and whether the workflow is suitable for learning, further testing, or blocked for model use. The closure must explicitly avoid production-readiness claims and must include limitation language."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m6", "title": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "Portfolio pack template, artifact-chain map, final self-review checklist", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: can a reviewer trace every claim to an artifact?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack: Can a reviewer trace the final decision back to earlier artifacts and visible evidence?", "follow_up": "Decide whether the portfolio proves L2 baseline workflow capability without claiming production readiness."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Portfolio kickoff: prove this was a controlled workflow, not random model testing", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack: What is the risk if the final portfolio looks like disconnected worksheets instead of a capability proof?", "follow_up": "State the risk of submitting disconnected files instead of a traceable evidence chain."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: identify what this L2 portfolio prepares for in L3 integration-readiness work", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack: What transfer note shows how this L2 learning prepares for L3 integration-readiness work?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for moving from baseline workflow to L3 integration-readiness."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide: artifact continuity and transfer readiness for L3 integration planning", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack: What concept helps you connect artifact continuity to L3 integration-readiness transfer?", "follow_up": "Explain how intake, validation, workflow, risk, and closure together prove capability."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Collect intake, validation, workflow, risk, and closure artifacts into one trail", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack: Which artifacts prove intake, validation, field choice, anomaly logic, risk review, and closure?", "follow_up": "Check that every prior artifact is present and linked to the final decision."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m6-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Portfolio task: assemble baseline workflow evidence, limitation summary, and transfer note", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack: How will you assemble the portfolio so each claim links to evidence and an artifact?", "follow_up": "Assemble the portfolio with artifact chain, evidence map, workflow summary, risk limits, retry log, and transfer note."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether the portfolio evidence trail connects M0 through M5 and states one L3 integration-readiness transfer rule.", "module_continuity_link": "Combines all previous artifacts into a final portfolio that transfers learning toward L3 integration-readiness."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m6-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m6-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Baseline Workflow Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s baseline workflow decision back through intake, evidence validation, field selection, anomaly logic, output review, risk handling, and closure?", "instructions": "Assemble the portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, baseline workflow summary, risk and limitation summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, and reviewer validation. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence used, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, reproducibility, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l2-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l2/ART_L2_M6_Baseline_Model_Portfolio_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M6_Baseline_Model_Portfolio_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Baseline Workflow Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s baseline workflow decision back through intake, evidence validation, field selection, anomaly logic, output review, risk handling, and closure?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Evidence-chain validation, portfolio readiness, transfer note, integration-readiness boundary", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Portfolio structure, reflection, proof of capability, transfer learning"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack by compiling a complete L2 evidence chain showing case intake, evidence validation, field selection, missing-data handling, simple baseline method, suspicious-output review, risk handling, closure decision, and transfer notes for L3 integration-readiness. The portfolio must show readiness for further integration planning, not production deployment.", "estimatedTime": "3 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may submit separate files without proving a connected evidence trail or transfer readiness for L3.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, final validation, L3 transfer readiness, non-production limitation", "reason_behind_concept": "A portfolio proves capability only when the reviewer can trace decisions from evidence through workflow logic to risks and closure.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use at the end of the course to assemble a connected evidence trail rather than separate module submissions."}, "student_confusion": "How do I show that my baseline workflow is ready for L3 integration-readiness discussion, not production use?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The reviewer needs proof that you did not randomly test a model. You must compile a complete L2 evidence chain showing case intake, model evidence validation, field selection, missing-data handling, anomaly logic, output review, risk handling, closure decision, and transfer notes for L3 integration-readiness work. The portfolio must not claim production readiness."}], "duration": "16 hours", "course_id": "crs-aiml-tel-l2", "xp_reward": 700, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "AI/ML engineers need a controlled baseline workflow before advanced modelling, production scoring, or integration readiness can be discussed.", "course_code": "AIML-TEL-L2", "description": "You prepare a controlled beginner-level baseline anomaly workflow using validated telemetry fields, documents field choices, handles remaining missing values through a simple stated rule, tests fixed-threshold/range-check/z-score-style or mean-standard-deviation logic, reviews suspicious outputs, and communicates limitations without claiming a production model.", "domain_name": "Data & AI", "level_label": "L2", "sequence_no": 2, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "AI/ML engineers must select usable fields, handle remaining missing values, choose an allowed simple baseline method, review suspicious outputs as unconfirmed, document limitations, and avoid advanced ML or production-readiness claims.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515879218367-8466d910aaa4?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "AI/ML Baseline Telemetry Anomaly Workflow", "difficulty_level": "beginner", "job_pathway_role": "AI / ML Engineer", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l2-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can the learner explain the purpose and boundary of an L2 baseline anomaly workflow without claiming production-readiness? Input: use the cleaned telemetry case brief, 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, excluded status_code, 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and C++/Qt display-planning requirement, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: L2 purpose, modelling boundary, usable field summary, non-owned decisions, baseline vs production distinction, tool awareness, risk awareness, readiness decision. Evidence to cite: L1 readiness result, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, excluded status_code reason, L2 workflow boundary, baseline-versus-production distinction, remaining missing values, absent anomaly labels, and non-owned decisions. Output decision: state whether the baseline workflow can support learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, needs escalation, or is blocked for model use. Do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, use advanced ML, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l2-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner clarified the baseline objective, selected fields, excluded fields, assumptions, role boundary, and output expectations before testing logic? Input: use the cleaned telemetry case brief, 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, excluded status_code, 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and C++/Qt display-planning requirement, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Case request, baseline objective, available data, selected fields, excluded fields, unknowns, assumptions, role boundary, clarification questions, intake decision. Evidence to cite: case request, available data, selected fields, excluded status_code, assumptions, unknowns, output expectation for C++/Qt planning, role boundary, and clarification questions. Output decision: state whether the baseline workflow can support learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, needs escalation, or is blocked for model use. Do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, use advanced ML, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l2-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Model Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner checked remaining missing values, timestamp continuity, field meaning, label availability, and baseline feature suitability before applying anomaly logic? Input: use the cleaned telemetry case brief, 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, excluded status_code, 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and C++/Qt display-planning requirement, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the L2 Model Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Evidence item, source/owner, field completeness, timestamp continuity, missing-data pattern, field meaning, label availability, baseline feature suitability, model-readiness decision. Evidence to cite: remaining missing sensor_temp and rpm values, field meaning, timestamp continuity, absent anomaly labels, baseline feature suitability, excluded status_code reason, and model/workflow-readiness decision. Output decision: state whether the baseline workflow can support learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, needs escalation, or is blocked for model use. Do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, use advanced ML, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l2-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the learner’s baseline anomaly workflow reproducible, evidence-based, and clear about field choices, missing-data handling, simple logic, suspicious outputs, and limitations? Input: use the cleaned telemetry case brief, 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, excluded status_code, 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and C++/Qt display-planning requirement, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the L2 Baseline Anomaly Workflow Note by filling these required fields: Dataset used, field selection rationale, missing-data handling, feature preparation, baseline method, suspicious output observations, false-positive review, human-first reasoning, handoff message, final action decision. Evidence to cite: field-selection rationale, missing-data handling choice, chosen allowed baseline method, suspicious output observations, false-positive review, reproducibility note, and limitation statement.  Missing-data handling must state whether values are dropped, marked, excluded from baseline logic, or handled through a simple documented rule. Allowed baseline methods are fixed threshold, range check, z-score-style outlier flag, simple mean/standard-deviation rule, or manually documented suspicious-row rule. Advanced ML models, unsupervised clustering, neural networks, and production scoring pipelines are not allowed at L2. Output decision: state whether the baseline workflow can support learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, needs escalation, or is blocked for model use. Do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, use advanced ML, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l2-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner separated suspicious outputs from confirmed anomalies and identified false-positive risks, label gaps, integration concerns, owners, and escalation needs? Input: use the cleaned telemetry case brief, 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, excluded status_code, 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and C++/Qt display-planning requirement, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, risk category, observed evidence, impact on anomaly detection, impact on integration, severity, owner, escalation reason, recommended next action. Evidence to cite: suspicious outputs, false-positive risk, label gap, threshold sensitivity, missing-data impact, integration concern, escalation owner, and recommended next action.  Treat suspicious outputs as review signals, not confirmed anomalies. Decide whether each issue needs more testing, evidence fixing, escalation, or blocking from model use. Output decision: state whether the baseline workflow can support learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, needs escalation, or is blocked for model use. Do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, use advanced ML, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l2-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Model Quality and Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the final baseline workflow decision clear, professionally communicated, and supported by evidence, assumptions, limitations, reproducibility notes, and open issues? Input: use the cleaned telemetry case brief, 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, excluded status_code, 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and C++/Qt display-planning requirement, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the L2 Model Quality and Closure Report by filling these required fields: Work completed, evidence used, model quality observation, reproducibility note, assumptions and limitations, open issues, stakeholder message, closure confidence, closure decision. Evidence to cite: work completed, fields used, missing-data handling, assumptions, limitations, reproducibility note, open issues, stakeholder message, closure confidence, and closure decision.  The closure must include limitation language and must not imply deployable or production-ready anomaly detection. Output decision: state whether the baseline workflow can support learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, needs escalation, or is blocked for model use. Do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, use advanced ML, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l2-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can a reviewer trace the learner’s baseline workflow decision back through intake, evidence validation, field selection, anomaly logic, output review, risk handling, and closure? Input: use the cleaned telemetry case brief, 690 usable rows, selected fields sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, excluded status_code, 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and C++/Qt display-planning requirement, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the L2 Baseline Model Portfolio Pack by filling these required fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, baseline workflow summary, risk and limitation summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: full artifact chain, evidence map, baseline workflow summary, risk and limitation summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, and reviewer validation.  The transfer note should connect L2 outputs to L3 integration-readiness planning, not production deployment. Output decision: state whether the baseline workflow can support learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, needs escalation, or is blocked for model use. Do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, use advanced ML, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Baseline Anomaly Detection Workflow for Telemetry Data", "description": "After the L1 telemetry-readiness review, the team accepts that part of the telemetry evidence is usable but not production-ready. A senior engineer now asks for a controlled baseline anomaly-detection workflow using only the fields that passed the first review. You receive a cleaned sample of 690 usable telemetry rows, selected fields including sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, while status_code is excluded because its values are not clearly defined. The cleaned data still contains 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and a requirement that any output must be explainable enough for later C++/Qt display planning. At L2, you do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, or diagnose embedded-system root cause. You prepare a beginner-level baseline anomaly workflow, documents field selection, missing-data handling, simple threshold or statistical anomaly logic, suspicious outputs, false-positive risks, and decides whether the result can support further testing, needs evidence fixes, or is blocked for model use."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready L2 evidence for baseline anomaly workflow planning and limitation communication", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "After the L1 telemetry-readiness review, the team accepts that part of the telemetry evidence is usable but not production-ready. A senior engineer now asks for a controlled baseline anomaly-detection workflow using only the fields that passed the first review. You receive a cleaned sample of 690 usable telemetry rows, selected fields including sensor_temp, voltage, current, and rpm, while status_code is excluded because its values are not clearly defined. The cleaned data still contains 4 missing sensor_temp values, 3 missing rpm values, no labelled anomaly column, and a requirement that any output must be explainable enough for later C++/Qt display planning. At L2, you do not claim production-readiness, deploy a model, or diagnose embedded-system root cause. You prepare a beginner-level baseline anomaly workflow, documents field selection, missing-data handling, simple threshold or statistical anomaly logic, suspicious outputs, false-positive risks, and decides whether the result can support further testing, needs evidence fixes, or is blocked for model use."}, {"id": "lpc-aiml-tel-l3", "gap": 2, "badge": "Integration Readiness", "title": "Real-Time AI/ML Integration Readiness for Telemetry Systems", "status": "not_started", "modules": [{"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l3-m0", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "tools": {"tools_used": "Course brief, integration-readiness worksheet, C++/Qt requirement note", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l3/content/c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: defend the integration readiness sheet decision with evidence", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Integration Readiness Sheet: What decision can you defend using evidence from this module?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence; state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, needs escalation, or is blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l3/content/c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Integration Readiness Sheet kickoff: workplace risk and decision boundary", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Integration Readiness Sheet: What is the workplace risk in this module before any solution or recommendation is suggested?", "follow_up": "Name the risk using this module context: Learner may treat an offline baseline result as integration-ready without checking interface, latency, and explainability constraints."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l3/content/c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: transfer integration readiness sheet reasoning to the next AI/ML workflow", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Integration Readiness Sheet: How can this learning transfer to the next dataset, team handoff, or level?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for transferring this artifact to L4 automation/reporting."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l3/content/c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide: concepts and role boundary for integration readiness sheet", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Integration Readiness Sheet: Which concept or boundary helps you understand this issue?", "follow_up": "Explain in simple words using these concepts: Offline versus near-real-time workflow, C++/Qt display context, input-output mapping, latency expectation, explainability need"}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l3/content/c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for integration readiness sheet", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Integration Readiness Sheet: What visible evidence should you inspect before completing this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to module-specific evidence: baseline workflow summary, 690 usable rows, selected fields, offline-versus-real-time boundary, C++/Qt context, latency expectation, explainability need"}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l3/content/c-aiml-tel-l3-m0-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L3 Integration Readiness Sheet", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Integration Readiness Sheet: What exactly will you write in the artifact so it is useful to a reviewer?", "follow_up": "Include the required fields: L3 purpose, offline vs real-time difference, C++/Qt integration context, expected input fields, expected output fields, latency expectation, explainability need, readiness decision"}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to explain the difference between offline test output and integration-ready output, then define the L3 boundary in your own words.", "module_continuity_link": "Creates the Integration Readiness Sheet that becomes the context input for integration case intake."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l3-m0-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l3-m0-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L3 Integration Readiness Sheet", "description": "Can you explain the difference between offline baseline output and integration-ready evidence for C++/Qt planning