 workflow", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Portfolio Pack: How can this learning transfer to the next dataset, team handoff, or level?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for transferring this artifact to L5 solution validation."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m6-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m6-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide: concepts and role boundary for automation portfolio pack", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Portfolio Pack: Which concept or boundary helps you understand this issue?", "follow_up": "Explain in simple words using these concepts: Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, controlled report summary, automation risk summary, transfer to L5 solution validation"}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m6-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m6-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for automation portfolio pack", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Portfolio Pack: What visible evidence should you inspect before completing this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to module-specific evidence: full artifact chain from readiness, intake, validation, controlled report, automation risk, closure, and transfer note for L5 solution validation"}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m6-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m6-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L4 Automation Portfolio Pack", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Portfolio Pack: What exactly will you write in the artifact so it is useful to a reviewer?", "follow_up": "Include the required fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, controlled report summary, automation risk summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation"}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether every report claim links to evidence or is marked as assumption, not to create new claims.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses all previous artifacts to produce the L4 portfolio and transfer note for L5 solution validation."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l4-m6-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l4-m6-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L4 Automation Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s controlled reporting decision through intake, validation, report revision, risk handling, closure, and transfer to L5?", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering: Can a reviewer trace you’s controlled reporting decision through intake, validation, report revision, risk handling, closure, and transfer to L5? Fill the required workbook fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, controlled report summary, automation risk summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L4 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l4-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l4/ART_L4_M6_Automation_Portfolio_Template", "file_name": "ART_L4_M6_Automation_Portfolio_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l4-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l4-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l4-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l4-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L4 Automation Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s controlled reporting decision through intake, validation, report revision, risk handling, closure, and transfer to L5?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Evidence mapping, artifact chain, controlled report summary, automation risk summary, transfer note", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Portfolio structure, claim traceability, proof of capability"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the L4 Automation Portfolio Pack by completing the L4 telemetry AI/ML task: The reviewer needs proof that the learner can use AI automation responsibly. The learner must compile the complete L4 evidence chain showing intake, evidence validation, controlled reporting, unsupported claim handling, risk escalation, closure decision, and transfer notes for L5 solution validation.", "estimatedTime": "3 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may submit a polished report without showing the evidence chain, claim corrections, risks, and controls behind it.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, controlled report summary, automation risk summary, transfer to L5 solution validation", "reason_behind_concept": "A portfolio proves L4 capability when the reviewer can trace claims from evidence to controls and closure.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use at the end of L4 to assemble a complete automation and reporting-control evidence trail."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that AI-assisted reporting was controlled and evidence-based?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The reviewer needs proof that you can use AI automation responsibly. You must compile the complete L4 evidence chain showing intake, evidence validation, controlled reporting, unsupported claim handling, risk escalation, closure decision, and transfer notes for L5 solution validation."}], "duration": "20 hours", "course_id": "crs-aiml-tel-l4", "xp_reward": 1100, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "AI/ML engineers need to control predictive and LLM reporting workflows so anomaly outputs are not mistaken for confirmed engineering conclusions.", "course_code": "AIML-TEL-L4", "description": "You can extend anomaly outputs into predictive insight and reporting workflows, validate automation boundaries, review LLM-generated summaries, and control risks around false insight, weak explanation, and decision misuse.", "domain_name": "Data & AI", "level_label": "L4", "sequence_no": 4, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "AI/ML engineers must separate evidence-based observations from AI-generated interpretation, revise unsupported claims, define human review controls, and communicate automation limitations clearly.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515879218367-8466d910aaa4?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "AI/ML Predictive Analytics and Reporting Control", "difficulty_level": "advanced", "job_pathway_role": "AI / ML Engineer", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l4-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Automation Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can the learner explain the boundary between evidence, prediction, LLM interpretation, and decision support? Input: use the L4 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: 690 cleaned rows, 26 anomaly flags, trend summary, draft LLM incident summary, evidence-versus-interpretation boundary, human review need. Action: complete the L4 Automation Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: L4 purpose, anomaly-to-insight boundary, LLM reporting boundary, evidence vs interpretation rule, human review need, automation risk awareness, readiness decision. Evidence to cite: 690 cleaned rows, 26 anomaly flags, trend summary, draft LLM incident summary, evidence-versus-interpretation boundary, human review need. Output decision: state whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, needs more evidence, or is blocked until reporting boundaries are corrected. Do not claim confirmed failure, autonomous engineering decision, production prediction, or component degradation without labelled failure data and validated evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l4-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Predictive Analytics Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner clarified what can be predicted, described, reviewed by humans, or treated as unsafe to claim? Input: use the L4 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: senior engineer reporting request, anomaly flags, 3-cycle trend summary, LLM draft, no labelled failure data, unsafe claims, role boundary. Action: complete the L4 Predictive Analytics Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Reporting request, available evidence, trend scope, LLM draft input, unsupported claims, role boundary, assumptions, clarification questions, intake decision. Evidence to cite: senior engineer reporting request, anomaly flags, 3-cycle trend summary, LLM draft, no labelled failure data, unsafe claims, role boundary. Output decision: state whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, needs more evidence, or is blocked until reporting boundaries are corrected. Do not claim confirmed failure, autonomous engineering decision, production prediction, or component degradation without labelled failure data and validated evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l4-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 AI/LLM Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner checked anomaly flags, short trend history, LLM faithfulness, unsupported claims, and predictive-language justification? Input: use the L4 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: 26 anomaly flags, 3-cycle trend summary, unsupported degradation claim, LLM draft statements, labelled failure absence, maintenance record absence, predictive-language evidence. Action: complete the L4 AI/LLM Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Evidence item, source/owner, anomaly flag review, trend history check, LLM faithfulness check, unsupported claim check, predictive-language validation, automation-readiness decision. Evidence to cite: 26 anomaly flags, 3-cycle trend summary, unsupported degradation claim, LLM draft statements, labelled failure absence, maintenance record absence, predictive-language evidence. Output decision: state whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, needs more evidence, or is blocked until reporting boundaries are corrected. Do not claim confirmed failure, autonomous engineering decision, production prediction, or component degradation without labelled failure data and validated evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l4-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Predictive Insight and Report Automation Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Does the learner separate observed facts, trend assumptions, anomaly interpretation, unsupported claims, and human review points? Input: use the L4 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: observed telemetry facts, trend-based assumptions, anomaly interpretations, removed unsupported claims, revised report text, human review points. Action: complete the L4 Predictive Insight and Report Automation Note by filling these required fields: Evidence-backed observations, trend-based assumptions, anomaly interpretation, removed unsupported claims, revised report text, human review points, final report decision. Evidence to cite: observed telemetry facts, trend-based assumptions, anomaly interpretations, removed unsupported claims, revised report text, human review points. Output decision: state whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, needs more evidence, or is blocked until reporting boundaries are corrected. Do not claim confirmed failure, autonomous engineering decision, production prediction, or component degradation without labelled failure data and validated evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l4-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Automation Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner classified unsupported LLM claims, overconfident wording, short trend history, label gaps, explainability risk, and misuse risk? Input: use the L4 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: unsupported LLM claims, short trend history, no failure labels, weak explainability, report misuse risk, owners and escalation needs. Action: complete the L4 Automation Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, risk category, observed evidence, consequence, severity, owner, escalation reason, recommended next action. Evidence to cite: unsupported LLM claims, short trend history, no failure labels, weak explainability, report misuse risk, owners and escalation needs. Output decision: state whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, needs more evidence, or is blocked until reporting boundaries are corrected. Do not claim confirmed failure, autonomous engineering decision, production prediction, or component degradation without labelled failure data and validated evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l4-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Insight Quality and Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the final report decision clear about evidence-supported insights, rejected claims, remaining limitations, and human review controls? Input: use the L4 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: accepted insights, rejected or revised claims, limitations, human review conditions, stakeholder message, closure confidence and decision. Action: complete the L4 Insight Quality and Closure Report by filling these required fields: Work completed, evidence used, accepted insights, rejected claims, remaining limitations, stakeholder message, closure confidence, closure decision. Evidence to cite: accepted insights, rejected or revised claims, limitations, human review conditions, stakeholder message, closure confidence and decision. Output decision: state whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, needs more evidence, or is blocked until reporting boundaries are corrected. Do not claim confirmed failure, autonomous engineering decision, production prediction, or component degradation without labelled failure data and validated evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l4-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Automation Portfolio Pack", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can a reviewer trace the learner’s controlled reporting decision through intake, validation, report revision, risk handling, closure, and transfer to L5? Input: use the L4 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: full artifact chain from readiness, intake, validation, controlled report, automation risk, closure, and transfer note for L5 solution validation. Action: complete the L4 Automation Portfolio Pack by filling these required fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, controlled report summary, automation risk summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: full artifact chain from readiness, intake, validation, controlled report, automation risk, closure, and transfer note for L5 solution validation. Output decision: state whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, needs more evidence, or is blocked until reporting boundaries are corrected. Do not claim confirmed failure, autonomous engineering decision, production prediction, or component degradation without labelled failure data and validated evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Predictive Analytics, LLM Reporting, and AI Workflow Control for Telemetry Systems", "description": "After L3 integration-readiness review, the senior engineer wants to know whether anomaly outputs can support a simple predictive analytics and reporting workflow. You receive 690 cleaned telemetry rows, 26 anomaly flags from the baseline workflow, a 3-cycle trend summary, a draft LLM-generated incident summary, and a requirement that any report must clearly separate evidence-based observations from AI-generated interpretation. The draft report incorrectly states that “rpm instability confirms component degradation,” even though no labelled failure data or maintenance record is available. You must decide whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, or blocked until evidence, trend logic, and reporting boundaries are corrected."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready L4 evidence for predictive insight, LLM reporting control, and automation risk communication", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "After L3 integration-readiness review, the senior engineer wants to know whether anomaly outputs can support a simple predictive analytics and reporting workflow. You receive 690 cleaned telemetry rows, 26 anomaly flags from the baseline workflow, a 3-cycle trend summary, a draft LLM-generated incident summary, and a requirement that any report must clearly separate evidence-based observations from AI-generated interpretation. The draft report incorrectly states that “rpm instability confirms component degradation,” even though no labelled failure data or maintenance record is available. You must decide whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, or blocked until evidence, trend logic, and reporting boundaries are corrected."}, {"id": "lpc-aiml-tel-l5", "gap": 2, "badge": "Decision-Support Validation", "title": "End-to-End AI/ML Telemetry Decision-Support Validation", "status": "not_started", "modules": [{"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l5-m0", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "tools": {"tools_used": "Course brief, solution-readiness worksheet, L1-L4 evidence map", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l5-m0-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l5/content/c-aiml-tel-l5-m0-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: defend the solution readiness sheet decision with evidence", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Solution Readiness Sheet: What decision can you defend using evidence from this module?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence; state whether the workflow is ready as a supervised decision-support prototype, ready only for further controlled testing, or blocked until stronger evidence and governance controls are added."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l5-m0-engag