 "module_no": 0, "description": "Build the L5 Solution Readiness Sheet by completing the L5 telemetry AI/ML task: The learner is moving from module-level work to end-to-end solution validation. The risk is that separate artifacts may look individually acceptable but fail as a connected decision-support workflow. The learner must understand how data readiness, baseline modelling, integration, reporting, and governance connect before making a final recommendation.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may judge artifacts individually without checking whether the full workflow is safe as connected decision support.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "End-to-end workflow map, L1-L4 evidence summary, decision-support boundary, human review requirement, governance awareness", "reason_behind_concept": "A solution can be safe only when data, model, integration, reporting, and risk evidence work together under human control.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use before final solution validation so the learner understands how earlier evidence connects and where governance applies."}, "student_confusion": "If each earlier level has artifacts, does that mean the full AI/ML workflow is ready?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Solution Readiness Orientation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You are moving from module-level work to end-to-end solution validation. The risk is that separate artifacts may look individually acceptable but fail as a connected decision-support workflow. You must understand how data readiness, baseline modelling, integration, reporting, and governance connect before making a final recommendation."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l5-m1", "title": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "tools": {"tools_used": "End-to-end case intake template, stakeholder request, risk register", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_sec