"currentStreak": "18 days", "longestStreak": "143 days"}, "learnerProfile": {"domain": "Backend Engineering", "industry": "Information Technology & AI", "grade_level": "Undergraduate", "skill_level": "Beginner", "target_role": "Backend Engineer"}, "currentLearningPathTitle": "Current Learning Path: Product Design Foundation"}', '{"courses": [{"id": "lpc-001", "gap": 2, "badge": "none", "title": "Observability: Logging, Monitoring & Debugging", "status": "in_progress", "modules": [{"id": "mod-001", "title": "System Failure Investigation", "tools": {"tools_used": "Free", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "completed", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "completed", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "completed", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "completed", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "completed", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "completed", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "completed", "content": [{"id": "c9", "url": "#", "order": 1, "stage": "empower", "title": "Final: Incident Investigation Report", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "Looking at the Final Incident Investigation Report requirements, what section do you think will be hardest to complete well, and what makes it challenging?", "follow_up": "Agreed - that section trips up a lot of engineers. What is your strategy to tackle it?"}], "content_type": "doc"}, {"id": "c1", "url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/courses/COURSE001/video/Video%201.mp4", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Incident Kickoff: API Latency Spike", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "You just watched the Incident Kickoff video. In your own words, what was the primary symptom of the API latency spike, and what made it hard to diagnose at first?", "follow_up": "Interesting take. How do you think the on-call engineer should have prioritised their first 15 minutes of investigation?"}, {"question": "What signals from the video would you look for first if you were the engineer on call during that incident?", "follow_up": "Good thinking. Would those signals alone be enough to identify the root cause, or would you need more data?"}], "content_type": "video", "duration_seconds": 540}, {"id": "c2", "url": "#", "order": 2, "stage": "engage", "title": "Failure Investigation Worksheet", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "After reviewing the Failure Investigation Worksheet, what do you think is the most important column to fill in first, and why?", "follow_up": "Nice reasoning. How would you handle a situation where you don''t have enough data to fill that column?"}], "content_type": "pdf"}, {"id": "c10", "url": "#", "order": 1, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection Prompts & Next Steps", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "Reflecting on everything you have done in this module: what is one mental model or habit you would do differently in your next real incident, and why?", "follow_up": "That is a meaningful reflection. How would you share that learning with a teammate who was not on this incident?"}], "content_type": "text"}, {"id": "c6", "url": "#", "order": 1, "stage": "explain", "title": "System Architecture Overview", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "You have just reviewed the System Architecture Overview slides. What part of the architecture surprised you most, and how does it affect the way you would approach debugging a failure in it?", "follow_up": "That is a thoughtful observation. How would you document that insight so that a new team member could benefit from it?"}, {"question": "Based on the slides, where in the system would you instrument logging first if you had to pick just one layer - and what would you capture there?", "follow_up": "Good choice. What would you sacrifice by instrumenting only that layer, and how would you compensate?"}], "content_type": "slide"}, {"id": "c7", "url": "#", "order": 2, "stage": "explain", "title": "Request Lifecycle Deep Dive", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "The Request Lifecycle Deep Dive covered many hops. Identify the single hop where you believe latency is most likely to accumulate silently, and explain why.", "follow_up": "Strong reasoning. What metric would you define to detect latency accumulating at that hop before it becomes a user-visible incident?"}], "content_type": "video", "duration_seconds": 960}, {"id": "c3", "url": "#", "order": 1, "stage": "explore", "title": "Structured Log Analysis Guide", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "The Structured Log Analysis Guide covers several log fields. Which field do you think gives the most diagnostic value during an incident, and what''s your reasoning?", "follow_up": "Good point. How does that field help you narrow down from hundreds of log lines to the ones that actually matter?"}], "content_type": "pdf"}, {"id": "c4", "url": "#", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Service Architecture Diagram", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "Looking at the Service Architecture Diagram, which service boundary do you think is the most likely source of latency under high load, and why?", "follow_up": "Solid analysis. What observability would you add at that boundary to catch issues earlier?"}], "content_type": "image"}, {"id": "c5", "url": "#", "order": 3, "stage": "explore", "title": "Reading Trace IDs in Distributed Systems", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "After watching the Trace IDs video, explain in your own words how a trace ID flows through a distributed system and why it matters for debugging.", "follow_up": "Great explanation. Can you think of a scenario where trace IDs alon