nt template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, or missed-risk prompts.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Risk category, severity, evidence consequence, owner mapping, escalation criteria", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Risk log basics, escalation logic, impact statements"}, "module_no": 4, "description": "Build the Risk and Escalation Note by classifying readiness issues as minor, major, blocker, or escalation-needed and assigning the right owner.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may ignore blockers such as unclear sensor meaning, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, or log warnings.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Blocker identification, risk classification, escalation criteria", "reason_behind_concept": "Escalation decisions must be based on observed evidence and consequence, not assumptions about system failure or root cause.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use when evidence issues may prevent safe next-step AI/ML work or require support from another owner."}, "student_confusion": "Which issues are minor observations and which are blockers?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Risk & Escalation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You now sees that missing temperature values may hide thermal anomalies, rpm gaps may weaken pattern detection, duplicate timestamps may create false anomaly spikes, packet jumps may indicate dropped data, and unclear field metadata may lead to wrong features. You must classify which issues are minor, which are blockers, what the consequence is, and whether the issue belongs to AI/ML, software, embedded, test, or senior engineering escalation."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l1-m5", "title": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "tools": {"tools_used": "Closure report template, reviewer checklist", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-empower", "url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod5_01_Artifact.pptx", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "M5 Empower: Final Quality and Closure Report submission: professional readiness closure", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What decision can you defend using evidence: ready, partially ready, blocked, or escalate? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Make sure your decision is based on evidence and does not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-engage", "url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/explore/mod5_exp.png", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "M5 Engage: Closure kickoff: senior engineer needs a clear readiness decision", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What is the workplace risk if this part of the telemetry readiness review is skipped or rushed? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Name the risk in one sentence before opening the template."}], "content_type": "image", "duration_seconds": 600}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-evolve", "url": "#", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "M5 Evolve: Transfer reflection: communicating readiness decisions in other technical reviews", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: How would you transfer this validation logic to another dataset, sensor stream, or industry case? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Write one transfer rule you can reuse in a future AI/ML evidence-readiness review."}], "content_type": "reflection", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-explain", "url": "#", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "M5 Explain: Closure communication guide: clear, careful, evidence-backed readiness decisions", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What concept or role boundary helps you understand the issue without overclaiming root cause? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "State the concept in simple words and link it to the telemetry case."}], "content_type": "video", "duration_seconds": 600}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-explore", "url": "#", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "M5 Explore: Review checks passed, checks failed, open issues, and confidence level", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What evidence can you observe in the case, dataset summary, logs, UDP description, or shared-memory field list? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Point to at least one visible evidence item rather than using a general opinion."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-express", "url": "#", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "M5 Express: Practice Quality and Closure Report using checks and decision options", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What exactly will you write in your artifact, and which evidence will you cite? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Check whether your artifact separates facts, assumptions, role boundary, and next action."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your closure message is clear to a non-technical reviewer and whether it avoids overclaiming.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the Risk and Escalation Note from Module 4 and creates the closure record that feeds the final portfolio in Module 6."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m5-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m5-f1", "order": 1, "title": "Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final decision clear: ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation, and is it supported by checks passed, checks failed, and open evidence issues?", "instructions": "Write the closure report showing work completed, evidence used, checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence level, closure message, and final readiness decision. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence, reasoning clarity, correct role boundary, escalation where needed, and complete fields.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l1-m5", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod5_02_Template.xlsx", "file_name": "Mod5_02_Template.xlsx", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m5-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m5-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m5-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m5-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final decision clear: ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation, and is it supported by checks passed, checks failed, and open evidence issues?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, or missed-risk prompts.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Closure reporting, reviewer communication, confidence level, decision statement", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Professional summary writing, quality assurance, evidence-backed communication"}, "module_no": 5, "description": "Build the Quality and Closure Report by summarising checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and the final readiness decision.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may communicate findings vaguely without a clear readiness decision.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Quality check, professional communication, closure decision", "reason_behind_concept": "A readiness review is valuable only when the final message is clear, evidence-backed, and careful about what L1 can and cannot claim.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use after risks and escalations are known and the learner must close the review professionally."}, "student_confusion": "How do I explain technical evidence to a reviewer or senior?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Closure Communication", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer needs a clear decision, not a long explanation. You must communicate what was checked, what passed, what failed, what evidence is still missing, and whether the telemetry pack is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for baseline anomaly detection. The closure must avoid overclaiming model-readiness and must clearly show what the next team should do."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l1-m6", "title": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "Portfolio pack template, final self-review checklist", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m6-empower", "url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod6_02_Artifact_portfolio.pptx", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "M6 Empower: Final Portfolio Pack submission: complete L1 capability proof", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Final Portfolio Pack: What decision can you defend using evidence: ready, partially ready, blocked, or escalate? Focus on artifact continuity, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, and reviewer validation.", "follow_up": "Make sure your decision is based on evidence and does not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m6-engage", "url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/explore/mod6_exp.png", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "M6 Engage: Portfolio kickoff: proving one connected evidence trail", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Final Portfolio Pack: What is the workplace risk if this part of the telemetry readiness review is skipped or rushed? Focus on artifact continuity, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, and reviewer validation.", "follow_up": "Name the risk in one sentence before opening the template."}], "content_type": "image", "duration_seconds": 600}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m6-evolve", "url": "#", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "M6 Evolve: Transfer reflection: reusing the portfolio evidence trail for future capability proof", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Final Portfolio Pack: How would you transfer this validation logic to another dataset, sensor stream, or industry case? Focus on artifact continuity, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, and reviewer validation.", "follow_up": "Write one transfer rule you can reuse in a future AI/ML evidence-readiness review."}], "content_type": "reflection", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m6-explain", "url": "#", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "M6 Explain: Portfolio validation guide: how reviewers trace evidence to final decision", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Final Portfolio Pack: What concept or role boundary helps you understand the issue without overclaiming root cause? Focus on artifact continuity, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, and reviewer validation.", "follow_up": "State the concept in simple words and link it to the telemetry case."}], "content_type": "video", "duration_seconds": 600}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m6-explore", "url": "#", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "M6 Explore: Map readiness, intake, validation, action, risk, and closure artifacts into one chain", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Final Portfolio Pack: What evidence can you observe in the case, dataset summary, logs, UDP description, or shared-memory field list? Focus on artifact continuity, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, and reviewer validation.", "follow_up": "Point to at least one visible evidence item rather than using a general opinion."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m6-express", "url": "#", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "M6 Express: Practice Final Portfolio Pack using artifact continuity map", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Final Portfolio Pack: What exactly will you write in your artifact, and which evidence will you cite? Focus on artifact continuity, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, and reviewer validation.", "follow_up": "Check whether your artifact separates facts, assumptions, role boundary, and next action."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your final portfolio shows a complete evidence trail and whether any artifact connection is missing.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses all previous artifacts and produces the final review-ready capability proof for certification or portfolio validation."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m6-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m6-f1", "order": 1, "title": "Final Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s final readiness decision back to earlier artifacts, evidence checks, risks, escalations, and closure communication?", "instructions": "Assemble the portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, and reviewer validation so the evidence trail is visible. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence, reasoning clarity, correct role boundary, escalation where needed, and complete fields.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l1-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod6_02_Template_Lean.xlsx", "file_name": "Mod6_02_Template_Lean.xlsx", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: Final Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s final readiness decision back to earlier artifacts, evidence checks, risks, escalations, and closure communication?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, or missed-risk prompts.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Evidence chain, artifact continuity, portfolio packaging, transfer reflection", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Self-review, artifact sequencing, portfolio proof"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the Final Portfolio Pack by connecting all previous artifacts into one evidence trail that proves L1 anomaly-readiness validation capability.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may submit separate worksheets without showing a connected evidence trail.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, final validation", "reason_behind_concept": "Capability proof requires traceability from the final decision back to earlier evidence, reasoning, risks, and closure communication.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use at the end of the course when the learner must package artifact evidence for review and transfer to other data-readiness contexts."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that my decision came from evidence?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The reviewer must see that you did not complete seven disconnected tasks. You must assemble a complete evidence chain from readiness, intake, validation, action, risk, and closure into one portfolio. The portfolio must prove that you can responsibly inspect telemetry evidence and make an L1 anomaly-readiness decision before model work begins."}], "duration": "14 hours", "course_id": "crs-aiml-tel-l1", "xp_reward": 500, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "AI/ML engineers must verify telemetry evidence quality before attempting anomaly detection or model work.", "course_code": "AIML-TEL-L1", "description": "You validate whether telemetry evidence is ready for AI/ML anomaly detection, identifies visible readiness gaps, separates AI/ML responsibility from software/embedded dependencies, and prepares an evidence-based readiness or escalation note.", "domain_name": "Data & AI", "level_label": "L1", "sequence_no": 1, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "AI/ML engineers must check telemetry evidence quality, role ownership, and escalation needs before treating any dataset as model-ready.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515879218367-8466d910aaa4?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "AI/ML Telemetry Evidence Readiness", "difficulty_level": "beginner", "job_pathway_role": "AI / ML Engineer", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Course Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: What does the learner understand about why telemetry data must be validated before AI/ML use, and can they map the industry context, role boundary, evidence sources, and readiness decision without jumping to model-building? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Course Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: Industry system map, telemetry source map, stakeholder map, AI/ML-owned responsibilities, software/embedded dependencies, evidence required before model work, learner readiness gaps, readiness decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner separated observed facts from assumptions and clarified what an L1 AI/ML learner owns versus what must be escalated? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Case request, available inputs, missing information, knowns, unknowns, assumptions, role boundary, clarification questions, intake decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner checked missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, field meaning, and warning logs before judging anomaly-readiness? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Evidence item, source/owner, completeness check, timestamp check, missing-value check, packet continuity check, field meaning check, ML-readiness impact, validation decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Telemetry Readiness Action Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the learner’s recommendation supported by evidence from the checklist and clearly separated into action, handoff, escalation, or blocked-readiness decision? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Telemetry Readiness Action Note by filling these required fields: Evidence reviewed, missing-value count, timestamp issues, packet jumps, log warnings, anomaly-readiness impact, human-first reasoning, handoff message, final action decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner identified which issues require senior, telemetry, embedded, software, test, or data-owner support and explained the consequence of each blocker? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, risk category, observed evidence, consequence, severity, owner, escalation reason, next action. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Quality and Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the final decision clear: ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation, and is it supported by checks passed, checks failed, and open evidence issues? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Quality and Closure Report by filling these required fields: Work completed, evidence used, checks passed, checks failed, open issues, closure message, confidence level, closure decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Final Portfolio Pack", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can a reviewer trace the learner’s final readiness decision back to earlier artifacts, evidence checks, risks, escalations, and closure communication? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Final Portfolio Pack by filling these required fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Telemetry Evidence Readiness for AI/ML Anomaly Detection", "description": "A telemetry test team has completed a 12-minute aerospace electronics lab run and shared a small evidence pack for AI/ML review before anomaly detection begins. The pack contains 720 telemetry rows with timestamp, packet_id, sensor_temp, voltage, current, rpm, and status_code, plus a short application log, UDP packet description, and shared-memory field list. During the first check, the evidence shows 18 missing sensor_temp values, 11 missing rpm values, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, and log warnings such as delayed UDP packets and shared-memory read timeout. At L1, you do not build an anomaly-detection model or diagnose embedded-system root cause. You validate whether telemetry data is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-detection work, and prepares an evidence-based readiness or escalation note supported by the visible evidence."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready L1 evidence for AI/ML telemetry readiness review", "completion_percentage": 14, "common_course_problem_statement": "A telemetry test team has completed a 12-minute aerospace electronics lab run and shared a small evidence pack for AI/ML review before anomaly detection begins. The pack contains 720 telemetry rows with timestamp, packet_id, sensor_temp, voltage, current, rpm, and status_code, plus a short application log, UDP packet description, and shared-memory field list. During the first check, the evidence shows 18 missing sensor_temp values, 11 missing rpm values, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, and log warnings such as delayed UDP packets and shared-memory read timeout. At L1, you do not build an anomaly-detection model or diagnose embedded-system root cause. You validate whether telemetry data is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-detection work, and prepares an evidence-based readiness or escalation note supported by the visible evidence."}, {"id": "lpc-aiml-tel-l2", "gap": 2, "badge": "Baseline Anomaly Workflow", "title": "Baseline Anomaly Detection Workflow for Telemetry Data", "status": "not_started", "modules": [{"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m0", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "tools": {"tools_used": "Course brief, model workflow map, readiness worksheet", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: can this case move from readiness review to controlled baseline workflow?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: What decision can you defend about moving from evidence-readiness to baseline workflow?", "follow_up": "Defend whether the workflow is for learning, further testing, evidence fixing, escalation, or blocked use."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Baseline workflow kickoff: why simple anomaly logic is not production AI", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: What is the workplace risk if a beginner presents a baseline anomaly experiment as a production model?", "follow_up": "Explain the risk as overclaiming a simple workflow as production AI, not as a coding problem."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: transfer baseline-versus-production caution to another AI/ML task", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: How would this baseline-versus-production boundary transfer to another AI/ML use case?", "follow_up": "Write one rule that stops L2 baseline work from becoming an unsupported production claim."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide: L2 boundary between baseline testing and production model claims", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: What concept helps you separate baseline workflow evidence from production model readiness?", "follow_up": "Define baseline workflow, production model, and limitation in simple telemetry words."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect L1-ready fields and remaining evidence limits before workflow planning", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: Which fields and limitations from the L1 review should control this L2 workflow?", "follow_up": "Point to the L1 readiness result, selected fields, excluded status_code, and remaining missing values."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Worksheet: document L2 purpose, usable fields, non-owned decisions, and readiness", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: What will you write in the readiness sheet to show L2 purpose, boundary, tools, and risks?", "follow_up": "Include L2 purpose, boundary, usable fields, non-owned decisions, and readiness decision."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to explain the difference between a baseline anomaly workflow and a production model, then write the boundary in your own words.", "module_continuity_link": "Creates the Model Workflow Readiness Sheet that becomes the context input for baseline case intake."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m0-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m0-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet", "description": "Can you explain the purpose and boundary of an L2 baseline anomaly workflow without claiming production-readiness?", "instructions": "Complete the readiness artifact by documenting L2 purpose, modelling boundary, usable field summary, non-owned decisions, baseline versus production distinction, tool awareness, risk awareness, and readiness decision. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence used, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, reproducibility, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l2-m0", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l2/ART_L2_M0_Model_Workflow_Readiness_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M0_Model_Workflow_Readiness_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m0-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m0-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m0-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m0-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet", "description": "Can you explain the purpose and boundary of an L2 baseline anomaly workflow without claiming production-readiness?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Baseline workflow purpose, model boundary, usable field awareness, production-readiness limitation", "academic_refresher_concepts": "AI/ML workflow stages, baseline experiment, model limitation language"}, "module_no": 0, "description": "Build the L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet by completing the L2 telemetry baseline workflow task: The learner is now moving from evidence-readiness to baseline anomaly workflow. The risk is that a beginner may overclaim a simple experiment as a production model. The learner must understand what L2 allows: selecting usable fields, handling remaining missing values, preparing simple anomaly logic, reviewing outputs, and documenting assumptions while clearly stating that the workflow is only baseline evidence.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may treat a baseline experiment as a production anomaly-detection model instead of a controlled learning workflow.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "L2 AI/ML workflow boundary, baseline versus production distinction, field-selection readiness, limitation awareness", "reason_behind_concept": "A beginner baseline is useful only when its purpose, assumptions, allowed decisions, and limitations are clear before work begins.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use at the start of an L2 telemetry workflow before selecting fields, handling missing values, or testing anomaly logic."}, "student_confusion": "Does building a baseline workflow mean I have built a real model?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Workflow Readiness Orientation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You are now moving from evidence-readiness to baseline anomaly workflow. The risk is that a beginner may overclaim a simple experiment as a production model. You must understand what L2 allows: selecting usable fields, handling remaining missing values, preparing simple anomaly logic, reviewing outputs, and documenting assumptions while clearly stating that the workflow is only baseline evidence."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m1", "title": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "tools": {"tools_used": "Case intake template, selected-field list, telemetry field description", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: is the baseline case intake clear enough to validate evidence?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: Is the case intake clear enough to move into evidence validation, or does it need escalation first?", "follow_up": "Make an intake decision before testing logic; do not jump directly to anomaly flags."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Case intake kickoff: unpack the senior engineer request for baseline anomaly workflow", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: What could go wrong if you begin testing anomaly logic before clarifying the senior engineer request?", "follow_up": "State why a broad baseline request can create wrong field choices or wrong ownership."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: reuse intake logic for another unlabelled telemetry workflow", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: How would you reuse this intake approach for another broad AI/ML request?", "follow_up": "Name one intake question you would reuse before any future baseline workflow."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Role boundary guide: what L2 AI/ML you can decide versus escalate", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: What role-boundary concept helps you know what L2 AI/ML can decide and what must be escalated?", "follow_up": "Separate what AI/ML can document from what senior, software, embedded, or data owners must confirm."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Identify selected fields, excluded status_code, assumptions, and output expectations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: What evidence do you see about selected fields, excluded status_code, assumptions, and output needs?", "follow_up": "Use the case request, selected fields, excluded status_code, assumptions, unknowns, and C++/Qt output expectation."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: write baseline objective, unknowns, assumptions, and clarification questions", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: What will you write in the case intake note to separate facts, unknowns, assumptions, and clarification questions?", "follow_up": "Write the intake with facts, unknowns, assumptions, clarification questions, and role boundary."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to help list clarification questions about anomaly definition, selected fields, excluded fields, and output format without asking it to decide the workflow for you.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the Model Workflow Readiness Sheet from Module 0 and produces a case intake note for evidence validation."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m1-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m1-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Baseline Workflow Case Intake Note", "description": "Has you clarified the baseline objective, selected fields, excluded fields, assumptions, role boundary, and output expectations before testing logic?", "instructions": "Record the case request, baseline objective, available data, selected fields, excluded fields, unknowns, assumptions, role boundary, clarification questions, and intake decision. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence used, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, reproducibility, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l2-m1", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l2/ART_L2_M1_Baseline_Model_Case_Intake_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M1_Baseline_Model_Case_Intake_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m1-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m1-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m1-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m1-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Baseline Workflow Case Intake Note", "description": "Has you clarified the baseline objective, selected fields, excluded fields, assumptions, role boundary, and output expectations before testing logic?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Baseline objective framing, selected-field confirmation, excluded-field reasoning, assumption logging", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Problem framing, stakeholder roles, input-output expectation setting"}, "module_no": 1, "description": "Build the L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note by completing the L2 telemetry baseline workflow task: The senior engineer asks for a baseline anomaly workflow, but the request is still broad. The learner must clarify what anomaly means for this case, which fields are allowed, why status_code is excluded, what assumptions are acceptable, and what output format will be useful for later C++/Qt display planning. The learner must define what AI/ML can decide and what needs software, embedded, or senior engineer confirmation.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may start testing logic without clarifying allowed fields, excluded fields, output expectations, or role ownership.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Baseline objective, case intake, selected and excluded fields, assumptions, role boundary, stakeholder confirmation", "reason_behind_concept": "Clear intake prevents the learner from using undefined fields, making unsupported anomaly claims, or preparing outputs that cannot support later display planning.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use when the baseline request is broad and the learner must define what can be tested safely at L2."}, "student_confusion": "Which parts of this baseline workflow can I decide, and which parts need senior or system-team confirmation?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Baseline Case Intake", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer asks for a baseline anomaly workflow, but the request is still broad. You must clarify what anomaly means for this case, which fields are allowed, why status_code is excluded, what assumptions are acceptable, and what output format will be useful for later C++/Qt display planning. You must define what AI/ML can decide and what needs software, embedded, or senior engineer confirmation."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m2", "title": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "Spreadsheet filter/sort, model evidence checklist, basic data scan", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_st