-tel-l3-m4-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L3 Integration Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you classified integration blockers, latency risks, explainability gaps, missing interface fields, owners, and escalation needs?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Risk classification, owner mapping, blocker assessment, escalation note", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Risk severity, responsibility assignment, escalation writing"}, "module_no": 4, "description": "Build the L3 Integration Risk and Escalation Note by completing the L3 telemetry AI/ML task: The learner identifies integration risks: offline logic may exceed the 500 ms expectation, anomaly output may not explain the source signal, the display requirement may need severity labels, and missing interface fields may cause software rework. The learner must classify which risks block integration planning and who owns each resolution.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may treat every gap as an AI/ML fix or ignore risks that belong to software, embedded, test, or senior engineering.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Latency risk, missing interface fields, explainability gap, owner mapping, escalation criteria", "reason_behind_concept": "Risk classification protects teams from building on unclear outputs and directs each issue to the correct owner.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use when handoff gaps could affect software planning or near-real-time display expectations."}, "st