hat exactly will you write in the artifact so the reviewer can see your evidence?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact entry as a reviewer-ready workplace note with evidence, owner, decision, and next action. Module focus: exception handling where urgency cannot override approval evidence. Artifact evidence: Exception workflow, approval hierarchy, urgent hiring risk, duplicate-check process, escalation pathway."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1800}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI as a coach to test your clarity, missing evidence, stakeholder ownership, or risk wording. Do not ask AI to approve the requisition or invent missing values.", "module_continuity_link": "Creates the L3 Exception Readiness Sheet, which feeds the next module and preserves the evidence trail for Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-mba-hr-req-l3-m0-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-mba-hr-req-l3-m0-f1", "order": 1, "title": "Final Submission: L3 Exception Readiness Sheet", "description": "Can you complete the L3 Exception Readiness Sheet using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information?", "instructions": "Use the existing template fields for L3 Exception Readiness Sheet. Required evidence: Exception workflow, approval hierarchy, urgent hiring risk, duplicate-check process, escalation pathway. For final submission, cite the specific case evidence from this level, write the decision in workplace language, and make clear whether the item is ready, partially ready, hold/split/escalate, conditionally acceptable, audit-ready, or blocked as relevant. Use AI only for guided questions and clarity checks, not for final approval or invented details.", "accepted_file_types": ["xlsx", "docx", "pdf", "zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "Excel + PDF"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-mba-hr-req-l3-m0", "versi