d by assumption?", "follow_up": "State the HR operations concept simply and connect it to requisition approval, data quality, or governance control. Module focus: show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline. Artifact evidence: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-mba-hr-req-l3-m6-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/mba-hr-req-l3/content/c-mba-hr-req-l3-m6-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation: Evidence inspection activity for show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Exception Handling Portfolio: Which source evidence can you point to before making a requisition decision?", "follow_up": "Cite a visible document, tracker, approval note, ATS field, defect record, or audit comment rather than giving a general opinion. Module focus: show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline. Artifact evidence: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-mba-hr-req-l3-m6-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/mba-hr-req-l3/content/c-mba-hr-req-l3-m6-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation: Artifact drafting activity for show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Exception Handling Portfolio: What exactly will you write in the artifact so the reviewer can see your evidence?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact entry as a reviewer-ready workplace note with evidence, owner, decision, and next action. Module focus: show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline. Artifact evidence: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1800}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI as a coach to test your clarity, missing evidence, stakeholder ownership, or risk wording. Do not ask AI to approve the requisition or invent missing values.", "module_continuity_link": "Creates the L3 Exception Handling Portfolio, which feeds the next module and preserves the evidence trail for Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-mba-hr-req-l3-m6-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-mba-hr-req-l3-m6-f1", "order": 1, "title": "Final Submission: L3 Exception Handling Portfolio", "description": "Can you complete the L3 Exception Handling Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information?", "instructions": "Use the existing template fields for L3 Exception Handling Portfolio. Required evidence: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation. For final submission, cite the specific case evidence from this level, write the decision in workplace language, and make clear whether the item is ready, partially ready, hold/split/escalate, conditionally acceptable, audit-ready, or blocked as relevant. Use AI only for guided questions and clarity checks, not for final approval or invented details.", "accepted_file_types": ["xlsx", "docx", "pdf", "zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "ZIP + PDF"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-mba-hr-req-l3-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/mba-hr-req-l3/ART_HR_REQ_L3_M6_Portfolio_Template", "file_name": "ART_HR_REQ_L3_M6_Portfolio_Template", "file_type": "docx", "artifact_id