ess-pressure documentation, split launch action, escalation, and defensible closure communication.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "Hiring Demand to Approved Requisition Launch", "difficulty_level": "intermediate", "job_pathway_role": "MBA HR / Talent Acquisition Associate", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Readiness Sheet using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for exception handling where urgency cannot override approval evidence. Action: complete the L3 Exception Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: Exception workflow, approval hierarchy, urgent hiring risk, duplicate-check process, escalation pathway. Evidence to cite: Exception workflow, approval hierarchy, urgent hiring risk, duplicate-check process, escalation pathway. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Case Intake Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for 8 requested, 4 approved, 2 pending, 2 possible duplicate roles. Action: complete the L3 Exception Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Requested roles, approved roles, pending roles, duplicate roles, manager pressure, missing evidence, assumptions. Evidence to cite: Requested roles, approved roles, pending roles, duplicate roles, manager pressure, missing evidence, assumptions. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Evidence Validation Checklist using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for approval tracker, budget exception note, duplicate report, and owner confirmations. Action: complete the L3 Exception Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Approval status, budget status, duplicate match, owner confirmation, evidence gap, proceed/hold decision. Evidence to cite: Approval status, budget status, duplicate match, owner confirmation, evidence gap, proceed/hold decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Requisition Exception Action Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Requisition Exception Action Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for create a split decision: proceed valid roles, hold pending roles, escalate duplicates. Action: complete the L3 Requisition Exception Action Note by filling these required fields: Launchable roles, held roles, duplicate cases, escalation message, manager response, final action decision. Evidence to cite: Launchable roles, held roles, duplicate cases, escalation message, manager response, final action decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Risk and Escalation Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for approval bypass, duplicate hiring, budget exposure, manager pressure. Action: complete the L3 Exception Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, evidence, consequence, policy impact, severity, owner, escalation path. Evidence to cite: Risk ID, evidence, consequence, policy impact, severity, owner, escalation path. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Closure Report using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for give a defensible split/hold/escalate response to the regional head. Action: complete the L3 Exception Closure Report by filling these required fields: Launch decision, held items, escalation owners, rationale, evidence references, closure message. Evidence to cite: Launch decision, held items, escalation owners, rationale, evidence references, closure message. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Handling Portfolio", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Handling Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline. Action: complete the L3 Exception Handling Portfolio by filling these required fields: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision", "description": "A regional head requests urgent hiring for 8 Operations Coordinators, but the HR tracker shows only 4 approved positions. Finance approval is pending for 2 roles, and 2 roles appear to duplicate an earlier requisition opened by another manager. You receive the hiring request, approval tracker, budget exception note, duplicate requisition report, and manager escalation email asking HR to “launch now and fix approvals later.” You must diagnose the exception, separate approved from unapproved demand, identify duplication risk, document business pressure, and decide whether to proceed, hold, split, or escalate. If you launch all 8 roles without evidence, HR may create duplicate hiring, budget breach, and audit risk."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready evidence for MBA HR requisition capability: L3 Exception Readiness Sheet, L3 Exception Case Intake Note, L3 Exception Evidence Validation Checklist, L3 Requisition Exception Action Note, L3 Exception Risk and Escalation Note, L3 Exception Closure Report, L3 Exception Handling Portfolio", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "A regional head requests urgent hiring for 8 Operations Coordinators, but the HR tracker shows only 4 approved positions. Finance approval is pending for 2 roles, and 2 roles appear to duplicate an earlier requisition opened by another manager. You r