em, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for 60 records, 14 exception approvals, 9 delayed finance approvals, 7 override requests. Action: complete the L5 Governance Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Review scope, record count, exception count, audit concern, stakeholders, decision criteria. Evidence to cite: Review scope, record count, exception count, audit concern, stakeholders, decision criteria. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l5-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Governance Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L5 Governance Evidence Validation Checklist using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for launch dates, approval dates, exception types, policy status, and audit evidence. Action: complete the L5 Governance Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Requisition ID, launch date, approval date, exception type, policy status, audit evidence, validation decision. Evidence to cite: Requisition ID, launch date, approval date, exception type, policy status, audit evidence, validation decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l5-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Governance Action and Coaching Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L5 Governance Action and Coaching Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for prepare governance recommendations and manager coaching actions. Action: complete the L5 Governance Action and Coaching Note by filling these required fields: Control gap, manager behavior, coaching message, approval rule, governance control, implementation owner. Evidence to cite: Control gap, manager behavior, coaching message, approval rule, governance control, implementation owner. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l5-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for pre-approval launch, override misuse, exception control failure, weak audit trail. Action: complete the L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, audit evidence, governance consequence, severity, owner, control required, escalation decision. Evidence to cite: Risk ID, audit evidence, governance consequence, severity, owner, control required, escalation decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l5-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Governance Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L5 Governance Closure Report using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for give a leadership-ready audit-readiness or governance-risk conclusion. Action: complete the L5 Governance Closure Report by filling these required fields: Audit readiness status, evidence strength, control gaps, recommended controls, leadership message, final decision. Evidence to cite: Audit readiness status, evidence strength, control gaps, recommended controls, leadership message, final decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l5-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for show governance review, coaching plan, risk register, closure, and certification proof. Action: complete the L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio by filling these required fields: Governance review pack, evidence checklist, coaching note, risk register, closure report, certification proof. Evidence to cite: Governance review pack, evidence checklist, coaching note, risk register, closure report, certification proof. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching", "description": "The HR head is preparing for a quarterly workforce governance review. You receive 60 requisition records, 14 exception approvals, 9 delayed finance approvals, 7 manager override requests, and an audit note questioning whether HR launched roles before documented approval. You must evaluate the requisition governance process, identify whether launch decisions were evidence-backed, classify policy exceptions, create a manager coaching plan, and recommend governance controls for future requisition launches. You must decide whether the requisition process is audit-ready, conditionally acceptable with controls, or exposed to governance risk."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready evidence for MBA HR requisition capability: L5 Requisition Governance Readiness Sheet, L5 Governance Case Intake Note, L5 Governance Evidence Validation Checklist, L5 Governance Action and Coaching Note, L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note, L5 Governance Closure Report, L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "The HR head is preparing for a quarterly workforce governance review. You receive 60 requisition records, 14 exception approvals, 9 delayed finance approvals, 7 manager override requests, and an audit note questioning whether HR launched roles before documented approval. You must evaluate the requisition governance process, identify whether launch decisions were evidence-backed, classify policy exceptions, create a manager coaching plan, and recommend governance controls for future requisition launches. You must decide whether the requisition process is audit-ready, conditionally acceptable with controls, or exposed to governance risk."}]}', '{"engage": {"color": "#6366f1", "label": "Engage", "estLabel": "20-30 minutes", "purposeTag": "Workplace Risk", "description": "Understand the workplace situation, stakeholder pressure, and why requisition decisions must be evidence-backed before HR processing or ATS launch."}, "evolve": {"color": "#8b5cf6", "label": "Evolve", "estLabel": "20-30 minutes", "purposeTag": "Transfer Learning", "description": "Reflect on how the same requisition-control logic transfers to another role, department, region, hiring cycle, or governance review."}, "empower": {"color": "#14b8a6", "label": "Empower", "estLabel": "20-30 minutes", "purposeTag": "Defensible Decision", "description": "Make a ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, conditionally acceptable, or blocked decision that can be defended with evidence."}, "explain": {"color": "#f59e0b", "label": "Explain", "estLabel": "30-45 minutes", "purposeTag": "Concept / Boundary", "description": "Learn the HR operations concept, approval boundary, audit expectation, role ownership, and decision rule needed for this requisition stage."}, "explore": {"color": "#22c55e", "label": "Explore", "estLabel": "30-45 minutes", "purposeTag": "Evidence Inspection", "description": "Inspect the hiring request, approval evidence, trackers, job description, ATS fields, exception notes, audit records, and other source documents relevant to the module."}, "express": {"color": "#ec4899", "label": "Express", "estLabel": "45-60 minutes", "purposeTag": "Artifact Creation", "description": "Create the required workplace artifact using evidence, not assumptions, and write the decision or handoff clearly enough for review."}}', '2026-06-09 07:08:54.765638+00', '2026-06-09 07:08:54.765638+00', 'naresh.kumar@seaim.ac.in'), ('c37007d8-091b-4d8c-995f-3cdccb610790', '