tion Checklist. Module problem context: You validate the evidence pack and finds 3 unclear reset behaviours, 2 signal-width mismatches, 4 interface fields without valid ranges, 5 missing testbench stimulus cases, 2 clock-domain notes without ownership, and 1 incomplete memory-map section. You must decide whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, or blocked for HDL implementation review. Clarify that unclear reset behaviour, CDC ownership notes, valid-range gaps, width mismatches, missing testbench cases, and memory-map gaps are evidence-readiness findings, not final design-correctness findings."}, "student_confusion": "How do I know whether the evidence is complete, consistent, and trustworthy enough for the next engineering step?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L1 Evidence / Requirement Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You validate the evidence pack and finds 3 unclear reset behaviours, 2 signal-width mismatches, 4 interface fields without valid ranges, 5 missing testbench stimulus cases, 2 clock-domain notes without ownership, and 1 incomplete memory-map section. You must decide whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, or blocked for HDL implementation review. Clarify that unclear reset behaviour, CDC ownership notes, valid-range gaps, width mismatches, missing testbench cases, and memory-map gaps are evidence-readiness findings, not final design-correctness findings."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l1-m3", "title": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L1_M3_FPGA_Design_Readiness_Action_Template; you evidence inputs: 12-signal interface list; top-level HDL skeleton; draft testbench; memory-map note; clock/reset description; design comment log; workbook field focus: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence