 scope, reset scenarios, boundary values, waveform evidence, and what cannot be assumed from a passing or failing simulation log alone. Clarify HDL wording: the evidence pack may use either Verilog or VHDL depending on the provided module draft; you are not required to switch between both languages."}, "student_confusion": "Which parts of this request do I own as a you, and which parts must be clarified or escalated?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L2 Case Intake & Role Boundary", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer asks whether the HDL module and testbench can support simulation review. You must clarify expected behaviours, stimulus coverage, assertion scope, reset scenarios, boundary values, waveform evidence, and what cannot be assumed from a passing or failing simulation log alone. Clarify HDL wording: the evidence pack may use either Verilog or VHDL depending on the provided module draft; you are not required to switch between both languages."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l2-m2", "title": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L2_M2_Simulation_Evidence_Validation_Template; you evidence inputs: Verilog/VHDL module draft; testbench with 120 stimulus cycles; waveform screenshots; simulation log; assertion summary; workbook field focus: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "ava