next level, or another embedded FPGA case?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for moving from this level toward L3 integration readiness without overclaiming responsibility."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m2-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m2-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide for L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist: concepts, ownership boundary, and safe you decision language", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist: Which concept or boundary explains why this evidence matters?", "follow_up": "Explain the key concept in simple engineering language and connect it to simulation-validation evidence review, not final RTL correctness."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m2-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m2-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist: 8 failing assertions; 14 waveform mismatches; 3 untested reset scenarios; 2 missing boundary-value tests; 1 valid_signal timing mismatch", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist: What exact evidence should you inspect before filling this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to the exact evidence for M2: HDL module draft, testbench, 120 stimulus cycles, waveform screenshots, simulation log, assertion summary, 8 failing assertions, 14 waveform mismatches, 3 untested reset scenarios, 2 missing boundary-value tests, and valid_signal timing mismatch."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m2-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m2-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist using the full module problem and required workbook fields", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact using M2 evidence; include facts, assumptions, owner boundary, and decision evidence."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI what evidence checks are relevant for HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review, then answer only from the provided evidence pack and module inputs. A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the L2 Simulation Case Intake Note as input and produces the L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist that feeds the L2 HDL Simulation Action Note. A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m2-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m2-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist", "description": "Has you validated the actual engineering evidence for HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review using the required fields: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.?", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Has you validated the actual engineering evidence for HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review using the required fields: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you inspected actual evidence gaps and made a defensible proceed, retry, or block decision. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l2-m2", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l2/ART_L2_M2_Simulation_Evidence_Validation_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M2_Simulation_Evidence_Validation_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m2-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m2-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m2-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m2-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist", "description": "Has you validated the actual engineering evidence for HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review using the required fields: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review technical focus: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision. A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Checklist validation, evidence quality, mismatch counting, requirement trace, readiness status"}, "module_no": 2, "description": "Build the L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist by completing this L2 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: You validate the simulation evidence: a testbench with 120 stimulus cycles, waveform screenshots, a simulation log, and assertion summary. The evidence shows 8 failing assertions, 14 waveform mismatches, 3 untested reset scenarios, 2 missing boundary-value tests, and 1 unexplained valid_signal timing mismatch. You must decide whether the evidence is simulation-ready, needs correction, or is blocked. A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may treat incomplete or inconsistent evidence as review-ready even though the case contains: 8 failing assertions; 14 waveform mismatches; 3 untested reset scenarios; 2 missing boundary-value tests; 1 valid_signal timing mismatch.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "evidence completeness, consistency, mismatch/gap count, source ownership, readiness impact. Required workbook field focus: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.", "reason_behind_concept": "Validation is required because the supplied evidence includes measurable gaps and actuals that affect the safety of the next review step. A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L2 HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist. Module problem context: You validate the simulation evidence: a testbench with 120 stimulus cycles, waveform screenshots, a simulation log, and assertion summary. The evidence shows 8 failing assertions, 14 waveform mismatches, 3 untested reset scenarios, 2 missing boundary-value tests, and 1 unexplained valid_signal timing mismatch. You must decide whether the evidence is simulation-ready, needs correction, or is blocked. A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic."}, "student_confusion": "How do I know whether the evidence is complete, consistent, and trustworthy enough for the next engineering step?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L2 Evidence / Requirement Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You validate the simulation evidence: a testbench with 120 stimulus cycles, waveform screenshots, a simulation log, and assertion summary. The evidence shows 8 failing assertions, 14 waveform mismatches, 3 untested reset scenarios, 2 missing boundary-value tests, and 1 unexplained valid_signal timing mismatch. You must decide whether the evidence is simulation-ready, needs correction, or is blocked. A failing assertion or waveform mismatch is not automatically a design failure. You classify whether the issue appears linked to RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l2-m3", "title": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L2_M3_HDL_Simulation_Action_Template; you evidence inputs: Verilog/VHDL module draft; testbench with 120 stimulus cycles; waveform screenshots; simulation log; assertion summary; workbook field focus: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: defend L2 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: simulation evidence acceptable, needs testbench correction, or blocked for design review; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "L2 L2 HDL Simulation Action Note kickoff: workplace risk, role boundary, and why HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review cannot be assumed", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: What workplace risk appears in this module before you propose any action?", "follow_up": "Name the workplace risk in M3 using simulation-validation evidence review, not final RTL correctness language before suggesting any action."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: transfer this reasoning to the next embedded FPGA level or workplace case", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: How does this module prepare you for the next module, next level, or another embedded FPGA case?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for moving from this level toward L3 integration readiness without overclaiming responsibility."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: concepts, ownership boundary, and safe you decision language", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: Which concept or boundary explains why this evidence matters?", "follow_up": "Explain why each assertion or waveform mismatch is only evidence to classify, not proof of final RTL failure."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: 8 failing assertions; 14 waveform mismatches; 3 untested reset scenarios; 2 missing boundary-value tests; 1 valid_signal timing mismatch", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: What exact evidence should you inspect before filling this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to the exact evidence for M3: HDL module draft, testbench, 120 stimulus cycles, waveform screenshots, simulation log, assertion summary, 8 failing assertions, 14 waveform mismatches, 3 untested reset scenarios, 2 missing boundary-value tests, and valid_signal timing mismatch."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m3-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L2 HDL Simulation Action Note using the full module problem and required workbook fields", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 HDL Simulation Action Note: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Include assertion ID or mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected category, testbench-correction need, and escalation next step."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to review whether your action or handoff note is evidence-based, reproducible, and level-safe without asking it to create the final answer. You map each failing assertion or waveform mismatch to assertion ID or mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, recommended next step, and whether the testbench must be corrected before design review. You do not claim final RTL correctness.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the L2 Simulation Evidence Validation Checklist as input and produces the L2 HDL Simulation Action Note that feeds the L2 Simulation Risk and Escalation Note. You map each failing assertion or waveform mismatch to assertion ID or mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, recommended next step, and whether the testbench must be corrected before design review. You do not claim final RTL correctness."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m3-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m3-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 HDL Simulation Action Note", "description": "Is your action or handoff note based on visible engineering evidence, documented reasoning, and a safe L2 boundary rather than unsupported fixing or overclaiming?", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Is your action or handoff note based on visible engineering evidence, documented reasoning, and a safe L2 boundary rather than unsupported fixing or overclaiming? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you performed a concrete engineering action and made the output usable by the next stakeholder. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: You map each failing assertion or waveform mismatch to assertion ID or mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, recommended next step, and whether the testbench must be corrected before design review. You do not claim final RTL correctness. Include baseline simulation evidence category, expected versus observed behaviour, possible testbench correction, and a statement that suspicious failures are not final RTL proof.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l2-m3", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l2/ART_L2_M3_HDL_Simulation_Action_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M3_HDL_Simulation_Action_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m3-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m3-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m3-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m3-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 HDL Simulation Action Note", "description": "Is your action or handoff note based on visible engineering evidence, documented reasoning, and a safe L2 boundary rather than unsupported fixing or overclaiming?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: You map each failing assertion or waveform mismatch to assertion ID or mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, recommended next step, and whether the testbench must be corrected before design review. You do not claim final RTL correctness. Include baseline simulation evidence category, expected versus observed behaviour, possible testbench correction, and a statement that suspicious failures are not final RTL proof.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review technical focus: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision. You map ea