 performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision. Required M3 action detail: map assertion ID or waveform mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, whether you can act or must escalate, and whether testbench correction is needed before design review.", "reason_behind_concept": "A usable action or handoff note must show exactly what evidence was reviewed, what was done, and what decision is still limited. You map each failing assertion or waveform mismatch to assertion ID or mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, recommended next step, and whether the testbench must be corrected before design review. You do not claim final RTL correctness.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L2 HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L2 HDL Simulation Action Note. Module problem context: You must perform a simulation validation action by mapping each failing assertion to expected behaviour, marking waveform mismatch locations, identifying missing reset and boundary tests, and preparing a reproducible simulation action note for the FPGA review team. You map each failing assertion or waveform mismatch to assertion ID or mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, recommended next step, and whether the testbench must be corrected before design review. You do not claim final RTL correctness. Required M3 action detail: map assertion ID or waveform mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, whether you can act or must escalate, and whether testbench correction is needed before design review."}, "student_confusion": "Should I fix the issue, document it, hand it off, or escalate it based on my level boundary?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L2 Guided Work Action or Handoff", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You must perform a simulation validation action by mapping each failing assertion to expected behaviour, marking waveform mismatch locations, identifying missing reset and boundary tests, and preparing a reproducible simulation action note for the FPGA review team. You map each failing assertion or waveform mismatch to assertion ID or mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, recommended next step, and whether the testbench must be corrected before design review. You do not claim final RTL correctness. Required M3 action detail: map assertion ID or waveform mismatch ID, expected behaviour, observed behaviour, suspected evidence category, whether you can act or must escalate, and whether testbench correction is needed before design review."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l2-m4", "title": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L2_M4_Simulation_Risk_Escalation_Template; you evidence inputs: Verilog/VHDL module draft; testbench with 120 stimulus cycles; waveform screenshots; simulation log; assertion summary; workbook field focus: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m4-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m4