ublished", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Risk and Escalation Note: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact using M4 evidence; include RTL behaviour, testbench expectation, reset setup, waveform interpretation, checker alignment, or unclear expected-output logic."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to help separate blocker, risk, owner, and escalation categories, then choose severity using the visible evidence yourself. You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the L2 HDL Simulation Action Note as input and produces the L2 Simulation Risk and Escalation Note that feeds the L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report. You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m4-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m4-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Simulation Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence?", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you links evidence to consequence, severity, owner, and escalation logic. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l2-m4", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l2/ART_L2_M4_Simulation_Risk_Escalation_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M4_Simulation_Risk_Escalation_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m4-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m4-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m4-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m4-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Simulation Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review technical focus: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action. You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Risk categories, severity, escalation logic, owner mapping, next-action planning"}, "module_no": 4, "description": "Build the L2 Simulation Risk and Escalation Note by completing this L2 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: You identify simulation risks: failing assertions may indicate design or testbench errors, waveform mismatches may hide timing or logic problems, untested reset scenarios may cause unstable start-up, and missing boundary tests may leave edge-case behaviour unknown. You must classify blockers and escalation owners. You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may ignore which issues are blockers, which are manageable, and which owner must resolve them before the next engineering step.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "risk category, consequence, severity, escalation owner, recommended next action. Required workbook field focus: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action.", "reason_behind_concept": "Risk classification makes blockers and escalation ownership visible before the design, simulation, integration, timing, or validation path proceeds. You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L2 HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L2 Simulation Risk and Escalation Note. Module problem context: You identify simulation risks: failing assertions may indicate design or testbench errors, waveform mismatches may hide timing or logic problems, untested reset scenarios may cause unstable start-up, and missing boundary tests may leave edge-case behaviour unknown. You must classify blockers and escalation owners. You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan."}, "student_confusion": "Which observations are minor, which are risks, and which are blockers that need owner confirmation?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L2 Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You identify simulation risks: failing assertions may indicate design or testbench errors, waveform mismatches may hide timing or logic problems, untested reset scenarios may cause unstable start-up, and missing boundary tests may leave edge-case behaviour unknown. You must classify blockers and escalation owners. You identify missing beginner-level testbench coverage, especially reset scenarios, boundary values, and expected-output checks, without creating a full verification plan."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l2-m5", "title": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L2_M5_Simulation_Quality_Closure_Template; you evidence inputs: Verilog/VHDL module draft; testbench with 120 stimulus cycles; waveform screenshots; simulation log; assertion summary; workbook field focus: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: defend L2 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: simulation evidence acceptable, needs testbench correction, or blocked for design review; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "L2 L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report kickoff: workplace risk, role boundary, and why HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review cannot be assumed", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: What workplace risk appears in this module before you propose any action?", "follow_up": "Name the workplace risk in M5 using simulation-validation evidence review, not final RTL correctness language before suggesting any action."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: transfer this reasoning to the next embedded FPGA level or workplace case", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: How does this module prepare you for the next module, next level, or another embedded FPGA case?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for moving from this level toward L3 integration readiness without overclaiming responsibility."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: concepts, ownership boundary, and safe you decision language", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: Which concept or boundary explains why this evidence matters?", "follow_up": "Explain the key concept in simple engineering language and connect it to simulation-validation evidence review, not final RTL correctness."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: 8 failing assertions; 14 waveform mismatches; 3 untested reset scenarios; 2 missing boundary-value tests; 1 valid_signal timing mismatch", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: What exact evidence should you inspect before filling this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to the exact evidence for M5: HDL module draft, testbench, 120 stimulus cycles, waveform screenshots, simulation log, assertion summary, 8 failing assertions, 14 waveform mismatches, 3 untested reset scenarios, 2 missing boundary-value tests, and valid_signal timing mismatch."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m5-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report using the full module problem and required workbook fields", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact using M5 evidence; include facts, assumptions, owner boundary, and decision evidence."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your closure message is clear, limitation-aware, and professional for a senior engineer reviewer. The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the L2 Simulation Risk and Escalation Note as input and produces the L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report that feeds the L2 Simulation Portfolio Pack. The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m5-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m5-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final closure message clear about what was checked, what remains limited, what decision is defensible, and what the next team should do?", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Is the final closure message clear about what was checked, what remains limited, what decision is defensible, and what the next team should do? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you communicate a clear, honest closure decision without overclaiming readiness. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l2-m5", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l2/ART_L2_M5_Simulation_Quality_Closure_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M5_Simulation_Quality_Closure_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m5-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m5-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l2-m5-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l2-m5-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final closure message clear about what was checked, what remains limited, what decision is defensible, and what the next team should do?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review technical focus: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision. The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Technical closure, reviewer communication, limitation wording, confidence level, decision summary"}, "module_no": 5, "description": "Build the L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report by completing this L2 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: The senior engineer needs a simulation closure update. You must report which behaviours are validated, which failures remain, what must be corrected, and whether the HDL/testbench evidence can proceed to SoC integration planning. The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may communicate a vague or overconfident closure decision without stating evidence strength, remaining limitations, and next action.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "quality check, closure communication, confidence level, limitation language, next-step decision. Required workbook field focus: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision.", "reason_behind_concept": "Closure language helps senior engineers understand the decision without confusing partial readiness with full approval. The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L2 HDL testbench and simulation validation before design review course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L2 Simulation Quality and Closure Report. Module problem context: The senior engineer needs a simulation closure update. You must report which behaviours are validated, which failures remain, what must be corrected, and whether the HDL/testbench evidence can proceed to SoC integration planning. The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review."}, "student_confusion": "How do I communicate a technical decision clearly without overclaiming readiness or hiding limitations?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L2 Quality, Communication & Closure", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer needs a simulation closure update. You must report which behaviours are validated, which failures remain, what must be corrected, and whether the HDL/testbench evidence can proceed to SoC integration planning. The closure must communicate which failures are evidence-supported, what may be testbench or expectation related, what remains uncertain, and what must be escalated before design review."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l2-m6", "title": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L2_M6_Simulation_Portfolio_Template; you evidence inputs: Verilog/VHDL module draft; testbench with 120 stimulus cycles; waveform screenshots; simulation log; assertion summary; workbook field focus: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l2-m6-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l2/content/c-emb-fpga-l2-m6-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L2 Simulation Portfolio Pack: defend L2 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Simulation Portfolio Pack: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: simulation evidence acceptable, needs testbench correction, or blocked for design review; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "chec