ip, clarification questions. Required workbook field focus: Case request; available inputs; missing information; knowns; unknowns; assumptions; role boundary; clarification questions; intake decision.", "reason_behind_concept": "A scoped intake prevents premature technical judgement and protects you from accepting decisions owned by other engineering roles. You clarifies what AI/embedded integration evidence is available and what must be confirmed by software, FPGA, memory-interface, or senior integration owners.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L3 SoC/FPGA integration readiness across CPU, bus, memory, interrupt, and interface handoffs course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L3 Integration Case Intake Note. Module problem context: The senior engineer asks whether the design can move to FPGA SoC integration planning. You must clarify the integration target, IP block responsibilities, CPU access needs, bus-address ownership, memory-interface assumptions, interrupt routing, and interface evidence required before integration work starts. You clarifies what AI/embedded integration evidence is available and what must be confirmed by software, FPGA, memory-interface, or senior integration owners."}, "student_confusion": "Which parts of this request do I own as a you, and which parts must be clarified or escalated?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L3 Case Intake & Role Boundary", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer asks whether the design can move to FPGA SoC integration planning. You must clarify the integration target, IP block responsibilities, CPU access needs, bus-address ownership, memory-interface assumptions, interrupt routing, and interface evidence required before integration work starts. You clarifies what AI/embedded integration evidence is available and what must be confirmed by software, FPGA, memory-interface, or senior integration owners."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l3-m2", "title": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L3_M2_SoC_Evidence_Validation_Template; you evidence inputs: 4 IP blocks; ARM/NIOS CPU access note; AXI/Avalon bus table; DDR/QDR memory summary; interrupt routing notes; integration issue log; workbook field focus: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l3-m2-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l3/content/c-emb-fpga-l3-m2-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L3 SoC Evidence Validation Checklist: defend L3 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 SoC Evidence Validation Checklist: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: ready for integration planning, partially ready with handoff gaps, or blocked until interface-owner confirmation; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l3-m2-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l3/content/c-emb-fpga-l3-m2-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "L3 L3 SoC Evidence Validation Checklist kickoff: workplace risk, role boundary, and