ion, 64 percent block memory utilization, and measured throughput of 5.8 Gbps against a 6.25 Gbps target. Negative slack of WNS -0.42 ns and 23 violated timing paths block timing-confidence claims until timing-closure evidence review evidence or targeted optimization evidence is provided. You should also note the 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps throughput gap as an approximately 7.2% shortfall.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may treat incomplete or inconsistent evidence as review-ready even though the case contains: WNS -0.42 ns; 23 violated timing paths; 2 unresolved CDC warnings; 78% logic utilization; 64% block memory; 5.8 Gbps measured vs 6.25 Gbps target.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "evidence completeness, consistency, mismatch/gap count, source ownership, readiness impact. Required workbook field focus: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.", "reason_behind_concept": "Validation is required because the supplied evidence includes measurable gaps and actuals that affect the safety of the next review step. Negative slack of WNS -0.42 ns and 23 violated timing paths block timing-confidence claims until timing closure evidence or targeted optimization evidence is provided. You should also note the 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps throughput gap as an approximately 7.2% shortfall.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L4 timing-closure evidence review, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L4 Timing Evidence Validation Checklist. Module problem context: You validate the performance evidence: a post-synthesis timing report, utilization summary, CDC warning list, interface throughput note, and validation log. The report shows WNS of -0.42 ns, 23 violated paths, 2 unresolved CDC warnings, 78 percent logic utilization, 64 percent block memory utilization, and measured throughput of 5.8 Gbps against a 6.25 Gbps target. Negative slack of WNS -0.42 ns and 23 violated timing paths block timing-confidence claims until timing-closure evidence review evidence or targeted optimization evidence is provided. You should also note the 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps throughput gap as an approximately 7.2% shortfall."}, "student_confusion": "How do I know whether the evidence is complete, consistent, and trustworthy enough for the next engineering step?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L4 Evidence / Requirement Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You validate the performance evidence: a post-synthesis timing report, utilization summary, CDC warning list, interface throughput note, and validation log. The report shows WNS of -0.42 ns, 23 violated paths, 2 unresolved CDC warnings, 78 percent logic utilization, 64 percent block memory utilization, and measured throughput of 5.8 Gbps against a 6.25 Gbps target. Negative slack of WNS -0.42 ns and 23 violated timing paths block timing-confidence claims until timing-closure evidence review evidence or targeted optimization evidence is provided. You should also note the 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps throughput gap as an approximately 7.2% shortfall."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l4-m3", "title": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L4_M3_Performance_Optimization_Handoff_Template; you evidence inputs: Post-synthesis timing report; utilization summary; CDC warnings; throughput note; performance validation log; workbook field focus: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: defend L4 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: timing-confidence blocked, retest or optimization required, or escalation required before performance confidence; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "L4 L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note kickoff: workplace risk, role boundary, and why timing-closure evidence review, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control cannot be assumed", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: What workplace risk appears in this module before you propose any action?", "follow_up": "Name the workplace risk in M3 using timing-closure evidence review, not you-performed timing closure or implementation sign-off language before suggesting any action."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: transfer this reasoning to the next embedded FPGA level or workplace case", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: How does this module prepare you for the next module, next level, or another embedded FPGA case?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for moving from this level toward L5 end-to-end validation without overclaiming responsibility."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: concepts, ownership boundary, and safe you decision language", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: Which concept or boundary explains why this evidence matters?", "follow_up": "Explain the key concept in simple engineering language and connect it to timing-closure evidence review, not you-performed timing closure or implementation sign-off."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: WNS -0.42 ns; 23 violated timing paths; 2 unresolved CDC warnings; 78% logic utilization; 64% block memory; 5.8 Gbps measured vs 6.25 Gbps target", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: What exact evidence should you inspect before filling this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to the exact evidence for M3: post-synthesis timing report, WNS -0.42 ns, 23 violated paths, 2 unresolved CDC warnings, 78% logic utilization, 64% block memory utilization, and 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps throughput evidence."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m3-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note using the full module problem and required workbook fields", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Include WNS, violated paths, CDC warning status, throughput shortfall, utilization pressure, missing implementation evidence, and owner handoff."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to review whether your action or handoff note is evidence-based, reproducible, and level-safe without asking it to create the final answer. You review timing and performance evidence, groups violated paths, records WNS/TNS-style evidence where available, notes the throughput shortfall, and prepares a handoff. You do not perform final timing closure or claim implementation sign-off.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the L4 Timing Evidence Validation Checklist as input and produces the L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note that feeds the L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note. You review timing and performance evidence, groups violated paths, records WNS/TNS-style evidence where available, notes the throughput shortfall, and prepares a handoff. You do not perform final timing closure or claim implementation sign-off."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l4-m3-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l4-m3-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note", "description": "Is your action or handoff note based on visible engineering evidence, documented reasoning, and a safe L4 boundary rather than unsupported fixing or overclaiming? You review timing-closure evidence and performance risk; they do not perform timing closure or claim implementation sign-off.", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Is your action or handoff note based on visible engineering evidence, documented reasoning, and a safe L4 boundary rather than unsupported fixing or overclaiming? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you performed a concrete engineering action and made the output usable by the next stakeholder. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L4 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: You review timing and performance evidence, groups violated paths, records WNS/TNS-style evidence where available, notes the throughput shortfall, and prepares a handoff. You do not perform final timing closure or claim implementation sign-off.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l4-m3", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l4/ART_L4_M3_Performance_Optimization_Handoff_Template", "file_name": "ART_L4_M3_Performance_Optimization_Handoff_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l4-m3-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l4-m3-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "al