claim implementation sign-off.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Engineering handoff writing, action notes, reproducibility, human-first reasoning, decision logging"}, "module_no": 3, "description": "Build the L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note by completing this L4 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: You must prepare a performance optimization handoff by grouping violated timing paths, identifying likely causes, marking CDC warnings, comparing throughput target versus result, documenting utilization pressure, and recommending whether to optimize, retest, or block. You review timing and performance evidence, groups violated paths, records WNS/TNS-style evidence where available, notes the throughput shortfall, and prepares a handoff. You do not perform final timing-closure evidence review or claim implementation sign-off.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may create the L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note as a generic note instead of making a concrete evidence-based action or handoff that another engineer can use.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "evidence-based action, handoff logic, human-first reasoning, level-safe engineering decision. Required workbook field focus: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision.", "reason_behind_concept": "A usable action or handoff note must show exactly what evidence was reviewed, what was done, and what decision is still limited. You review timing and performance evidence, groups violated paths, records WNS/TNS-style evidence where available, notes the throughput shortfall, and prepares a handoff. You do not perform final timing closure or claim implementation sign-off.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L4 timing-closure evidence review, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note. Module problem context: You must prepare a performance optimization handoff by grouping violated timing paths, identifying likely causes, marking CDC warnings, comparing throughput target versus result, documenting utilization pressure, and recommending whether to optimize, retest, or block. You review timing and performance evidence, groups violated paths, records WNS/TNS-style evidence where available, notes the throughput shortfall, and prepares a handoff. You do not perform final timing-closure evidence review or claim implementation sign-off."}, "student_confusion": "Should I fix the issue, document it, hand it off, or escalate it based on my level boundary?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L4 Guided Work Action or Handoff", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You must prepare a performance optimization handoff by grouping violated timing paths, identifying likely causes, marking CDC warnings, comparing throughput target versus result, documenting utilization pressure, and recommending whether to optimize, retest, or block. You review timing and performance evidence, groups violated paths, records WNS/TNS-style evidence where available, notes the throughput shortfall, and prepares a handoff. You do not perform final timing-closure evidence review or claim implementation sign-off."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l4-m4", "title": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L4_M4_Timing_Risk_Escalation_Template; you evidence inputs: Post-synthesis timing report; utilization summary; CDC warnings; throughput note; performance validation log; workbook field focus: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started",