0.42 ns, 23 violated paths, 2 unresolved CDC warnings, 78% logic utilization, 64% block memory utilization, and 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps throughput evidence."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m4-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m4-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note using the full module problem and required workbook fields", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact using M4 evidence; include negative slack, violated paths, unresolved CDC, throughput shortfall, utilization pressure, and missing place-and-route evidence."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to help separate blocker, risk, owner, and escalation categories, then choose severity using the visible evidence yourself. Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the L4 Performance Optimization Handoff Note as input and produces the L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note that feeds the L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report. Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l4-m4-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l4-m4-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence? You review timing-closure evidence and performance risk; they do not perform timing closure or claim implementation sign-off.", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you links evidence to consequence, severity, owner, and escalation logic. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L4 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l4-m4", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l4/ART_L4_M4_Timing_Risk_Escalation_Template", "file_name": "ART_L4_M4_Timing_Risk_Escalation_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l4-m4-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l4-m4-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l4-m4-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l4-m4-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence? You review timing-closure evidence and performance risk; they do not perform timing closure or claim implementation sign-off.", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "timing-closure evidence review, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control technical focus: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action. Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Risk categories, severity, escalation logic, owner mapping, next-action planning"}, "module_no": 4, "description": "Build the L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note by completing this L4 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: You identify timing and performance risks: negative slack may cause unreliable operation, CDC warnings may produce intermittent failures, high utilization may limit routing closure, and throughput shortfall may violate interface expectation. You must classify risks by severity and ownership. Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may ignore which issues are blockers, which are manageable, and which owner must resolve them before the next engineering step.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "risk category, consequence, severity, escalation owner, recommended next action. Required workbook field focus: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action.", "reason_behind_concept": "Risk classification makes blockers and escalation ownership visible before the design, simulation, integration, timing, or validation path proceeds. Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L4 timing-closure evidence review, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note. Module problem context: You identify timing and performance risks: negative slack may cause unreliable operation, CDC warnings may produce intermittent failures, high utilization may limit routing closure, and throughput shortfall may violate interface expectation. You must classify risks by severity and ownership. Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk."}, "student_confusion": "Which observations are minor, which are risks, and which are blockers that need owner confirmation?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L4 Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You identify timing and performance risks: negative slack may cause unreliable operation, CDC warnings may produce intermittent failures, high utilization may limit routing closure, and throughput shortfall may violate interface expectation. You must classify risks by severity and ownership. Unresolved CDC warnings are escalation-level risks unless the clock-domain owner provides justification, waiver, or synchronization evidence. Utilization is a pressure signal, not a blocker by itself, unless linked to timing failure, routing congestion, or future expansion risk."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l4-m5", "title": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L4_M5_Performance_Quality_Closure_Template; you evidence inputs: Post-synthesis timing report; utilization summary; CDC warnings; throughput note; performance validation log; workbook field focus: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: defend L4 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: timing-confidence blocked, retest or optimization required, or escalation required before performance confidence; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "L4 L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report kickoff: workplace risk, role boundary, and why timing-closure evidence review, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control cannot be assumed", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: What workplace risk appears in this module before you propose any action?", "follow_up": "Name the workplace risk in M5 using timing-closure evidence review, not you-performed timing closure or implementation sign-off language before suggesting any action."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: transfer this reasoning to the next embedded FPGA level or workplace case", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: How does this module prepare you for the next module, next level, or another embedded FPGA case?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for moving from this level toward L5 end-to-end validation without overclaiming responsibility."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: concepts, ownership boundary, and safe you decision language", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: Which concept or boundary explains why this evidence matters?", "follow_up": "Explain the key concept in simple engineering language and connect it to timing-closure evidence review, not you-performed timing closure or implementation sign-off."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: WNS -0.42 ns; 23 violated timing paths; 2 unresolved CDC warnings; 78% logic utilization; 64% block memory; 5.8 Gbps measured vs 6.25 Gbps target", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: What exact evidence should you inspect before filling this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to the exact evidence for M5: post-synthesis timing report, WNS -0.42 ns, 23 violated paths, 2 unresolved CDC warnings, 78% logic utilization, 64% block memory utilization, and 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps throughput evidence."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l4/content/c-emb-fpga-l4-m5-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report using the full module problem and required workbook fields", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact using M5 evidence; include facts, assumptions, owner boundary, and decision evidence."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your closure message is clear, limitation-aware, and professional for a senior engineer reviewer. The closure must clearly state that WNS -0.42 ns, 23 violated paths, unresolved CDC warnings, and 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps performance prevent performance-confidence claims unless retest, optimization, owner waiver, or place-and-route evidence is supplied.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the L4 Timing Risk and Escalation Note as input and produces the L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report that feeds the L4 Timing Portfolio Pack. The closure must clearly state that WNS -0.42 ns, 23 violated paths, unresolved CDC warnings, and 5.8 Gbps vs 6.25 Gbps performance prevent performance-confidence claims unless retest, optimization, owner waiver, or place-and-route evidence is supplied."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l4-m5-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l4-m5-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L4 Performance Quality and Closure Report", "