ted evidence-based capability proof for timing closure, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you connects all artifacts into a coherent capability proof. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L4 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: The final portfolio must prove timing/performance risk-review capability, not timing-closure execution. It should transfer unresolved evidence to L5 end-to-end validation with clear blockers and owner actions.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l4-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l4/ART_L4_M6_Timing_Portfolio_Template", "file_name": "ART_L4_M6_Timing_Portfolio_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l4-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l4-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l4-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l4-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L4 Timing Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace your final decision through all prior artifacts and see a connected evidence-based capability proof for timing closure, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control? You review timing-closure evidence and performance risk; they do not perform timing closure or claim implementation sign-off.", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: The final portfolio must prove timing/performance risk-review capability, not timing-closure execution. It should transfer unresolved evidence to L5 end-to-end validation with clear blockers and owner actions.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "timing-closure evidence review, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control technical focus: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation. The final portfolio must prove timing/performance risk-review capability, not timing-closure execution. It should transfer unresolved evidence to L5 end-to-end validation with clear blockers and owner actions.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Portfolio structure, artifact continuity, evidence mapping, self-review, transfer reflection"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the L4 Timing Portfolio Pack by completing this L4 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: The reviewer must see a complete timing/performance evidence chain. You must compile readiness, intake, evidence validation, optimization handoff, risk, closure, and final timing portfolio. The final portfolio must prove timing/performance risk-review capability, not timing-closure execution. It should transfer unresolved evidence to L5 end-to-end validation with clear blockers and owner actions.", "estimatedTime": "4 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may submit separate worksheets without proving a connected artifact chain, decision trail, and transfer readiness for the next level.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "artifact chain, evidence map, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Required workbook field focus: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation.", "reason_behind_concept": "Portfolio validation proves capability maturity by connecting every artifact into one evidence-backed decision trail. The final portfolio must prove timing/performance risk-review capability, not timing-closure execution. It should transfer unresolved evidence to L5 end-to-end validation with clear blockers and owner actions.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L4 timing-closure evidence review, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L4 Timing Portfolio Pack. Module problem context: The reviewer must see a complete timing/performance evidence chain. You must compile readiness, intake, evidence validation, optimization handoff, risk, closure, and final timing portfolio. The final portfolio must prove timing/performance risk-review capability, not timing-closure execution. It should transfer unresolved evidence to L5 end-to-end validation with clear blockers and owner actions."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that my final decision came from a connected evidence trail rather than isolated tasks?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L4 Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The reviewer must see a complete timing/performance evidence chain. You must compile readiness, intake, evidence validation, optimization handoff, risk, closure, and final timing portfolio. The final portfolio must prove timing/performance risk-review capability, not timing-closure execution. It should transfer unresolved evidence to L5 end-to-end validation with clear blockers and owner actions."}], "duration": "20 hours", "course_id": "crs-emb-fpga-l4", "xp_reward": 1100, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "Embedded design engineers need timing closure, performance validation, utilization, CDC, and interface reliability control because workplace review decisions depend on visible evidence, not assumptions or unverified implementation confidence. This L4 course is a timing-closure evidence review and performance-risk review, not a course where you performs timing closure. Negative slack, violated paths, unresolved CDC warnings, and throughput shortfall must be treated as evidence requiring review, retest, optimization handoff, or escalation.", "course_code": "EMB-FPGA-L4", "description": "You can evaluate timing/performance evidence, identify timing closure blockers, validate interface reliability signals, and communicate optimization or escalation decisions. This L4 course is a timing-closure evidence review and performance-risk review, not a course where you review timing-closure evidence. Negative slack, violated paths, unresolved CDC warnings, and throughput shortfall must be treated as evidence requiring review, retest, optimization handoff, or escalation.", "domain_name": "Embedded Systems / FPGA Design", "level_label": "L4", "sequence_no": 4, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "Learners build capability by completing seven connected artifacts using the full case evidence, required workbook fields, role boundaries, risk/escalation language, and human-first engineering judgement. This L4 course is a timing-closure evidence review and performance-risk review, not a course where you performs timing closure. Negative slack, violated paths, unresolved CDC warnings, and throughput shortfall must be treated as evidence requiring review, retest, optimization handoff, or escalation.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "Timing Closure and Performance Validation", "difficulty_level": "advanced", "job_pathway_role": "Embedded Design Engineer", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l4-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Timing Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you explain the L4 embedded FPGA work context, role boundary, evidence pack, and readiness decision before acting on the case? Input: use the full L4 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: Timing and performance evidence pack. Evidence given to you: Post-synthesis timing report; utilization summary; CDC warnings; throughput note; performance validation log. Evidence issues / actuals: WNS -0.42 ns; 23 violated timing paths; 2 unresolved CDC warnings; 78% logic utilization; 64% block memory; 5.8 Gbps measured vs 6.25 Gbps target. You decision required: Continue optimization / retest / blocked for timing closure. Action: complete the L4 Timing Readiness Sheet by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Level purpose; system/workflow context; evidence pack components; you responsibility; non-owned dependencies; readiness gaps; readiness decision. Evidence to cite: L4 timing/performance evidence-review purpose, post-synthesis timing report, utilization summary, CDC warning list, throughput note, role boundary, and timing-closure evidence limitation. Output decision: Continue optimization / retest / blocked for timing closure. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you understands the work context before acting and can separate their own role from other engineering owners. Restriction: stay inside L4 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: Frame the work as timing-closure evidence review and timing-readiness review. You can group violations, identify blockers, and prepare an optimization handoff, but should not be expected to close timing. You performs timing-closure evidence review, not timing closure. Negative slack and violated paths block timing-confidence claims until timing closure or targeted optimization evidence is provided. Unresolved CDC warnings require owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status. Throughput shortfall is about 7.2%. Utilization is a pressure signal unless linked to timing, routing, or expansion risk.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l4-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Timing Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has you converted the senior engineer request into a scoped case intake by separating facts, assumptions, unknowns, role ownership, and clarification questions? Input: use the full L4 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: Timing and performance evidence pack. Evidence given to you: Post-synthesis timing report; utilization summary; CDC warnings; throughput note; performance validation log. Evidence issues / actuals: WNS -0.42 ns; 23 violated timing paths; 2 unresolved CDC warnings; 78% logic utilization; 64% block memory; 5.8 Gbps measured vs 6.25 Gbps target. You decision required: Continue optimization / retest / blocked for timing closure. Action: complete the L4 Timing Case Intake Note by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Case request; available inputs; missing information; knowns; unknowns; assumptions; role boundary; clarification questions; intake decision. Evidence to cite: review request, available timing/performance evidence, missing implementation or place-and-route evidence, owner questions, assumptions, and timing-confidence limitation. Output decision: Continue optimization / retest / blocked for timing closure. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you converted a vague workplace request into a scoped technical case with clear assumptions and questions. Restriction: stay inside L4 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: Clarify that post-synthesis timing evidence indicates timing risk; final timing confidence requires implementation or place-and-route timing evidence and owner confirmation. You performs timing-closure evidence review, not timing closure. Negative slack and violated paths block timing-confidence claims until timing closure or targeted optimization evidence is provided. Unresolved CDC warnings require owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status. Throughput shortfall is about 7.2%. Utilization is a pressure signal unless linked to timing, routing, or expansion risk.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l4-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Timing Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has you validated the actual engineering evidence for timing closure, 