tion_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m2-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m2-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m2-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L5 Solution Evidence Validation Checklist", "description": "Has you validated the actual engineering evidence for end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof using the required fields: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.? You validate supervised prototype decision-support readiness only, not production release.", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: You check whether L1 evidence gaps, L2 simulation corrections, L3 integration risks, L4 timing/CDC findings, and L5 governance decisions are consistent or contradictory before recommending supervised prototype use.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof technical focus: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision. You check whether L1 evidence gaps, L2 simulation corrections, L3 integration risks, L4 timing/CDC findings, and L5 governance decisions are consistent or contradictory before recommending supervised prototype use. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Checklist validation, evidence quality, mismatch counting, requirement trace, readiness status"}, "module_no": 2, "description": "Build the L5 Solution Evidence Validation Checklist by completing this L5 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: You validate the full evidence chain: interface list, HDL skeleton, simulation logs, corrected assertions, SoC integration map, AXI/Avalon bus table, DDR/QDR notes, timing reports, throughput validation, interface documents, and 11 risks. Two risks remain unresolved: incomplete valid-range metadata and one CDC warning. You must decide whether evidence supports prototype validation. You check whether L1 evidence gaps, L2 simulation corrections, L3 integration risks, L4 timing/CDC findings, and L5 governance decisions are consistent or contradictory before recommending supervised prototype use. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may treat incomplete or inconsistent evidence as review-ready even though the case contains: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "evidence completeness, consistency, mismatch/gap count, source ownership, readiness impact. Required workbook field focus: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "reason_behind_concept": "Validation is required because the supplied evidence includes measurable gaps and actuals that affect the safety of the next review step. You check whether L1 evidence gaps, L2 simulation corrections, L3 integration risks, L4 timing/CDC findings, and L5 governance decisions are consistent or contradictory before recommending supervised prototype use.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L5 end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L5 Solution Evidence Validation Checklist. Module problem context: You validate the full evidence chain: interface list, HDL skeleton, simulation logs, corrected assertions, SoC integration map, AXI/Avalon bus table, DDR/QDR notes, timing reports, throughput validation, interface documents, and 11 risks. Two risks remain unresolved: incomplete valid-range metadata and one CDC warning. You must decide whether evidence supports prototype validation. You check whether L1 evidence gaps, L2 simulation corrections, L3 integration risks, L4 timing/CDC findings, and L5 governance decisions are consistent or contradictory before recommending supervised prototype use. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use."}, "student_confusion": "How do I know whether the evidence is complete, consistent, and trustworthy enough for the next engineering step?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L5 Evidence / Requirement Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You validate the full evidence chain: interface list, HDL skeleton, simulation logs, corrected assertions, SoC integration map, AXI/Avalon bus table, DDR/QDR notes, timing reports, throughput validation, interface documents, and 11 risks. Two risks remain unresolved: incomplete valid-range metadata and one CDC warning. You must decide whether evidence supports prototype validation. You check whether L1 evidence gaps, L2 simulation corrections, L3 integration risks, L4 timing/CDC findings, and L5 governance decisions are consistent or contradictory before recommending supervised prototype use. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l5-m3", "title": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L5_M3_Design_Validation_Template; you evidence inputs: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register; workbook field focus: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m3-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m3-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L5 Design Validation Note: defend L5 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Design Validation Note: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: supervised prototype validation only, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m3-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m3-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "L5 L5 Design Validation Note kickoff: workplace risk, role boundary, and why end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof cannot be assumed", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Design Validation Note: What workplace risk appears in this module before you propose any action?", "follow_up": "Name the workplace risk in M3 using supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval language before suggesting any action."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m3-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m3-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection for L5 Design Validation Note: transfer this reasoning to the next embedded FPGA level or workplace case", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Design Validation Note: How does this module prepare you for the next module, next level, or another embedded FPGA case?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for moving from this level toward workplace transfer and certification proof without overclaiming responsibility."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m3-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m3-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide for L5 Design Validation Note: concepts, ownership boundary, and safe you decision language", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitat