imits, and what must not be automated.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l5-m3", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l5/ART_L5_M3_Design_Validation_Template", "file_name": "ART_L5_M3_Design_Validation_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m3-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m3-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m3-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m3-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L5 Design Validation Note", "description": "Is your action or handoff note based on visible engineering evidence, documented reasoning, and a safe L5 boundary rather than unsupported fixing or overclaiming? You validate supervised prototype decision-support readiness only, not production release.", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: The decision-support validation note must define safe-use conditions, human review requirements, prohibited uses, evidence limits, and what must not be automated.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "end-to-end embedded FPGA