"Uses the L5 Design Validation Note as input and produces the L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note that feeds the L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report. Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m4-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m4-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence? You validate supervised prototype decision-support readiness only, not production release.", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you links evidence to consequence, severity, owner, and escalation logic. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L5 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l5-m4", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l5/ART_L5_M4_Governance_Risk_Escalation_Template", "file_name": "ART_L5_M4_Governance_Risk_Escalation_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m4-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m4-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m4-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m4-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence? You validate supervised prototype decision-support readiness only, not production release.", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof technical focus: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action. Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Risk categories, severity, escalation logic, owner mapping, next-action planning"}, "module_no": 4, "description": "Build the L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note by completing this L5 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: You review final governance risks: incomplete metadata may affect validation confidence, an unresolved CDC warning may affect reliability, and documentation gaps may weaken review traceability. You must decide which risks block prototype validation and which can proceed under controls. Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may ignore which issues are blockers, which are manageable, and which owner must resolve them before the next engineering step.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "risk category, consequence, severity, escalation owner, recommended next action. Required workbook field focus: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "reason_behind_concept": "Risk classification makes blockers and escalation ownership visible before the design, simulation, integration, timing, or validation path proceeds. Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L5 end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note. Module problem context: You review final governance risks: incomplete metadata may affect validation confidence, an unresolved CDC warning may affect reliability, and documentation gaps may weaken review traceability. You must decide which risks block prototype validation and which can proceed under controls. Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use."}, "student_confusion": "Which observations are minor, which are risks, and which are blockers that need owner confirmation?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L5 Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You review final governance risks: incomplete metadata may affect validation confidence, an unresolved CDC warning may affect reliability, and documentation gaps may weaken review traceability. You must decide which risks block prototype validation and which can proceed under controls. Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l5-m5", "title": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L5_M5_Final_Solution_Quality_Closure_Template; you evidence inputs: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register; workbook field focus: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: defend L5 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: supervised prototype validation only, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "L5 L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report kickoff: workplace risk, role boundary, and why end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof cannot be assumed", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: What workplace risk appears in this module before you propose any action?", "follow_up": "Name the workplace risk in M5 using supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval language before suggesting any action."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: transfer this reasoning to the next embedded FPGA level or workplace case", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: How does this module prepare you for the next module, next level, or another embedded FPGA case?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for moving from this level toward workplace transfer and certification proof without overclaiming responsibility."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: concepts, ownership boundary, and safe you decision language", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: Which concept or boundary explains why this evidence matters?", "follow_up": "Explain the key concept in simple engineering language and connect it to supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: What exact evidence should you inspect before filling this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to the exact evidence for M5: L1-L4 evidence chain, interface docs, simulation corrections, integration map, timing reports, throughput validation, 11-risk register, incomplete valid-range metadata, and unresolved CDC warning."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m5-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report using the full module problem and required workbook fields", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact using M5 evidence; include facts, assumptions, owner boundary, and decision evidence."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your closure message is clear, limitation-aware, and professional for a senior engineer reviewer. The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note as input and produces the L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report that feeds the L5 Certification Portfolio Pack. The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m5-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m5-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final closure message clear about what was checked, what remains limited, what decision is defensible, and what the next team should do? You validate supervised prototype decision-support readiness only, not production release.", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Is the final closure message clear about what was checked, what remains limited, what decision is defensible, and what the next team should do? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you communicate a clear, honest closure decision without overclaiming readiness. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L5 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l5-m5", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l5/ART_L5_M5_Final_Solution_Quality_Closure_Template", "file_name": "ART_L5_M5_Final_Solution_Quality_Closure_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m5-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m5-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m5-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m5-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final closure message clear about what was checked, what remains limited, what decision is defensible, and what the next team should do? You validate supervised prototype decision-support readiness only, not production release.", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof technical focus: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision. The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Technical closure, reviewer communication, limitation wording, confidence level, decision summary"}, "module_no": 5, "description": "Build the L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report by completing this L5 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: The stakeholder needs a final recommendation. You must communicate evidence strength, unresolved limitations, required controls, human review needs, and whether the workflow is ready for supervised prototype validation, further controlled testing, or blocked. The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may communicate a vague or overconfident closure decision without stating evidence strength, remaining limitations, and next action.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "quality check, closure communication, confidence level, limitation language, next-step decision. Required workbook field focus: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "reason_behind_concept": "Closure language helps senior engineers understand the decision without confusing partial readiness with full approval. The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L5 end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report. Module problem context: The stakeholder needs a final recommendation. You must communicate evidence strength, unresolved limitations, required controls, human review needs, and whether the workflow is ready for supervised prototype validation, further controlled testing, or blocked. The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use."}, "student_confusion": "How do I communicate a technical decision clearly without overclaiming readiness or hiding limitations?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L5 Quality, Communication & Closure", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The stakeholder needs a final recommendation. You must communicate evidence strength, unresolved limitations, required controls, human review needs, and whether the workflow is ready for supervised prototype validation, further controlled testing, or blocked. The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use."}, {"id": "mod-emb-fpga-l5-m6", "title": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "ART_L5_M6_Certification_Portfolio_Template; you evidence inputs: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register; workbook field focus: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation.", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "template + evidence pack"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m6-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m6-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check for L5 Certification Portfolio Pack: defend L5 readiness using visible evidence and limitations", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Certification Portfolio Pack: What decision can you defend from the evidence at this stage?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence: supervised prototype validation only, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use; do not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "