up": "Explain the key concept in simple engineering language and connect it to supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m6-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m6-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for L5 Certification Portfolio Pack: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Certification Portfolio Pack: What exact evidence should you inspect before filling this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to the exact evidence for M6: L1-L4 evidence chain, interface docs, simulation corrections, integration map, timing reports, throughput validation, 11-risk register, incomplete valid-range metadata, and unresolved CDC warning."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-emb-fpga-l5-m6-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/emb-fpga-l5/content/c-emb-fpga-l5-m6-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L5 Certification Portfolio Pack using the full module problem and required workbook fields", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Certification Portfolio Pack: What will you write in the artifact so a reviewer can verify your work?", "follow_up": "Write the artifact using M6 evidence; include facts, assumptions, owner boundary, and decision evidence."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your portfolio shows a connected evidence trail, missing-risk visibility, and transfer readiness across modules. The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses all previous artifacts to create final portfolio proof and transfer learning for the next level or workplace review. The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m6-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m6-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L5 Certification Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace your final decision through all prior artifacts and see a connected evidence-based capability proof for end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof? You validate supervised prototype decision-support readiness only, not production release.", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering the workplace artifact question: Can a reviewer trace your final decision through all prior artifacts and see a connected evidence-based capability proof for end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof? Fill the required workbook fields fully: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation. Reviewer expectation: Checks whether you connects all artifacts into a coherent capability proof. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L5 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness. Do not use AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks. Level-specific review correction: The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-emb-fpga-l5-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/emb-fpga-l5/ART_L5_M6_Certification_Portfolio_Template", "file_name": "ART_L5_M6_Certification_Portfolio_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-emb-fpga-l5-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-emb-fpga-l5-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L5 Certification Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace your final decision through all prior artifacts and see a connected evidence-based capability proof for end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof? You validate supervised prototype decision-support readiness only, not production release.", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the full module problem and required fields: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation.. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks. Level-specific review correction: The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof technical focus: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation. The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Portfolio structure, artifact continuity, evidence mapping, self-review, transfer reflection"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the L5 Certification Portfolio Pack by completing this L5 Embedded Design Engineer task without truncating the case context: The reviewer needs certification-level proof. You must compile all L1 to L5 artifacts into a final portfolio that proves end-to-end embedded FPGA design validation capability. The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "estimatedTime": "4 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may submit separate worksheets without proving a connected artifact chain, decision trail, and transfer readiness for the next level.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "artifact chain, evidence map, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Required workbook field focus: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use.", "reason_behind_concept": "Portfolio validation proves capability maturity by connecting every artifact into one evidence-backed decision trail. The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module inside the L5 end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof course when you must turn the supplied case evidence into the artifact: L5 Certification Portfolio Pack. Module problem context: The reviewer needs certification-level proof. You must compile all L1 to L5 artifacts into a final portfolio that proves end-to-end embedded FPGA design validation capability. The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that my final decision came from a connected evidence trail rather than isolated tasks?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "L5 Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The reviewer needs certification-level proof. You must compile all L1 to L5 artifacts into a final portfolio that proves end-to-end embedded FPGA design validation capability. The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation. Use supervised prototype validation language only; do not imply production release, autonomous approval, or unattended use."}], "duration": "24 hours", "course_id": "crs-emb-fpga-l5", "xp_reward": 1300, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "Embedded design engineers need end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof because workplace review decisions depend on visible evidence, not assumptions or unverified implementation confidence. This L5 capstone is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. You evaluates governance, unresolved risks, evidence consistency, and final decision-support readiness.", "course_code": "EMB-FPGA-L5", "description": "You can evaluate an end-to-end embedded FPGA design evidence chain across design readiness, simulation, integration, timing, risk, documentation, and final stakeholder decision readiness. This L5 capstone is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. You evaluates governance, unresolved risks, evidence consistency, and final decision-support readiness.", "domain_name": "Embedded Systems / FPGA Design", "level_label": "L5", "sequence_no": 5, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "Learners build capability by completing seven connected artifacts using the full case evidence, required workbook fields, role boundaries, risk/escalation language, and human-first engineering judgement. This L5 capstone is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. You evaluates governance, unresolved risks, evidence consistency, and final decision-support readiness.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1518770660439-4636190af475?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "End-to-End Embedded FPGA Design Validation", "difficulty_level": "certification-ready advanced", "job_pathway_role": "Embedded Design Engineer", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l5-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Solution Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you explain the L5 embedded FPGA work context, role boundary, evidence pack, and readiness decision before acting on the case? Input: use the full L5 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: End-to-end validation evidence pack. Evidence given to you: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register. Evidence issues / actuals: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path. You decision required: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Action: complete the L5 Solution Readiness Sheet by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Level purpose; system/workflow context; evidence pack components; you responsibility; non-owned dependencies; readiness gaps; readiness decision. Evidence to cite: full L1-L4 evidence chain, interface docs, simulation corrections, integration map, timing reports, throughput validation, risk register, role boundary, and supervised-prototype limitation. Output decision: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you understands the work context before acting and can separate their own role from other engineering owners. Restriction: stay inside L5 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: Make the capstone boundary explicit: the final recommendation may support supervised prototype validation or controlled testing, but not production release or autonomous system approval. Final decision language is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. Unresolved risks must be classified as acceptable with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l5-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 End-to-End Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has you converted the senior engineer request into a scoped case intake by separating facts, assumptions, unknowns, role ownership, and clarification questions? Input: use the full L5 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: End-to-end validation evidence pack. Evidence given to you: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register. Evidence issues / actuals: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path. You decision required: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Action: complete the L5 End-to-End Case Intake Note by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Case request; available inputs; missing information; knowns; unknowns; assumptions; role boundary; clarification questions; intake decision. Evidence to cite: stakeholder request, decision-support objective, expected users, autonomy boundary, available L1-L4 evidence, unresolved risks, and clarification questions. Output decision: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you converted a vague workplace request into a scoped technical case with clear assumptions and questions. Restriction: stay inside L5 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: Clarify decision-support meaning, expected users, human-review requirement, prohibited autonomy, available L1-L4 evidence, unresolved risks, and final recommendation format. Final decision language is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. Unresolved risks must be classified as acceptable with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l5-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Solution Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has you validated the actual engineering evidence for end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof using the required fields: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision.? Input: use the full L5 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: End-to-end validation evidence pack. Evidence given to you: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register. Evidence issues / actuals: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path. You decision required: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Action: complete the L5 Solution Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Evidence item; source/owner; completeness check; consistency check; mismatch/gap count; impact on design or validation; readiness decision. Evidence to cite: L1 evidence gaps, L2 simulation corrections, L3 integration risks, L4 timing/CDC findings, risk-register status, unresolved field metadata, unresolved CDC warning, and any contradictions across the evidence chain. Output decision: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you inspected actual evidence gaps and made a defensible proceed, retry, or block decision. Restriction: stay inside L5 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: You check whether L1 evidence gaps, L2 simulation corrections, L3 integration risks, L4 timing/CDC findings, and L5 governance decisions are consistent or contradictory before recommending supervised prototype use. Final decision language is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. Unresolved risks must be classified as acceptable with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l5-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Design Validation Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is your action or handoff note based on visible engineering evidence, documented reasoning, and a safe L5 boundary rather than unsupported fixing or overclaiming? Input: use the full L5 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: End-to-end validation evidence pack. Evidence given to you: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register. Evidence issues / actuals: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path. You decision required: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Action: complete the L5 Design Validation Note by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Evidence reviewed; action performed; issue counts or observations; human-first reasoning; engineering impact; handoff message; final action decision. Evidence to cite: evidence chain summary, safe-use conditions, human-review requirement, prohibited uses, unresolved risk controls, stakeholder handoff, and final recommendation. Output decision: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you performed a concrete engineering action and made the output usable by the next stakeholder. Restriction: stay inside L5 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: The decision-support validation note must define safe-use conditions, human review requirements, prohibited uses, evidence limits, and what must not be automated. Final decision language is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. Unresolved risks must be classified as acceptable with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l5-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has you identified blockers, risks, ownership gaps, severity, escalation reason, and next action using module evidence? Input: use the full L5 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: End-to-end validation evidence pack. Evidence given to you: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register. Evidence issues / actuals: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path. You decision required: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Action: complete the L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Risk ID; risk category; observed evidence; consequence; severity; owner; escalation reason; recommended next action. Evidence to cite: incomplete valid-range metadata, unresolved CDC warning affecting one low-frequency status path, owner confirmation or waiver needs, governance category, control required, and release/prototype classification. Output decision: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you links evidence to consequence, severity, owner, and escalation logic. Restriction: stay inside L5 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: Classify each unresolved risk as acceptable for supervised prototype with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production. The unresolved CDC warning requires owner confirmation, waiver justification, synchronization evidence, or blocker status. Final decision language is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. Unresolved risks must be classified as acceptable with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l5-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the final closure message clear about what was checked, what remains limited, what decision is defensible, and what the next team should do? Input: use the full L5 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: End-to-end validation evidence pack. Evidence given to you: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register. Evidence issues / actuals: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path. You decision required: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Action: complete the L5 Final Solution Quality and Closure Report by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Work completed; evidence used; checks passed; checks failed; open issues; closure message; confidence level; closure decision. Evidence to cite: final readiness recommendation, limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, supervised-prototype-only language, stakeholder message, and closure confidence. Output decision: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you communicate a clear, honest closure decision without overclaiming readiness. Restriction: stay inside L5 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: The closure must state supervised prototype validation only, remaining limitations, governance controls, human-review requirement, and why the workflow is not approved for autonomous or production release. Final decision language is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. Unresolved risks must be classified as acceptable with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-emb-fpga-l5-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Certification Portfolio Pack", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can a reviewer trace your final decision through all prior artifacts and see a connected evidence-based capability proof for end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof? Input: use the full L5 course problem statement, the module-specific problem statement, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this level evidence: Evidence pack: End-to-end validation evidence pack. Evidence given to you: L1-L4 evidence chain; interface docs; simulation corrections; integration map; timing reports; throughput validation; 11-risk register. Evidence issues / actuals: 2 unresolved risks: incomplete valid-range metadata and unresolved CDC warning affecting low-frequency status path. You decision required: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Action: complete the L5 Certification Portfolio Pack by filling these required workbook fields without shortening the text: Portfolio cover note; artifact chain; evidence map; retry log; capability proof; transfer note; reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: L1-L5 artifact chain, capability evidence map, unresolved risk summary, reviewer validation, and how each level changed the final recommendation. Output decision: Supervised prototype validation / controlled testing / blocked. Reviewer reads this artifact as follows: Checks whether you connects all artifacts into a coherent capability proof. Restriction: stay inside L5 Embedded Design Engineer responsibility. Do not claim full production approval, diagnose unproven root cause, or take ownership of software/test/integration/timing decisions that require senior or cross-team confirmation. Use AI only as a coach for guided questions, not as the final answer provider. Level-specific correction: The certification portfolio must prove maturity from evidence readiness to simulation validation to integration readiness to timing/performance risk review to final decision-support validation. Reviewer should be able to trace how each level changed the final recommendation. Final decision language is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. Unresolved risks must be classified as acceptable with controls, needs controlled testing, or blocks release/production use.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "End-to-End Embedded FPGA Design Validation and Certification Portfolio", "description": "The technology solutions team now wants to decide whether the embedded FPGA workflow is mature enough to enter a supervised prototype validation review. You receive the full L1 to L4 evidence chain: the 12-signal interface list, HDL skeleton, simulation logs with corrected assertion outcomes, SoC integration map, AXI/Avalon bus table, DDR/QDR memory notes, timing reports, throughput validation, interface documents, and a risk register with 11 total risks. Most risks have mitigation notes, but 2 remain unresolved: incomplete valid-range metadata for one telemetry-facing register group and an unresolved CDC warning affecting one low-frequency status path. You must decide whether the workflow is ready for supervised prototype validation, ready only for further controlled testing, or blocked until evidence and governance controls are strengthened. This L5 capstone is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. You evaluates governance, unresolved risks, evidence consistency, and final decision-support readiness."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready L5 evidence for end-to-end embedded FPGA decision-support validation and certification-level portfolio proof.", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "The technology solutions team now wants to decide whether the embedded FPGA workflow is mature enough to enter a supervised prototype validation review. You receive the full L1 to L4 evidence chain: the 12-signal interface list, HDL skeleton, simulation logs with corrected assertion outcomes, SoC integration map, AXI/Avalon bus table, DDR/QDR memory notes, timing reports, throughput validation, interface documents, and a risk register with 11 total risks. Most risks have mitigation notes, but 2 remain unresolved: incomplete valid-range metadata for one telemetry-facing register group and an unresolved CDC warning affecting one low-frequency status path. You must decide whether the workflow is ready for supervised prototype validation, ready only for further controlled testing, or blocked until evidence and governance controls are strengthened. This L5 capstone is supervised prototype validation only, not production release or autonomous system approval. You evaluates governance, unresolved risks, evidence consistency, and final decision-support readiness."}]}', '{"engage": {"color": "#6366f1", "label": "Engage", "estLabel": "20-30 minutes", "purposeTag": "Workplace Risk", "description": "Understand the workplace situation, engineering risk, and L1 FPGA design evidence readiness before HDL implementation review boundary before creating any artifact."}, "evolve": {"color": "#ef4444", "label": "Evolve", "estLabel": "20-30 minutes", "purposeTag": "Transfer Learning", "description": "Reflect on how the same evidence-based reasoning transfers to the next level or another embedded FPGA workflow."}, "empower": {"color": "#f59e0b", "label": "Empower", "estLabel": "20-30 minutes", "purposeTag": "Defend Decision", "description": "Make and defend a readiness, correction, escalation, optimization, or validation decision using evidence."}, "explain": {"color": "#06b6d4", "label": "Explain", "estLabel": "20-30 minutes", "purposeTag": "Learn Boundary", "description": "Understand the concept, responsibility boundary, or engineering rule that makes the evidence meaningful."}, "explore": {"color": "#8b5cf6", "label": "Explore", "estLabel": "20-30 minutes", "purposeTag": "Inspect Evidence", "description": "Inspect the available design, simulation, integration, timing, validation, or portfolio evidence before deciding."}, "express": {"color": "#22c55e", "label": "Express", "estLabel": "30-45 minutes", "purposeTag": "Create Artifact", "description": "Create the module artifact using visible evidence, role boundary, and human-first engineering reasoning."}}', '2026-06-09 16:09:09.874457+00', '2026-06-09 16:09:09.874457+00', 'kar