 approved Customer Support roles, shift, location, salary band, recruiter owner. Action: complete the L2 Requisition Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Role count, department, location, shift timing, salary band, reporting manager, recruiter owner, assumptions. Evidence to cite: Role count, department, location, shift timing, salary band, reporting manager, recruiter owner, assumptions. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l2-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 ATS Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L2 ATS Evidence Validation Checklist using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Routine Requisition Preparation and ATS Drafting case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for 9 incomplete ATS fields and evidence support for each mandatory field. Action: complete the L2 ATS Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Missing ATS fields, source evidence, approval ID, budget confirmation, JD version, salary band, validation result. Evidence to cite: Missing ATS fields, source evidence, approval ID, budget confirmation, JD version, salary band, validation result. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l2-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 ATS Draft Completion Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L2 ATS Draft Completion Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Routine Requisition Preparation and ATS Drafting case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for complete supported ATS fields and prepare recruiter handoff without inventing values. Action: complete the L2 ATS Draft Completion Note by filling these required fields: Completed fields, corrected fields, pending fields, source reference, recruiter handoff message, final launch status. Evidence to cite: Completed fields, corrected fields, pending fields, source reference, recruiter handoff message, final launch status. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l2-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Requisition Launch Risk Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L2 Requisition Launch Risk Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Routine Requisition Preparation and ATS Drafting case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for wrong shift, wrong salary band, outdated JD, missing approval reference. Action: complete the L2 Requisition Launch Risk Note by filling these required fields: Risk category, affected field, evidence source, launch impact, owner, severity, next action. Evidence to cite: Risk category, affected field, evidence source, launch impact, owner, severity, next action. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l2-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 ATS Launch Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L2 ATS Launch Closure Report using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Routine Requisition Preparation and ATS Drafting case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for give a launch-ready, correction-needed, or hold decision. Action: complete the L2 ATS Launch Closure Report by filling these required fields: Fields completed, evidence checked, launch blockers, recruiter note, launch decision, closure confidence. Evidence to cite: Fields completed, evidence checked, launch blockers, recruiter note, launch decision, closure confidence. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l2-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L2 Requisition Preparation Portfolio", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L2 Requisition Preparation Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Routine Requisition Preparation and ATS Drafting case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for show the requisition was drafted from approved evidence. Action: complete the L2 Requisition Preparation Portfolio by filling these required fields: Intake note, validation checklist, ATS action note, risk note, closure report, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: Intake note, validation checklist, ATS action note, risk note, closure report, reviewer validation. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Routine Requisition Preparation and ATS Drafting", "description": "The recruitment team receives an approved hiring request for 5 Customer Support Associates for a new service desk process starting next month. You receive a manager-approved hiring form, budget confirmation for all 5 roles, updated job description, shift timing details, work location, salary band, reporting manager, and an ATS requisition draft with 9 incomplete fields. You must validate role data, check approval alignment, complete the ATS draft, and prepare a launch-ready recruiter handoff. If you miss salary band, shift timing, location, reporting manager, or approval reference, the requisition may be launched incorrectly and create candidate mismatch or approval rework."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready evidence for MBA HR requisition capability: L2 ATS Draft Readiness Sheet, L2 Requisition Case Intake Note, L2 ATS Evidence Validation Checklist, L2 ATS Draft Completion Note, L2 Requisition Launch Risk Note, L2 ATS Launch Closure Report, L2 Requisition Preparation Portfolio", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "The recruitment team receives an approved hiring request for 5 Customer Support Associates for a new service desk process starting next month. You receive a manager-approved hiring form, budget confirmation for all 5 roles, updated job description, shift timing details, work location, salary band, reporting manager, and an ATS requisition draft with 9 incomplete fields. You must validate role data, check approval alignment, complete the ATS draft, and prepare a launch-ready recruiter handoff. If you miss salary band, shift timing, location, reporting manager, or approval reference, the requisition may be launched incorrectly and create candidate mismatch or approval rework."}, {"id": "lpc-mba-h