acts without showing a connected evidence chain from intake to final recommendation. In this level, focus on show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, decision trail, reviewer validation, transfer of learning", "reason_behind_concept": "This concept matters because requisition launch affects budget discipline, manager trust, candidate quality, recruiter workload, and audit evidence.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module when handling show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline in the hiring-demand-to-requisition workflow."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that my final decision came from all earlier evidence and not from opinion?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio, Transfer and Final Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You prove they handled a high-pressure requisition without violating approval discipline."}], "duration": "18 hours", "course_id": "crs-mba-hr-req-l3", "xp_reward": 850, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "MBA HR professionals must handle urgency without bypassing evidence. Exception management requires split decisions, audit-safe reasoning, and controlled escalation rather than blanket approval or blanket refusal.", "course_code": "MBA-HR-REQ-L3", "description": "You can handle high-pressure requisition exceptions by separating approved, pending, duplicate, and escalation-required demand, then preparing a defensible split, hold, proceed, or escalate decision.", "domain_name": "MBA - Human Resources", "level_label": "L3", "sequence_no": 3, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "You complete exception-handling artifacts that prove approval discipline, duplicate checks, business-pressure documentation, split launch action, escalation, and defensible closure communication.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "Hiring Demand to Approved Requisition Launch", "difficulty_level": "intermediate", "job_pathway_role": "MBA HR / Talent Acquisition Associate", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Readiness Sheet using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for exception handling where urgency cannot override approval evidence. Action: complete the L3 Exception Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: Exception workflow, approval hierarchy, urgent hiring risk, duplicate-check process, escalation pathway. Evidence to cite: Exception workflow, approval hierarchy, urgent hiring risk, duplicate-check process, escalation pathway. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Case Intake Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for 8 requested, 4 approved, 2 pending, 2 possible duplicate roles. Action: complete the L3 Exception Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Requested roles, approved roles, pending roles, duplicate roles, manager pressure, missing evidence, assumptions. Evidence to cite: Requested roles, approved roles, pending roles, duplicate roles, manager pressure, missing evidence, assumptions. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Evidence Validation Checklist using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for approval tracker, budget exception note, duplicate report, and owner confirmations. Action: complete the L3 Exception Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Approval status, budget status, duplicate match, owner confirmation, evidence gap, proceed/hold decision. Evidence to cite: Approval status, budget status, duplicate match, owner confirmation, evidence gap, proceed/hold decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Requisition Exception Action Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Requisition Exception Action Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for create a split decision: proceed valid roles, hold pending roles, escalate duplicates. Action: complete the L3 Requisition Exception Action Note by filling these required fields: Launchable roles, held roles, duplicate cases, escalation message, manager response, final action decision. Evidence to cite: Launchable roles, held roles, duplicate cases, escalation message, manager response, final action decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent