Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for give a defensible split/hold/escalate response to the regional head. Action: complete the L3 Exception Closure Report by filling these required fields: Launch decision, held items, escalation owners, rationale, evidence references, closure message. Evidence to cite: Launch decision, held items, escalation owners, rationale, evidence references, closure message. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l3-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Exception Handling Portfolio", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L3 Exception Handling Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline. Action: complete the L3 Exception Handling Portfolio by filling these required fields: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Requisition Exception Handling and Launch Decision", "description": "A regional head requests urgent hiring for 8 Operations Coordinators, but the HR tracker shows only 4 approved positions. Finance approval is pending for 2 roles, and 2 roles appear to duplicate an earlier requisition opened by another manager. You receive the hiring request, approval tracker, budget exception note, duplicate requisition report, and manager escalation email asking HR to “launch now and fix approvals later.” You must diagnose the exception, separate approved from unapproved demand, identify duplication risk, document business pressure, and decide whether to proceed, hold, split, or escalate. If you launch all 8 roles without evidence, HR may create duplicate hiring, budget breach, and audit risk."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready evidence for MBA HR requisition capability: L3 Exception Readiness Sheet, L3 Exception Case Intake Note, L3 Exception Evidence Validation Checklist, L3 Requisition Exception Action Note, L3 Exception Risk and Escalation Note, L3 Exception Closure Report, L3 Exception Handling Portfolio", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "A regional head requests urgent hiring for 8 Operations Coordinators, but the HR tracker shows only 4 approved positions. Finance approval is pending for 2 roles, and 2 roles appear to duplicate an earlier requisition opened by another manager. You receive the hiring request, approval tracker, budget exception note, duplicate requisition report, and manager escalation email aski