ce, competency demonstration, workplace transfer"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio by completing the MBA HR requisition task: You prove capability to improve requisition launch quality, not only process individual requests. Required evidence inside the artifact: Defect analysis, validation checklist, improvement note, risk note, closure report, reviewer validation.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may submit separate artifacts without showing a connected evidence chain from intake to final recommendation. In this level, focus on show defect validation, improvement logic, risk control, and closure recommendation.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, decision trail, reviewer validation, transfer of learning", "reason_behind_concept": "This concept matters because requisition launch affects budget discipline, manager trust, candidate quality, recruiter workload, and audit evidence.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module when handling show defect validation, improvement logic, risk control, and closure recommendation in the hiring-demand-to-requisition workflow."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that my final decision came from all earlier evidence and not from opinion?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio, Transfer and Final Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You prove capability to improve requisition launch quality, not only process individual requests."}], "duration": "20 hours", "course_id": "crs-mba-hr-req-l4", "xp_reward": 1000, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "MBA HR learners must progress from individual request processing to process-quality thinking. Requisition quality control protects hiring speed, candidate fit, recruiter utilization, audit readiness, and manager accountability.", "course_code": "MBA-HR-REQ-L4", "description": "You can review multiple requisitions, validate defect evidence, identify recurring quality failures, find process causes, recommend control checkpoints, and propose a revised requisition-readiness checklist.", "domain_name": "MBA - Human Resources", "level_label": "L4", "sequence_no": 4, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "You complete quality-improvement artifacts that prove defect validation, pattern analysis, root-cause reasoning, control design, implementation prioritization, and closure recommendation.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "Hiring Demand to Approved Requisition Launch", "difficulty_level": "advanced-intermediate", "job_pathway_role": "MBA HR / Talent Acquisition Associate", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Requisition Quality Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Requisition Quality Readiness Sheet using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for process quality review across multiple requisitions. Action: complete the L4 Requisition Quality Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: Defect categories, process map, quality-control checkpoints, stakeholder ownership, review plan. Evidence to cite: Defect categories, process map, quality-control checkpoints, stakeholder ownership, review plan. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Quality Review Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Quality Review Case Intake Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for 25 requisitions, 11 rework cases, 6 salary corrections, 4 wrong assignments, 3 cancellations. Action: complete the L4 Quality Review Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Review scope, defect counts, data sources, review assumptions, stakeholders, intake decision. Evidence to cite: Review scope, defect counts, data sources, review assumptions, stakeholders, intake decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Requisition Defect Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Requisition Defect Validation Checklist using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for defect log, approval turnaround data, recruiter tracker, correction emails, ATS audit comments. Action: complete the L4 Requisition Defect Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Defect ID, requisition ID, defect source, defect type, root evidence, impact, validation decision. Evidence to cite: Defect ID, requisition ID, defect source, defect type, root evidence, impact, validation decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Process Improvement Action Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Process Improvement Action Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for identify root causes and design a revised requisition-readiness checklist. Action: complete the L4 Process Improvement Action Note by filling these required fields: Root cause, affected step, proposed control, checklist field, owner, expected improvement. Evidence to cite: Root cause, affected step, proposed control, checklist field, owner, expected improvement. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Requisition Process Risk Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Requisition Process Risk Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for repeated salary errors, weak justification, wrong assignment, delayed approvals. Action: complete the L4 Requisition Process Risk Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, defect pattern, business impact, control gap, severity, owner, mitigation. Evidence to cite: Risk ID, defect pattern, business impact, control gap, severity, owner, mitigation. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Quality Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Quality Closure Report using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for recommend implementable quality controls to the HR operations lead. Action: complete the L4 Quality Closure Report by filling these required fields: Defect summary, root causes, recommended controls, priority, implementation note, closure decision. Evidence to cite: Defect summary, root causes, recommended controls, priority, implementation note, closure decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for show defect validation, improvement logic, risk control, and closure recommendation. Action: complete the L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio by filling these required fields: Defect analysis, validation checklist, improvement note, risk note, closure report, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: Defect analysis, validation checklist, improvement note, risk note, closure report, reviewer validation. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement", "description": "The HR operations lead asks you to review 25 requisitions launched in the last quarter because 11 had rework, 6 had salary-band corrections after launch, 4 had wrong recruiter assignment, and 3 were cancelled due to unclear business justification. You receive a requisition defect log, approval turnaround data, recruiter assignment tracker, manager correction emails, and ATS audit comments. You must identify recurring requisition quality failures, find root causes, recommend control checkpoints, and propose a revised requisition-readiness checklist. If you only corrects individual forms without identifying process causes, the same rework will continue across future hiring cycles."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready evidence for MBA HR requisition capability: L4 Requisition Quality Readiness Sheet, L4 Quality Review Case Intake Note, L4 Requisition Defect Validation Checklist, L4 Process Improvement Action Note, L4 Requisition Process Risk Note, L4 Quality Closure Report, L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "The HR operations lead asks you to review 25 requisitions launched in the last quarter because 11 had rework, 6 had salary-band corrections after launch, 4 had wrong recruiter assignment, and 3 were cancelled due to unclear business justification. You receive a requisition defect log, approval turnaround data, recruiter assignment tracker, manager correction emails, and ATS audit comments. You must identify recurring requisition quality failures, find root causes, recommend control checkpoints, and propose a revised requisition-readiness checklist. If you only corrects individual forms without identifying process causes, the same rework will continue across future hiring cycles."}, {"id": "lpc-mba-hr-req-l5", "gap": 2, "badge": "Requisition Governance Audit Readiness", "title": "Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching", "status": "not_started", "modules": [{"id": "mod-mba-hr-req-l5-m0", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "tools": {"tools_used": "Course brief, requisition workflow map, readiness worksheet", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-mba-hr-req-l5-m0-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/mba-hr-req-l5/content/c-mba-hr-req-l5-m0-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness: Decision defense check for governance-level requisition control and audit readiness", "status": "published", "isView