sts. Action: complete the L5 Governance Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Review scope, record count, exception count, audit concern, stakeholders, decision criteria. Evidence to cite: Review scope, record count, exception count, audit concern, stakeholders, decision criteria. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l5-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Governance Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L5 Governance Evidence Validation Checklist using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for launch dates, approval dates, exception types, policy status, and audit evidence. Action: complete the L5 Governance Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Requisition ID, launch date, approval date, exception type, policy status, audit evidence, validation decision. Evidence to cite: Requisition ID, launch date, approval date, exception type, policy status, audit evidence, validation decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the modul