on, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching", "description": "The HR head is preparing for a quarterly workforce governance review. You receive 60 requisition records, 14 exception approvals, 9 delayed finance approvals, 7 manager override requests, and an audit note questioning whether HR launched roles before documented approval. You must evaluate the requisition governance process, identify whether launch decisions were evidence-backed, classify policy exceptions, create a manager coaching plan, and recommend governance controls for future requisition launches. You must decide whether the requisition process is audit-ready, conditionally acceptable with controls, or exposed to governance risk."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready evidence for MBA HR requisition capability: L5 Requisition Governance Readiness Sheet, L5 Governance Case Intake Note, L5 Governance Evidence Validation Checklist, L5 Governance Action and Coaching Note, L5 Governance Risk and Escalation Note, L5 Governance Closure Report, L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "The HR head is preparing for a quarterly workforce governance review. You receive 60 requisition records, 14 exception approvals, 9 delayed finance approvals, 7 manager override requests, and an audit note questioning whether HR launched roles before documented approval. You must evaluate the requisition governance process, identify whether launch decisions were evidence-backed, classify policy exceptions, create a manager coaching plan, and recommend governance controls for future requisition launches. You must decide whether the requisition process is audit-ready, conditionally accept