in, evidence map, decision trail, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. For final submission, cite the specific case evidence from this level, write the decision in workplace language, and make clear whether the item is ready, partially ready, hold/split/escalate, conditionally acceptable, audit-ready, or blocked as relevant. Use AI only for guided questions and clarity checks, not for final approval or invented details.", "accepted_file_types": ["xlsx", "docx", "pdf", "zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "ZIP + PDF"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-mba-hr-req-l1-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/mba/Mod6_02_Template.xlsx", "file_name": "Mod6_02_Template.xlsx", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-mba-hr-req-l1-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-mba-hr-req-l1-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-mba-hr-req-l1-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-mba-hr-req-l1-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: Requisition Launch Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can you complete the Requisition Launch Portfolio Pack using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information?", "instructions": "Use the existing template fields for Requisition Launch Portfolio Pack. Required evidence: Artifact chain, evidence map, decision trail, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. For final submission, cite the specific case evidence from this level, write the decision in workplace language, and make clear whether the item is ready, partially ready, hold/split/escalate, conditionally acceptable, audit-ready, or blocked as relevant. Use AI only for guided questions and clarity checks, not for final approval or invented details.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Portfolio chain, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, final reviewer validation", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Reflective practice, portfolio evidence, competency demonstration, workplace transfer"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the Requisition Launch Portfolio Pack by completing the MBA HR requisition task: The reviewer must see that you did not simply fill a form. You must connect intake, validation, action, risk, and closure into a complete requisition-readiness proof. Required evidence inside the artifact: Artifact chain, evidence map, decision trail, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may submit separate artifacts without showing a connected evidence chain from intake to final recommendation. In this level, focus on show readiness, intake, validation, action, risk, closure, and portfolio evidence.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, decision trail, reviewer validation, transfer of learning", "reason_behind_concept": "This concept matters because requisition launch affects budget discipline, manager trust, candidate quality, recruiter workload, and audit evidence.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module when handling show readiness, intake, validation, action, risk, closure, and portfolio evidence in the hiring-demand-to-requisition workflow."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that my final decision came from all earlier evidence and not from opinion?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio, Transfer and Final Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The reviewer must see that you did not simply fill a form. You must connect intake, validation, action, risk, and closure into a complete requisition-readiness proof."}], "duration": "14 hours", "course_id": "crs-mba-hr-req-l1", "xp_reward": 600, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "MBA HR professionals must not open roles only because a manager has urgent demand. They must check approval, budget, role clarity, job-description readiness, and ownership before requisition launch.", "course_code": "MBA-HR-REQ-L1", "description": "You can convert an incomplete manager hiring demand into a structured requisition-readiness decision by checking role details, headcount approval, budget evidence, missing information, HR ownership, and ATS launch readiness before processing.", "domain_name": "MBA - Human Resources", "level_label": "L1", "sequence_no": 1, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "You complete seven connected requisition-readiness artifacts that prove intake discipline, evidence checking, controlled HR handoff, risk escalation, and closure communication.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "Hiring Demand to Approved Requisition Launch", "difficulty_level": "beginner", "job_pathway_role": "MBA HR / Talent Acquisition Associate", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l1-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Requisition Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the Requisition Readiness Sheet using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Guided Requisition Intake and Readiness Check case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for manager demand versus approved headcount. Action: complete the Requisition Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: Workflow map, stakeholder map, HR-owned checks, manager-owned inputs, finance approval need, ATS readiness requirements, readiness gaps. Evidence to cite: Workflow map, stakeholder map, HR-owned checks, manager-owned inputs, finance approval need, ATS readiness requirements, readiness gaps. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l1-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Hiring Request Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the Hiring Request Case Intake Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Guided Requisition Intake and Readiness Check case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for 1 approved replacement role and 2 unapproved expansion roles. Action: complete the Hiring Request Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Request summary, requested headcount, approved headcount, role reason, knowns, unknowns, assumptions, clarification questions. Evidence to cite: Request summary, requested headcount, approved headcount, role reason, knowns, unknowns, assumptions, clarification questions. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l1-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Requisition Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the Requisition Evidence Validation Checklist using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Guided Requisition Intake and Readiness Check case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for role-count mismatch, salary range gap, territory split gap, reporting manager gap. Action: complete the Requisition Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Evidence item, source owner, completeness check, budget check, approval check, JD check, salary range check, validation decision. Evidence to cite: Evidence item, source owner, completeness check, budget check, approval check, JD check, salary range check, validation decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l1-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Requisition Readiness Action Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the Requisition Readiness Action Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Guided Requisition Intake and Readiness Check case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for mark 1 role process-ready, 2 roles approval-pending, and prepare a controlled HR handoff. Action: complete the Requisition Readiness Action Note by filling these required fields: Approved role count, blocked role count, missing fields, ATS-ready fields, clarification message, handoff owner, final action. Evidence to cite: Approved role count, blocked role count, missing fields, ATS-ready fields, clarification message, handoff owner, final action. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l1-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Requisition Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the Requisition Risk and Escalation Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Guided Requisition Intake and Readiness Check case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for budget-control breach, old JD risk, missing salary range delay, unclear ownership. Action: complete the Requisition Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, risk category, observed evidence, consequence, severity, owner, escalation reason, next action. Evidence to cite: Risk ID, risk category, observed evidence, consequence, severity, owner, escalation reason, next action. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l1-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Requisition Quality and Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the Requisition Quality and Closure Report using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Guided Requisition Intake and Readiness Check case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for explain what can move and what is blocked before ATS launch. Action: complete the Requisition Quality and Closure Report by filling these required fields: Work completed, checks passed, checks failed, open issues, manager message, confidence level, closure decision. Evidence to cite: Work completed, checks passed, checks failed, open issues, manager message, confidence level, closure decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l1-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Requisition Launch Portfolio Pack", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the Requisition Launch Portfolio Pack using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Guided Requisition Intake and Readiness Check case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for show readiness, intake, validation, action, risk, closure, and portfolio evidence. Action: complete the Requisition Launch Portfolio Pack by filling these required fields: Artifact chain, evidence map, decision trail, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: Artifact chain, evidence map, decision trail, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Guided Requisition Intake and Readiness Check", "description": "A business unit manager has raised a request to hire 3 Sales Executives for the South Zone because the team missed its last two monthly revenue targets by 18% and 22%. You receive a hiring request email, an old job description, a headcount tracker, a budget approval screenshot, and a vacancy tracker showing 1 approved replacement role and 2 unapproved expansion roles. The request is incomplete because the manager has not clarified territory allocation, salary range, reporting manager, replacement versus new-role justification, and whether the budget covers all 3 positions. You must decide whether the requisition is ready for HR processing, partially ready with missing information, or blocked until role, budget, and approval gaps are clarified."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready evidence for MBA HR requisition capability: Requisition Readiness Sheet, Hiring Request Case Intake Note, Requisition Evidence Validation Checklist, Requisition Readiness Action Note, Requisition Risk and Escalation Note, Requisition Quality and Closure Report, Requisition Launch Portfolio Pack", "completion_percentage": 14, "common_course_problem_statement": "A business unit manager has raised a request to hire 3 Sales Executives for the South Zone because the team missed its last two monthly revenue targets by 18% and 22%. You receive a hiring request email, an old job description, a headcount tracker, a budget approval screenshot, and a vacancy tracker showing 1 approved replacement role and 2 unapproved expansion roles. The request is incomplete because the manager has not clarified territory allocation, salary range, reporting manager, replacement versus new-role justification, and whether the budget covers all 3 positions. You must decide whether the requisition is ready for HR processing, partially ready with missing information, or blocked until role, budget, and approval gaps are clarified."}, {"id": "lpc-mba-hr-req-l2", "gap": 2, "badge": "ATS Requisition Drafting", "title": "Routine Requisition Preparation and ATS Drafting", "status": "not_started", "modules": [{"id": "mod-mba-hr-req-l2