rtfolio", "description": "Can you complete the L3 Exception Handling Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information?", "instructions": "Use the existing template fields for L3 Exception Handling Portfolio. Required evidence: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation. For final submission, cite the specific case evidence from this level, write the decision in workplace language, and make clear whether the item is ready, partially ready, hold/split/escalate, conditionally acceptable, audit-ready, or blocked as relevant. Use AI only for guided questions and clarity checks, not for final approval or invented details.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Portfolio chain, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, final reviewer validation", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Reflective practice, portfolio evidence, competency demonstration, workplace transfer"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the L3 Exception Handling Portfolio by completing the MBA HR requisition task: You prove they handled a high-pressure requisition without violating approval discipline. Required evidence inside the artifact: Evidence chain, split decision, risk log, escalation trail, closure proof, reviewer validation.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may submit separate artifacts without showing a connected evidence chain from intake to final recommendation. In this level, focus on show high-pressure exception handling without violating approval discipline.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, decision trai