tput decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Requisition Process Risk Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Requisition Process Risk Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for repeated salary errors, weak justification, wrong assignment, delayed approvals. Action: complete the L4 Requisition Process Risk Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, defect pattern, business impact, control gap, severity, owner, mitigation. Evidence to cite: Risk ID, defect pattern, business impact, control gap, severity, owner, mitigation. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Quality Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Quality Closure Report using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for recommend implementable quality controls to the HR operations lead. Action: complete the L4 Quality Closure Report by filling these required fields: Defect summary, root causes, recommended controls, priority, implementation note, closure decision. Evidence to cite: Defect summary, root causes, recommended controls, priority, implementation note, closure decision. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l4-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for show defect validation, improvement logic, risk control, and closure recommendation. Action: complete the L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio by filling these required fields: Defect analysis, validation checklist, improvement note, risk note, closure report, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: Defect analysis, validation checklist, improvement note, risk note, closure report, reviewer validation. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Requisition Quality Control and Process Improvement", "description": "The HR operations lead asks you to review 25 requisitions launched in the last quarter because 11 had rework, 6 had salary-band corrections after launch, 4 had wrong recruiter assignment, and 3 were cancelled due to unclear business justification. You receive a requisition defect log, approval turnaround data, recruiter assignment tracker, manager correction emails, and ATS audit comments. You must identify recurring requisition quality failures, find root causes, recommend control checkpoints, and propose a revised requisition-readiness checklist. If you only corrects individual forms without identifying process causes, the same rework will continue across future hiring cycles."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready evidence for MBA HR requisition capability: L4 Requisition Quality Readiness Sheet, L4 Quality Review Case Intake Note, L4 Requisition Defect Validation Checklist, L4 Process Improvement Action Note, L4 Requisition Process Risk Note, L4 Quality Closure Report, L4 Quality Improvement Portfolio", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "The HR operations lead asks you to review 25 requisitions launched in the last quarter because 11 had rework, 6 had salary-band corrections after launch, 4 had wrong recruiter assignment, and 3 were cancelled due to unclear business justification. You receive a requisition defect log, approval turnaround data, recruiter assignment tracker, manager correction emails, and ATS audit comments. You must identify recurring requisition quality failures, find root causes, recommend control checkpoints, and propose a revised requisition-readiness checklist. If you only corrects individual forms without identifying process causes, the same rework will continue across future hiring cycles."}, {"id": "lpc-mba-hr-req-l5", "gap": 2, "badge": "Requisition Governance Audit Readiness", "title": "Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching", "status": "not_started", "modules": [{"id": "mod-mba-hr-req-l5-m0", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "tools": {"tools_used": "Course brief, requisition workflow map, readiness worksheet", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-mba-hr-req-l5-m0-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/mba-hr-req-l5/content/c-mba-hr-req-l5-m0-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness: Decision defense check for governance-level requisition control and audit readiness", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L5 Requisition Governance Readiness Sheet: What decision can you defend using the evidence: ready, partial, hold, split, escalate, conditional, or blocked?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence; use AI only 