ce Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information?", "instructions": "Use the existing template fields for L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio. Required evidence: Governance review pack, evidence checklist, coaching note, risk register, closure report, certification proof. For final submission, cite the specific case evidence from this level, write the decision in workplace language, and make clear whether the item is ready, partially ready, hold/split/escalate, conditionally acceptable, audit-ready, or blocked as relevant. Use AI only for guided questions and clarity checks, not for final approval or invented details.", "accepted_file_types": ["xlsx", "docx", "pdf", "zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "ZIP + PDF"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-mba-hr-req-l5-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/mba-hr-req-l5/ART_HR_REQ_L5_M6_Portfolio_Template", "file_name": "ART_HR_REQ_L5_M6_Portfolio_Template", "file_type": "docx", "artifact_id": "ma-mba-hr-req-l5-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-mba-hr-req-l5-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-mba-hr-req-l5-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-mba-hr-req-l5-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio", "description": "Can you complete the L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information?", "instructions": "Use the existing template fields for L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio. Required evidence: Governance review pack, evidence checklist, coaching note, risk register, closure report, certification proof. For final submission, cite the specific case evidence from this level, write the decision in workplace language, and make clear whether the item is ready, partially ready, hold/split/escalate, conditionally acceptable, audit-ready, or blocked as relevant. Use AI only for guided questions and clarity checks, not for final approval or invented details.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Portfolio chain, evidence map, retry log, transfer note, final reviewer validation", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Reflective practice, portfolio evidence, competency demonstration, workplace transfer"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the L5 Requisition Governance Portfolio by completing the MBA HR requisition task: You prove capability to evaluate requisition governance and coach managers using evidence. Required evidence inside the artifact: Governance review pack, evidence checklist, coaching note, risk register, closure report, certification proof.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "You may submit separate artifacts without showing a connected evidence chain from intake to final recommendation. In this level, focus on show governance review, coaching plan, risk register, closure, and certification proof.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, decision trail, reviewer validation, transfer of learning", "reason_behind_concept": "This concept matters because requisition launch affects budget discipline, manager trust, candidate quality, recruiter workload, and audit evidence.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use this module when handling show governance review, coaching plan, risk register, closure, and certification proof in the hiring-demand-to-requisition workflow."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that my final decision came from all earlier evidence and not from opinion?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio, Transfer and Final Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You prove capability to evaluate requisition governance and coach managers using evidence."}], "duration": "22 hours", "course_id": "crs-mba-hr-req-l5", "xp_reward": 1200, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "MBA HR professionals at advanced level must connect operational requisition work to governance, audit evidence, manager behavior, exception control, and leadership decision-making.", "course_code": "MBA-HR-REQ-L5", "description": "You can evaluate requisition governance across a large evidence set, classify policy exceptions, assess audit readiness, design manager coaching actions, and recommend controls for future requisition launches.", "domain_name": "MBA - Human Resources", "level_label": "L5", "sequence_no": 5, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "You complete governance artifacts that prove audit-scope framing, evidence validation across records, exception classification, manager coaching design, risk escalation, leadership closure, and certification-ready portfolio proof.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1454165804606-c3d57bc86b40?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "Hiring Demand to Approved Requisition Launch", "difficulty_level": "advanced", "job_pathway_role": "MBA HR / Talent Acquisition Associate", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l5-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Requisition Governance Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L5 Requisition Governance Readiness Sheet using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for governance-level requisition control and audit readiness. Action: complete the L5 Requisition Governance Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: Governance scope, audit questions, control framework, manager coaching need, readiness criteria. Evidence to cite: Governance scope, audit questions, control framework, manager coaching need, readiness criteria. Also cite the concrete case facts from this level, including role counts, approvals, exceptions, defects, audit records, or governance indicators where applicable. Output decision: state the module-appropriate decision such as ready, partially ready, hold, split, escalate, ready after correction, conditionally acceptable with controls, audit-ready, or blocked. Do not invent missing values, bypass approval evidence, launch unapproved roles, hide risks, or ask AI to make the final HR decision.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-mba-hr-req-l5-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L5 Governance Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can you complete the L5 Governance Case Intake Note using the module evidence and show a defensible MBA HR requisition decision without assuming missing approval, budget, ownership, or launch information? Input: use the Requisition Governance, Audit Readiness, and Manager Coaching case problem, module scenario, and relevant source evidence for 60 records, 14 exception approvals, 9 delayed finance approvals, 7 override requests. Action: complete the L5 Governance Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Review scope, record count, exception count, audit concern, stakeholders, decision criteria. Evidence to cite: Review scope, record count, exception count, audit concern, stakeholders, de