ty checks, or missed-risk prompts.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Action-note writing, handoff framing, readiness impact explanation, decision options", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Technical note structure, evidence-to-action reasoning, L1 handoff language"}, "module_no": 3, "description": "Build the Telemetry Readiness Action Note by translating the validated evidence into a practical next-step action, handoff, or escalation recommendation.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may recommend action without enough proof or without separating fix, handoff, and escalation.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Evidence-based action note, handoff logic, readiness decision", "reason_behind_concept": "A handoff is useful only when it cites evidence, explains impact, and separates learner-owned validation from team-owned fixes.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use after evidence validation when the learner must document what can be acted on and what should be handed off."}, "student_confusion": "Should I clean the data, escalate the issue, or mark it as not ready?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Readiness Action", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You must perform a first-level telemetry-readiness action using the evidence already validated. They must count and mark missing values, identify timestamp gaps, list packet jumps, connect warning logs to data trust issues, identify unclear fields, and explain how each issue could affect anomaly detection. The output must be a usable technical handoff, not a generic observation note."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l1-m4", "title": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations"