ckers in other evidence packs", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Risk and Escalation Note: How would you transfer this validation logic to another dataset, sensor stream, or industry case? Focus on blockers, risk severity, consequences, owners, and escalation criteria.", "follow_up": "Write one transfer rule you can reuse in a future AI/ML evidence-readiness review."}], "content_type": "reflection", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m4-explain", "url": "#", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "M4 Explain: Risk guide: blocker classification and escalation criteria", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Risk and Escalation Note: What concept or role boundary helps you understand the issue without overclaiming root cause? Focus on blockers, risk severity, consequences, owners, and escalation criteria.", "follow_up": "State the concept in simple words and link it to the telemetry case."}], "content_type": "video", "duration_seconds": 600}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m4-explore", "url": "#", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "M4 Explore: Identify minor issues, major issues, blockers, owners, and escalation needs", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Risk and Escalation Note: What evidence can you observe in the case, dataset summary, logs, UDP description, or shared-memory field list? Focus on blockers, risk severity, consequences, owners, and escalation criteria.", "follow_up": "Point to at least one visible evidence item rather than using a general opinion."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m4-express", "url": "#", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "M4 Express: Practice Risk and Escalation Note using blocker and owner mapping", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Risk and Escalation Note: What exactly will you write in your artifact, and which evidence will you cite? Focus on blockers, risk severity, consequences, owners, and escalation criteria.", "follow_up": "Check whether your artifact separates facts, assumptions, role boundary, and next action."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to help classify blockers as data, system, ownership, or escalation issues while you keep the final judgement evidence-based.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the action/handoff note from Module 3 and produces risk decisions that must be communicated in Module 5."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m4-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m4-f1", "order": 1, "title": "Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you identified which issues require senior, telemetry, embedded, software, test, or data-owner support and explained the consequence of each blocker?", "instructions": "Classify risks using observed evidence, consequence, severity, owner, escalation reason, and next action. Do not diagnose embedded-system root cause. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence, reasoning clarity, correct role boundary, escalation where needed, and complete fields.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l1-m4", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod4_02_template%20.xlsx", "file_name": "Mod4_02_template.xlsx", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m4-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m4-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m4-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m4-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: Risk and Escalation Note", "description": "Has you identified which issues require senior, telemetry, embedded, software, test, or data-owner support and explained the consequence of each blocker?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, or missed-risk prompts.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Risk category, severity, evidence consequence, owner mapping, escalation criteria", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Risk log basics, escalation logic, impact statements"}, "module_no": 4, "description": "Build the Risk and Escalation Note by classifying readiness issues as minor, major, blocker, or escalation-needed and assigning the right owner.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may ignore blockers such as unclear sensor meaning, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, or log warnings.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Blocker identification, risk classification, escalation criteria", "reason_behind_concept": "Escalation decisions must be based on observed evidence and consequence, not assumptions about system failure or root cause.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use when evidence issues may prevent safe next-step AI/ML work or require support from another owner."}, "student_confusion": "Which issues are minor observations and which are blockers?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Risk & Escalation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You now sees that missing temperature values may hide thermal anomalies, rpm gaps may weaken pattern detection, duplicate timestamps may create false anomaly spikes, packet jumps may indicate dropped data, and unclear field metadata may lead to wrong features. You must classify which issues are minor, which are blockers, what the consequence is, and whether the issue belongs to AI/ML, software, embedded, test, or senior engineering escalation."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l1-m5", "title": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "tools": {"tools_used": "Closure report template, reviewer checklist", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-empower", "url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod5_01_Artifact.pptx", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "M5 Empower: Final Quality and Closure Report submission: professional readiness closure", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What decision can you defend using evidence: ready, partially ready, blocked, or escalate? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Make sure your decision is based on evidence and does not ask AI to decide for you."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-engage", "url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/explore/mod5_exp.png", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "M5 Engage: Closure kickoff: senior engineer needs a clear readiness decision", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What is the workplace risk if this part of the telemetry readiness review is skipped or rushed? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Name the risk in one sentence before opening the template."}], "content_type": "image", "duration_seconds": 600}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-evolve", "url": "#", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "M5 Evolve: Transfer reflection: communicating readiness decisions in other technical reviews", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: How would you transfer this validation logic to another dataset, sensor stream, or industry case? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Write one transfer rule you can reuse in a future AI/ML evidence-readiness review."}], "content_type": "reflection", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-explain", "url": "#", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "M5 Explain: Closure communication guide: clear, careful, evidence-backed readiness decisions", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What concept or role boundary helps you understand the issue without overclaiming root cause? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "State the concept in simple words and link it to the telemetry case."}], "content_type": "video", "duration_seconds": 600}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-explore", "url": "#", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "M5 Explore: Review checks passed, checks failed, open issues, and confidence level", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What evidence can you observe in the case, dataset summary, logs, UDP description, or shared-memory field list? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Point to at least one visible evidence item rather than using a general opinion."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l1-m5-express", "url": "#", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "M5 Express: Practice Quality and Closure Report using checks and decision options", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for Quality and Closure Report: What exactly will you write in your artifact, and which evidence will you cite? Focus on checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence, and readiness decision.", "follow_up": "Check whether your artifact separates facts, assumptions, role boundary, and next action."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your closure message is clear to a non-technical reviewer and whether it avoids overclaiming.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses the Risk and Escalation Note from Module 4 and creates the closure record that feeds the final portfolio in Module 6."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m5-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m5-f1", "order": 1, "title": "Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final decision clear: ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation, and is it supported by checks passed, checks failed, and open evidence issues?", "instructions": "Write the closure report showing work completed, evidence used, checks passed, checks failed, open issues, confidence level, closure message, and final readiness decision. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence, reasoning clarity, correct role boundary, escalation where needed, and complete fields.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l1-m5", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod5_02_Template.xlsx"