trail is visible. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence, reasoning clarity, correct role boundary, escalation where needed, and complete fields.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l1-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://storage-sp.rareminds.in/LTE/aiml/Mod6_02_Template_Lean.xlsx", "file_name": "Mod6_02_Template_Lean.xlsx", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l1-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l1-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: Final Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s final readiness decision back to earlier artifacts, evidence checks, risks, escalations, and closure communication?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, or missed-risk prompts.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Evidence chain, artifact continuity, portfolio packaging, transfer reflection", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Self-review, artifact sequencing, portfolio proof"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the Final Portfolio Pack by connecting all previous artifacts into one evidence trail that proves L1 anomaly-readiness validation capability.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may submit separate worksheets without showing a connected evidence trail.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, final validation", "reason_behind_concept": "Capability proof requires traceability from the final decision back to earlier evidence, reasoning, risks, and closure communication.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use at the end of the course when the learner must package artifact evidence for review and transfer to other data-readiness contexts."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that my decision came from evidence?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The reviewer must see that you did not complete seven disconnected tasks. You must assemble a complete evidence chain from readiness, intake, validation, action, risk, and closure into one portfolio. The portfolio must prove that you can responsibly inspect telemetry evidence and make an L1 anomaly-readiness decision before model work begins."}], "duration": "14 hours", "course_id": "crs-aiml-tel-l1", "xp_reward": 500, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "AI/ML engineers must verify telemetry evidence quality before attempting anomaly detection or model work.", "course_code": "AIML-TEL-L1", "description": "You validate whether telemetry evidence is ready for AI/ML anomaly detection, identifies visible readiness gaps, separates AI/ML responsibility from software/embedded dependencies, and prepares an evidence-based readiness or escalation note.", "domain_name": "Data & AI", "level_label": "L1", "sequence_no": 1, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "AI/ML engineers must check telemetry evidence quality, role ownership, and escalation needs before treating any dataset as model-ready.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515879218367-8466d910aaa4?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "AI/ML Telemetry Evidence Readiness", "difficulty_level": "beginner", "job_pathway_role": "AI / ML Engineer", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Course Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: What does the learner understand about why telemetry data must be validated before AI/ML use, and can they map the industry context, role boundary, evidence sources, and readiness decision without jumping to model-building? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Course Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: Industry system map, telemetry source map, stakeholder map, AI/ML-owned responsibilities, software/embedded dependencies, evidence required before model work, learner readiness gaps, readiness decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner separated observed facts from assumptions and clarified what an L1 AI/ML learner owns versus what must be escalated? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Case request, available inputs, missing information, knowns, unknowns, assumptions, role boundary, clarification questions, intake decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner checked missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, field meaning, and warning logs before judging anomaly-readiness? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Evidence item, source/owner, completeness check, timestamp check, missing-value check, packet continuity check, field meaning check, ML-readiness impact, validation decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Telemetry Readiness Action Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the learner’s recommendation supported by evidence from the checklist and clearly separated into action, handoff, escalation, or blocked-readiness decision? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Telemetry Readiness Action Note by filling these required fields: Evidence reviewed, missing-value count, timestamp issues, packet jumps, log warnings, anomaly-readiness impact, human-first reasoning, handoff message, final action decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner identified which issues require senior, telemetry, embedded, software, test, or data-owner support and explained the consequence of each blocker? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, risk category, observed evidence, consequence, severity, owner, escalation reason, next action. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Quality and Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the final decision clear: ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation, and is it supported by checks passed, checks failed, and open evidence issues? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Quality and Closure Report by filling these required fields: Work completed, evidence used, checks passed, checks failed, open issues, closure message, confidence level, closure decision. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l1-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "Final Portfolio Pack", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can a reviewer trace the learner’s final readiness decision back to earlier artifacts, evidence checks, risks, escalations, and closure communication? Input: use the telemetry case brief, 720-row sample summary, missing sensor_temp count of 18, missing rpm count of 11, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, warning logs, UDP packet description, shared-memory field list, and prior module artifacts where applicable. Action: complete the Final Portfolio Pack by filling these required fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: visible missing values, duplicate timestamps, timestamp gaps, packet jumps, warning logs, unclear field ownership, and AI/ML role-boundary reasoning. Output decision: state whether the evidence is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-readiness validation. Do not build a model, diagnose embedded-system root cause, or ask AI to produce the final answer.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Telemetry Evidence Readiness for AI/ML Anomaly Detection", "description": "A telemetry test team has completed a 12-minute aerospace electronics lab run and shared a small evidence pack for AI/ML review before anomaly detection begins. The pack contains 720 telemetry rows with timestamp, packet_id, sensor_temp, voltage, current, rpm, and status_code, plus a short application log, UDP packet description, and shared-memory field list. During the first check, the evidence shows 18 missing sensor_temp values, 11 missing rpm values, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, and log warnings such as delayed UDP packets and shared-memory read timeout. At L1, you do not build an anomaly-detection model or diagnose embedded-system root cause. You validate whether telemetry data is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-detection work, and prepares an evidence-based readiness or escalation note supported by the visible evidence."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready L1 evidence for AI/ML telemetry readiness review", "completion_percentage": 14, "common_course_problem_statement": "A telemetry test team has completed a 12-minute aerospace electronics lab run and shared a small evidence pack for AI/ML review before anomaly detection begins. The pack contains 720 telemetry rows with timestamp, packet_id, sensor_temp, voltage, current, rpm, and status_code, plus a short application log, UDP packet description, and shared-memory field list. During the first check, the evidence shows 18 missing sensor_temp values, 11 missing rpm values, 7 duplicate timestamps, 4 timestamp gaps above 2 seconds, 4 packet-id jumps, and log warnings such as delayed UDP packets and shared-memory read timeout. At L1, you do not build an anomaly-detection model or diagnose embedded-system root cause. You validate whether telemetry data is ready, partially ready, blocked, or needs escalation for next-step AI/ML anomaly-detection work, and prepares an evidence-based readiness or escalation note supported by the visible evidence."}, {"id": "lpc-aiml-tel-l2", "gap": 2, "badge": "Baseline Anomaly Workflow", "title": "Baseline Anomaly Detection Workflow for Telemetry Data", "status": "not_started", "modules": [{"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m0", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "tools": {"tools_used": "Course brief, model workflow map, readiness worksheet", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: can this case move from readiness review to controlled baseline workflow?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: What decision can you defend about moving from evidence-readiness to baseline workflow?", "follow_up": "Defend whether the workflow is for learning, further testing, evidence fixing, escalation, or blocked use."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Baseline workflow kickoff: why simple anomaly logic is not production AI", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: What is the workplace risk if a beginner presents a baseline anomaly experiment as a production model?", "follow_up": "Explain the risk as overclaiming a simple workflow as production AI, not as a coding problem."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: transfer baseline-versus-production caution to another AI/ML task", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: How would this baseline-versus-production boundary transfer to another AI/ML use case?", "follow_up": "Write one rule that stops L2 baseline work from becoming an unsupported production claim."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide: L2 boundary between baseline testing and production model claims", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: What concept helps you separate baseline workflow evidence from production model readiness?", "follow_up": "Define baseline workflow, production model, and limitation in simple telemetry words."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect L1-ready fields and remaining evidence limits before workflow planning", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: Which fields and limitations from the L1 review should control this L2 workflow?", "follow_up": "Point to the L1 readiness result, selected fields, excluded status_code, and remaining missing values."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m0-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Worksheet: document L2 purpose, usable fields, non-owned decisions, and readiness", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet: What will you write in the readiness sheet to show L2 purpose, boundary, tools, and risks?", "follow_up": "Include L2 purpose, boundary, usable fields, non-owned decisions, and readiness decision."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to explain the difference between a baseline anomaly workflow and a production model, then write the boundary in your own words.", "module_continuity_link": "Creates the Model Workflow Readiness Sheet that becomes the context input for baseline case intake."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m0-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m0-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet", "description": "Can you explain the purpose and boundary of an L2 baseline anomaly workflow without claiming production-readiness?", "instructions": "Complete the readiness artifact by documenting L2 purpose, modelling boundary, usable field summary, non-owned decisions, baseline versus production distinction, tool awareness, risk awareness, and readiness decision. Submit the final artifact for review with evidence used, reasoning clarity, correct L2 role boundary, escalation where needed, reproducibility, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l2-m0", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l2/ART_L2_M0_Model_Workflow_Readiness_Template", "file_name": "ART_L2_M0_Model_Workflow_Readiness_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m0-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m0-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m0-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m0-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet", "description": "Can you explain the purpose and boundary of an L2 baseline anomaly workflow without claiming production-readiness?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Baseline workflow purpose, model boundary, usable field awareness, production-readiness limitation", "academic_refresher_concepts": "AI/ML workflow stages, baseline experiment, model limitation language"}, "module_no": 0, "description": "Build the L2 Model Workflow Readiness Sheet by completing the L2 telemetry baseline workflow task: The learner is now moving from evidence-readiness to baseline anomaly workflow. The risk is that a beginner may overclaim a simple experiment as a production model. The learner must understand what L2 allows: selecting usable fields, handling remaining missing values, preparing simple anomaly logic, reviewing outputs, and documenting assumptions while clearly stating that the workflow is only baseline evidence.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may treat a baseline experiment as a production anomaly-detection model instead of a controlled learning workflow.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "L2 AI/ML workflow boundary, baseline versus production distinction, field-selection readiness, limitation awareness", "reason_behind_concept": "A beginner baseline is useful only when its purpose, assumptions, allowed decisions, and limitations are clear before work begins.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use at the start of an L2 telemetry workflow before selecting fields, handling missing values, or testing anomaly logic."}, "student_confusion": "Does building a baseline workflow mean I have built a real model?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Workflow Readiness Orientation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You are now moving from evidence-readiness to baseline anomaly workflow. The risk is that a beginner may overclaim a simple experiment as a production model. You must understand what L2 allows: selecting usable fields, handling remaining missing values, preparing simple anomaly logic, reviewing outputs, and documenting assumptions while clearly stating that the workflow is only baseline evidence."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m1", "title": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "tools": {"tools_used": "Case intake template, selected-field list, telemetry field description", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: is the baseline case intake clear enough to validate evidence?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: Is the case intake clear enough to move into evidence validation, or does it need escalation first?", "follow_up": "Make an intake decision before testing logic; do not jump directly to anomaly flags."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Case intake kickoff: unpack the senior engineer request for baseline anomaly workflow", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: What could go wrong if you begin testing anomaly logic before clarifying the senior engineer request?", "follow_up": "State why a broad baseline request can create wrong field choices or wrong ownership."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: reuse intake logic for another unlabelled telemetry workflow", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: How would you reuse this intake approach for another broad AI/ML request?", "follow_up": "Name one intake question you would reuse before any future baseline workflow."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Role boundary guide: what L2 AI/ML you can decide versus escalate", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Baseline Model Case Intake Note: What role-boundary concept helps you know what L2 AI/ML can decide and what must be escalated?", "follow_up": "Separate what AI/ML can document from what senior, software, embedded, or data owners must confirm."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m1-explor