ethod choice, or why the baseline is not production-ready.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Missing-data handling options, allowed baseline methods, suspicious-output review, reproducibility, L2 limitation language", "reason_behind_concept": "A workflow note must be reproducible and explainable so another engineer can understand what was tested and why the output is only baseline evidence.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use after validation when the learner can safely design a small baseline workflow using only allowed fields and clearly stated assumptions."}, "student_confusion": "Which simple method can I use, and how should I safely handle the remaining missing values?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Baseline Workflow Action", "module_specific_problem_statement": "You must prepare a baseline anomaly workflow using the selected telemetry fields. They must document field selection, handle remaining missing values by stating whether values are dropped, marked, excluded from baseline logic, or handled through a simple documented rule, apply or design an allowed simple baseline method (fixed threshold, range check, z-score-style outlier flag, mean/standard-deviation rule, or manually documented suspicious-row rule), identify suspicious rows, explain why outputs are suspicious and not confirmed anomalies, and prepare a workflow note another engineer can reproduce. They must not use advanced ML models, clustering, neural networks, or production scoring pipelines at L2."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m4", "title": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "tools": {"tools_used": "Risk log, false-positive review table, escalation matrix", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": 