n needs?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "False positives, label gaps, threshold sensitivity, offline-versus-real-time limitations, escalation criteria", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Risk categories, severity, cause versus evidence, escalation message basics"}, "module_no": 4, "description": "Build the L2 Model Risk and Escalation Note by reviewing suspicious outputs without treating them as confirmed anomalies. The learner must classify whether flags may be caused by remaining missing values, weak feature meaning, no labelled anomaly data, threshold sensitivity, or mismatch between offline testing and future real-time inference, then decide whether the issue needs more testing, evidence fixing, escalation, or blocking from model use.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may present suspicious outputs as true anomalies instead of reviewing false-positive causes and escalation ownership.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Suspicious output versus confirmed anomaly, false-positive risk, threshold sensitivity, label gap, escalation ownership", "reason_behind_concept": "Risk review prevents a weak baseline from being treated as a reliable anomaly detector or integrated without confirmation.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use after suspicious outputs appear and the learner must classify risks before communicating baseline usefulness."}, "student_confusion": "How do I decide whether a suspicious flag is a real anomaly, a data issue, or an escalation item?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Model Risk & Escalation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The baseline workflow produces suspicious outputs, but suspicious output does not mean confirmed anomaly. Some flags may be caused by remaining missing values, weak feature meaning, no labelled anomaly data, threshold sensitivity, or mismatch between offline testing and future real-time inference. You must classify false-positive risks, model/workflow limitations, data gaps, and integration concerns, then decide what must be escalated and to whom."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m5", "title": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "tools": {"tools_used": "Closure report template, limitation checklist, senior-review message draft", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: suitable for learning, further testing, evidence fixes, or blocked?", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: Can you defend the closure decision: learning only, further testing, needs evidence fixes, or blocked for model use?", "follow_up": "Make the closure decision clear: learning only, further testing, evidence fixes, escalation, or blocked for model use."}], "content_type": "decision check", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Closure kickoff: communicate baseline usefulness without production-readiness claims", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: What is the workplace risk if the closure report overclaims the baseline workflow result?", "follow_up": "Frame the closure risk as overclaiming baseline results to a senior engineer."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: reuse closure language for another baseline AI/ML review", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: How would you reuse this closure style for another AI/ML baseline review?", "follow_up": "State one communication habit you will reuse when reporting uncertain AI/ML outputs."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Communication guide: model quality observation versus model success claim", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: What communication concept helps you separate model quality observation from model success claim?", "follow_up": "Explain why limitation language is part of quality, not a weakness in the report."}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Gather fields used, suspicious outputs, assumptions, limitations, and open issues", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: What evidence should be included: fields used, logic tested, suspicious outputs, assumptions, risks, and open issues?", "follow_up": "Use work completed, fields used, assumptions, limitations, reproducibility note, and open issues."}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l2/content/c-aiml-tel-l2-m5-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Closure report task: write evidence-based stakeholder message and decision", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L2 Model Quality and Closure Report: How will you write the closure message so it is clear to a senior reviewer?", "follow_up": "Write the message as if a senior engineer will review it before deciding next steps."}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 900}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether your closure message is clear to a senior engineer and includes assumptions, limitations, and next-step decision.", "module_continuity_link": "Turns M4 risk classification into a senior-review communication and closure decision."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l2-m5-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l2-m5-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L2 Model Quality and Closure Report", "description": "Is the final baseline workflow decision clear, professionally communicated, and supported by evidence, assumptions, limitations, reproducibility notes, and open issues?", "instructions": "Write the closure report showing work completed, evidence used, model quality observation, reproducibility note, assumptions and limitations, open issues, stakeholder message, closure confidence, and closure decision. Submit the final 