ed baseline workflow result with clear limitation language. The learner must state what was tested, which fields were used, how missing values were handled, what suspicious outputs appeared, what assumptions and risks remain, whether outputs are only suspicious and not confirmed anomalies, and whether the workflow supports learning, further testing, evidence fixes, escalation, or is blocked for model use.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may give a vague success message without limitations, reproducibility notes, or a clear readiness decision.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Closure decision, limitation language, reproducibility note, stakeholder communication, next-step readiness", "reason_behind_concept": "Closure communication protects the team from overusing a baseline result and shows exactly what further evidence or testing is needed.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use after risk review when the learner must give a clear and role-safe closure decision to a senior reviewer."}, "student_confusion": "How do I communicate a useful baseline result without making it sound production-ready?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Model Closure Communication", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer asks whether the baseline anomaly workflow can support next-step planning. You must communicate what was tested, which fields were used, what suspicious outputs appeared, how missing values were handled, what assumptions were made, what risks remain, and whether the workflow is suitable for learning, further testing, or blocked for model use. The closure must explicitly avoid production-readiness claims and must include limitation language."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l2-m6", "title": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "Portfolio pack template, artifact-chain map, final self-review checklist", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages":