arification questions, intake decision"}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to help list integration clarification questions about output fields, latency, owners, and interface contract without asking it to decide readiness.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses Module 0 readiness context and produces an intake note for integration evidence validation."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l3-m1-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l3-m1-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L3 Integration Case Intake Note", "description": "Has you clarified AI/ML, software, embedded/test, and senior-engineer responsibilities before integration planning?", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering: Has you clarified AI/ML, software, embedded/test, and senior-engineer responsibilities before integration planning? Fill the required workbook fields: Integration request, available evidence, expected application use, unknown interface fields, role boundary, assumptions, clarification questions, intake decision. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L3 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l3-m1", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l3/ART_L3_M1_Integration_Case_Intake_Template", "file_name": "ART_L3_M1_Integration_Case_Intake_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l3-m1-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l3-m1-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l3-m1-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l3-m1-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L3 Integration Case Intake Note", "description": "Has you clarified AI/ML, software, embedded/test, and senior-engineer responsibilities before integration planning?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Integration objective framing, stakeholder ownership, interface unknowns, assumption logging", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Case intake, stakeholder mapping, responsibility boundary"}, "module_no": 1, "description": "Build the L3 Integration Case Intake Note by completing the L3 telemetry AI/ML task: The senior engineer asks, “Can this baseline anomaly output be prepared for C++/Qt integration planning?” The learner has a baseline workflow summary, sample anomaly output, application display requirement, and latency expectation, but not the final interface contract. The learner must clarify what AI/ML must provide, what software must confirm, what embedded/test teams must validate, and what assumptions are unsafe.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may prepare a handoff without clarifying the interface contract, ownership, latency proof, or unsafe assumptions.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Integration request, role boundary, expected application use, unknown interface fields, unsafe assumptions", "reason_behind_concept": "Clear intake prevents AI/ML from promising real-time performance or display behavior that has not been confirmed.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use when the integration request is broad and the learner must define safe AI/ML handoff responsibility."}, "student_confusion": "What does AI/ML own in integration planning, and what must software or embedded teams confirm?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Integration Case Intake", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The senior engineer asks, “Can this baseline anomaly output be prepared for C++/Qt integration planning?” You have a baseline workflow summary, sample anomaly output, application display requirement, and latency expectation, but not the final interface contract. You must clarify what AI/ML must provide, what software must confirm, what embedded/test teams must validate, and what assumptions are unsafe."}, {"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l3-m2", "title": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "tools": {"tools_used": "Evidence checklist, sample anomaly output, C++/Qt display requirement note", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l3-m2-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l3/content/c-aiml-tel-l3-m2-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: defend the model-input evidence validation checklist decision with evidence", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Model-Input Evidence Validation Checklist: What decision can you defend using evidence from this module?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence; state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface chang