re, and transfer note for L4 automation/reporting"}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l3-m6-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l3/content/c-aiml-tel-l3-m6-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L3 Integration Portfolio Pack", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L3 Integration Portfolio Pack: What exactly will you write in the artifact so it is useful to a reviewer?", "follow_up": "Include the required fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, output schema summary, integration risk summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation"}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to check whether every portfolio claim links to an artifact and whether the transfer note supports L4 automation/reporting readiness.", "module_continuity_link": "Uses all previous artifacts to produce the L3 portfolio and transfer note for L4 automation and reporting work."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l3-m6-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l3-m6-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L3 Integration Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s integration-readiness decision through intake, validation, schema mapping, risk handling, closure, and transfer to L4?", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering: Can a reviewer trace you’s integration-readiness decision through intake, validation, schema mapping, risk handling, closure, and transfer to L4? Fill the required workbook fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, output schema summary, integration risk summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L3 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l3-m6", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l3/ART_L3_M6_Integration_Portfolio_Template", "file_name": "ART_L3_M6_Integration_Portfolio_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l3-m6-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l3-m6-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l3-m6-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l3-m6-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L3 Integration Portfolio Pack", "description": "Can a reviewer trace you’s integration-readiness decision through intake, validation, schema mapping, risk handling, closure, and transfer to L4?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Evidence mapping, artifact chain, output schema summary, integration risk summary, transfer note", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Portfolio structure, proof of capability, transfer learning"}, "module_no": 6, "description": "Build the L3 Integration Portfolio Pack by completing the L3 telemetry AI/ML task: The reviewer needs proof that the learner can translate AI/ML output into integration-ready evidence. The learner must compile the complete L3 artifact chain showing integration intake, evidence validation, output schema mapping, risk handling, closure decision, and transfer notes for L4 automation and reporting work.", "estimatedTime": "3 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may submit separate integration worksheets without proving a connected handoff and readiness decision trail.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Portfolio evidence, artifact continuity, output schema summary, integration risk summary, transfer readiness", "reason_behind_concept": "A portfolio proves L3 capability when the reviewer can trace intake, evidence, schema, risk, and closure into one decision.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use at the end of L3 to assemble a connected integration-readiness evidence trail."}, "student_confusion": "How do I prove that integration-readiness came from evidence and is ready to transfer to L4?", "artifact_submitted": false, "completion_percentage": 0, "engineering_workflow_stage": "Portfolio Validation", "module_specific_problem_statement": "The reviewer needs proof that you can translate AI/ML output into integration-ready evidence. You must compile the complete L3 artifact chain showing integration intake, evidence validation, output schema mapping, risk handling, closure decision, and transfer notes for L4 automation and reporting work."}], "duration": "18 hours", "course_id": "crs-aiml-tel-l3", "xp_reward": 900, "started_at": null, "why_needed": "AI/ML engineers need to translate offline anomaly outputs into integration-ready evidence before software teams can plan C++/Qt display or real-time usage.", "course_code": "AIML-TEL-L3", "description": "You can prepare a model integration-readiness plan by checking latency, input/output mapping, C++/Qt handoff expectations, real-time/offline differences, model output usability, and integration risks.", "domain_name": "Data & AI", "level_label": "L3", "sequence_no": 3, "completed_at": null, "how_to_build": "AI/ML engineers must compare offline workflow outputs with application expectations, map inputs and outputs, document latency and explainability gaps, and prepare a controlled handoff without claiming deployment-readiness.", "current_level": 1, "priority_band": "A", "thumbnail_url": "https://images.unsplash.com/photo-1515879218367-8466d910aaa4?q=80&w=2670&auto=format&fit=crop", "required_level": 3, "capability_name": "AI/ML Real-Time Integration Readiness", "difficulty_level": "intermediate", "job_pathway_role": "AI / ML Engineer", "problem_artifacts": [{"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l3-m0", "no": 1, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Integration Readiness Sheet", "module": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can the learner explain the difference between offline baseline output and integration-ready evidence for C++/Qt planning? Input: use the L3 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: baseline workflow summary, 690 usable rows, selected fields, offline-versus-real-time boundary, C++/Qt context, latency expectation, explainability need. Action: complete the L3 Integration Readiness Sheet by filling these required fields: L3 purpose, offline vs real-time difference, C++/Qt integration context, expected input fields, expected output fields, latency expectation, explainability need, readiness decision. Evidence to cite: baseline workflow summary, 690 usable rows, selected fields, offline-versus-real-time boundary, C++/Qt context, latency expectation, explainability need. Output decision: state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, needs escalation, or is blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved. Do not claim deployment-readiness, real-time performance, embedded root cause, or final software behavior without confirmed interface and latency evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l3-m1", "no": 2, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Integration Case Intake Note", "module": "Case Intake & Role Boundary", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner clarified AI/ML, software, embedded/test, and senior-engineer responsibilities before integration planning? Input: use the L3 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: senior engineer request, baseline workflow summary, sample anomaly output, C++/Qt screen requirement, latency expectation, missing interface contract, role boundary. Action: complete the L3 Integration Case Intake Note by filling these required fields: Integration request, available evidence, expected application use, unknown interface fields, role boundary, assumptions, clarification questions, intake decision. Evidence to cite: senior engineer request, baseline workflow summary, sample anomaly output, C++/Qt screen requirement, latency expectation, missing interface contract, role boundary. Output decision: state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, needs escalation, or is blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved. Do not claim deployment-readiness, real-time performance, embedded root cause, or final software behavior without confirmed interface and latency evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l3-m2", "no": 3, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Model-Input Evidence Validation Checklist", "module": "Evidence / Requirement Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner checked output completeness, feature explanation availability, latency evidence, application display match, and missing interface fields? Input: use the L3 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: 26 flagged records, 9 records without feature-level explanation, current output fields timestamp/score/flag, expected fields timestamp/anomaly_score/severity/source_signal/explanation/recommended_action, latency evidence. Action: complete the L3 Model-Input Evidence Validation Checklist by filling these required fields: Evidence item, source/owner, output completeness, feature explanation availability, latency evidence, application display match, missing interface fields, integration-readiness decision. Evidence to cite: 26 flagged records, 9 records without feature-level explanation, current output fields timestamp/score/flag, expected fields timestamp/anomaly_score/severity/source_signal/explanation/recommended_action, latency evidence. Output decision: state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, needs escalation, or is blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved. Do not claim deployment-readiness, real-time performance, embedded root cause, or final software behavior without confirmed interface and latency evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l3-m3", "no": 4, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 AI Output Handoff Note", "module": "Guided Work Action or Handoff", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the learner’s AI output handoff understandable, schema-based, explainable, and clear about latency and missing output fields? Input: use the L3 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: selected telemetry inputs, current anomaly output fields, proposed output schema, explanation gaps, severity mapping, latency concerns, software handoff needs. Action: complete the L3 AI Output Handoff Note by filling these required fields: Selected input fields, current output fields, proposed output schema, anomaly explanation, severity mapping, latency note, software handoff message, final action decision. Evidence to cite: selected telemetry inputs, current anomaly output fields, proposed output schema, explanation gaps, severity mapping, latency concerns, software handoff needs. Output decision: state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, needs escalation, or is blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved. Do not claim deployment-readiness, real-time performance, embedded root cause, or final software behavior without confirmed interface and latency evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l3-m4", "no": 5, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Integration Risk and Escalation Note", "module": "Exceptions, Blockers, Risks & Escalations", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Has the learner classified integration blockers, latency risks, explainability gaps, missing interface fields, owners, and escalation needs? Input: use the L3 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: offline test limitation, 500 ms latency expectation, missing source-signal explanation, missing severity labels, missing interface fields, owner and escalation evidence. Action: complete the L3 Integration Risk and Escalation Note by filling these required fields: Risk ID, risk category, observed evidence, integration impact, severity, owner, escalation reason, recommended next action. Evidence to cite: offline test limitation, 500 ms latency expectation, missing source-signal explanation, missing severity labels, missing interface fields, owner and escalation evidence. Output decision: state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, needs escalation, or is blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved. Do not claim deployment-readiness, real-time performance, embedded root cause, or final software behavior without confirmed interface and latency evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l3-m5", "no": 6, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Integration Quality and Closure Report", "module": "Quality, Communication & Closure", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Is the integration-readiness decision clear: proceed for planning, revise interface, or block until latency/explainability/output-format gaps are resolved? Input: use the L3 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: work completed, output readiness, interface gaps, latency assumptions, open issues, evidence links, closure confidence and decision. Action: complete the L3 Integration Quality and Closure Report by filling these required fields: Work completed, evidence used, output readiness, interface gaps, latency assumptions, open issues, stakeholder message, closure confidence, closure decision. Evidence to cite: work completed, output readiness, interface gaps, latency assumptions, open issues, evidence links, closure confidence and decision. Output decision: state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, needs escalation, or is blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved. Do not claim deployment-readiness, real-time performance, embedded root cause, or final software behavior without confirmed interface and latency evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}, {"id": "pa-aiml-tel-l3-m6", "no": 7, "text": "", "score": 0, "title": "L3 Integration Portfolio Pack", "module": "Portfolio, Transfer & Final Validation", "prompt": "Final artifact question: Can a reviewer trace the learner’s integration-readiness decision through intake, validation, schema mapping, risk handling, closure, and transfer to L4? Input: use the L3 course case, prior module artifacts where applicable, and this evidence: full artifact chain from readiness, intake, validation, handoff, risk, closure, and transfer note for L4 automation/reporting. Action: complete the L3 Integration Portfolio Pack by filling these required fields: Portfolio cover note, artifact chain, evidence map, output schema summary, integration risk summary, retry log, capability proof, transfer note, reviewer validation. Evidence to cite: full artifact chain from readiness, intake, validation, handoff, risk, closure, and transfer note for L4 automation/reporting. Output decision: state whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, needs escalation, or is blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved. Do not claim deployment-readiness, real-time performance, embedded root cause, or final software behavior without confirmed interface and latency evidence. Do not ask AI to produce the final answer; use AI only as a coach for guided questions and clarity checks.", "status": "not_started"}], "problem_statement": {"title": "Real-Time AI/ML Integration Readiness for Telemetry Systems", "description": "After the L2 baseline anomaly workflow, the senior engineer wants to understand whether the baseline logic can be prepared for future integration into a C++/Qt telemetry application. You receive a baseline workflow summary, 690 usable telemetry rows, selected input fields, a sample anomaly output file with 26 flagged records, a C++/Qt screen requirement note, and a latency expectation that anomaly status should be available within 500 milliseconds for near-real-time display. However, the baseline workflow was tested offline, the anomaly output format is not yet aligned with the application team’s expected display fields, and some flagged records do not clearly explain which telemetry feature caused the anomaly. You must decide whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, or blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved."}, "certification_value": "Portfolio-ready L3 evidence for C++/Qt integration-readiness planning and handoff communication", "completion_percentage": 0, "common_course_problem_statement": "After the L2 baseline anomaly workflow, the senior engineer wants to understand whether the baseline logic can be prepared for future integration into a C++/Qt telemetry application. You receive a baseline workflow summary, 690 usable telemetry rows, selected input fields, a sample anomaly output file with 26 flagged records, a C++/Qt screen requirement note, and a latency expectation that anomaly status should be available within 500 milliseconds for near-real-time display. However, the baseline workflow was tested offline, the anomaly output format is not yet aligned with the application team’s expected display fields, and some flagged records do not clearly explain which telemetry feature caused the anomaly. You must decide whether the AI/ML output is ready for integration planning, partially ready with interface changes, or blocked until latency, explainability, and output-format gaps are resolved."}, {"id": "lpc-aiml-tel-l4", "gap": 2, "badge": "Automation Reporting Control", "title": "Predictive Analytics, LLM Reporting, and AI Workflow Control for Telemetry Systems", "status": "not_started", "modules": [{"id": "mod-aiml-tel-l4-m0", "title": "Industry, Role & Course Readiness", "tools": {"tools_used": "Course brief, automation-readiness worksheet, anomaly/reporting context", "tool_type_free_or_paid": "free"}, "stages": [{"key": "engage", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explore", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "explain", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "express", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "empower", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}, {"key": "evolve", "status": "not_started", "time_spent_seconds": 0}], "status": "available", "content": [{"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-empower", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-empower", "order": 5, "stage": "empower", "title": "Decision check: defend the automation readiness sheet decision with evidence", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Readiness Sheet: What decision can you defend using evidence from this module?", "follow_up": "Make the decision yourself using evidence; state whether the predictive insight and LLM reporting workflow is usable, partially usable with human review controls, needs more evidence, or is blocked until reporting boundaries are corrected."}], "content_type": "checklist", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-engage", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-engage", "order": 1, "stage": "engage", "title": "Automation Readiness Sheet kickoff: workplace risk and decision boundary", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Readiness Sheet: What is the workplace risk in this module before any solution or recommendation is suggested?", "follow_up": "Name the risk using this module context: Learner may overtrust anomaly flags or LLM text and present interpretation as confirmed engineering evidence."}], "content_type": "case brief", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-evolve", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-evolve", "order": 6, "stage": "evolve", "title": "Reflection: transfer automation readiness sheet reasoning to the next AI/ML workflow", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Readiness Sheet: How can this learning transfer to the next dataset, team handoff, or level?", "follow_up": "State one reusable rule for transferring this artifact to L5 solution validation."}], "content_type": "reflection prompt", "duration_seconds": 1200}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-explain", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-explain", "order": 3, "stage": "explain", "title": "Guide: concepts and role boundary for automation readiness sheet", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Readiness Sheet: Which concept or boundary helps you understand this issue?", "follow_up": "Explain in simple words using these concepts: Anomaly-to-insight boundary, evidence versus interpretation, LLM reporting boundary, human review need, automation risk awareness"}], "content_type": "explainer", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-explore", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-explore", "order": 2, "stage": "explore", "title": "Inspect evidence for automation readiness sheet", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Readiness Sheet: What visible evidence should you inspect before completing this artifact?", "follow_up": "Point to module-specific evidence: 690 cleaned rows, 26 anomaly flags, trend summary, draft LLM incident summary, evidence-versus-interpretation boundary, human review need"}], "content_type": "practice activity", "duration_seconds": 900}, {"id": "c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-express", "url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/courses/aiml-tel-l4/content/c-aiml-tel-l4-m0-express", "order": 4, "stage": "express", "title": "Template task: complete the L4 Automation Readiness Sheet", "status": "published", "isViewed": false, "facilitator": [{"question": "AI coach for L4 Automation Readiness Sheet: What exactly will you write in the artifact so it is useful to a reviewer?", "follow_up": "Include the required fields: L4 purpose, anomaly-to-insight boundary, LLM reporting boundary, evidence vs interpretation rule, human review need, automation risk awareness, readiness decision"}], "content_type": "worksheet", "duration_seconds": 1200}], "support": {"ai_support_tips": "Ask AI to explain evidence versus interpretation in simple terms, then write the reporting boundary yourself.", "module_continuity_link": "Creates the Automation Readiness Sheet that becomes the context input for predictive analytics intake."}, "artifacts": {"empower": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l4-m0-f", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l4-m0-f1", "order": 1, "title": "L4 Automation Readiness Sheet", "description": "Can you explain the boundary between evidence, prediction, LLM interpretation, and decision support?", "instructions": "Complete the final artifact by answering: Can you explain the boundary between evidence, prediction, LLM interpretation, and decision support? Fill the required workbook fields: L4 purpose, anomaly-to-insight boundary, LLM reporting boundary, evidence vs interpretation rule, human review need, automation risk awareness, readiness decision. Submit with visible evidence, reasoning clarity, correct L4 role boundary, escalation where needed, limitation language, and artifact completeness.", "accepted_file_types": [".xlsx", ".docx", ".pdf", ".zip"], "submission_required": true, "expected_submission_type": "file"}], "templates": [{"id": "at-aiml-tel-l4-m0", "version": 1, "file_url": "https://content.rareminds.dev/templates/aiml-tel-l4/ART_L4_M0_Automation_Readiness_Template", "file_name": "ART_L4_M0_Automation_Readiness_Template", "file_type": "xlsx", "artifact_id": "ma-aiml-tel-l4-m0-f", "question_id": "aq-aiml-tel-l4-m0-f1", "is_downloadable": true}], "submissions": [], "total_score": 100, "max_attempts": 3, "artifact_type": "final", "passing_score": 70, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": true}, "express": {"id": "ma-aiml-tel-l4-m0-p", "questions": [{"id": "aq-aiml-tel-l4-m0-p1", "order": 1, "title": "Practice Draft: L4 Automation Readiness Sheet", "description": "Can you explain the boundary between evidence, prediction, LLM interpretation, and decision support?", "instructions": "Draft a first pass using the relevant template fields. Think through the evidence manually first and use AI only as a coach for guided questions, clarity checks, missed-risk prompts, or limitation checks.", "submission_required": false, "expected_submission_type": "text"}], "templates": [], "submissions": [], "total_score": 0, "max_attempts": null, "artifact_type": "practice", "passing_score": null, "allow_resubmission": true, "require_review_unlock": false}}, "knowledge": {"technical_concepts_learnt": "Predictive insight boundary, LLM summary risk, human review control, decision-support language", "academic_refresher_concepts": "Prediction versus observation, LLM faithfulness, report control"}, "module_no": 0, "description": "Build the L4 Automation Readiness Sheet by completing the L4 telemetry AI/ML task: The learner is moving from integration-readiness to predictive analytics and report automation. The risk is that anomaly flags and LLM summaries may be treated as confirmed engineering conclusions. The learner must understand the boundary between evidence, prediction, interpretation, and decision support before using automation in a mission-critical telemetry context.", "estimatedTime": "2 hrs", "pressure_points": "Learner may overtrust anomaly flags or LLM text and present interpretation as confirmed engineering evidence.", "learning_content": {"major_concepts": "Anomaly-to-insight boundary, evidence versus interpretation, LLM reporting boundary, human review need, automation risk awareness", "reason_behind_concept": "Responsible automation requires separating observed evidence from generated interpretation and decision support.", "implementation_context_when_to_use": "Use before predictive or reporting work so the l